{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi4bcnqf1mm9hJ92tSPp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016Q3PfZHedr3GKwC7vxaf2X","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-074118__x0e4b02/work/PLAN.md","limit":300},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3249,"cache_read_input_tokens":19394,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3249},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b1b95e-beb5-4384-ba72-665ccf7128b3","uuid":"f633db6e-9f3d-4922-adc3-8e4b91615c9e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:41:27.588Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi4bcYD25SRFRJoWS67U","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016Q3PfZHedr3GKwC7vxaf2X":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-074118__x0e4b02/work/PLAN.md","limit":300}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016Q3PfZHedr3GKwC7vxaf2X","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Olympiyikes!\n2\t\n3\t**Tagline:** *Faster. Higher. Yikes.*\n4\t**One line:** the complete Summer *and* Winter Games, held in the same fortnight in one twin-city host, played as\n5\tan over-the-top arcade multi-event: 12 events, 8 nations, ceremonies, a rival, two hyperventilating commentators,\n6\t1–4 players on the couch and AI Hub ghost heats online.\n7\t\n8\t> **How the title was picked (TASK.md rule):** 50 riffs on \"Olympic Games\" were brainstormed silently, then\n9\t> `secrets.randbelow(50)` (Python, OS CSPRNG) returned **16 → \"Olympiyikes!\"**. Do not re-roll it. Its file-name\n10\t> form is `Olympiyikes`; the SOURCE token is `OlympicGames`.\n11\t\n12\t---\n13\t\n14\t## 0. Read this first (ground rules for the builders)\n15\t\n16\t- **Inputs:** `TASK.md` (requirements) + this plan. If they disagree, TASK.md wins. Where this plan is silent, follow\n17\t  the engine's own docs (`API.md`, `AI_GUIDE.md`) and the plan's spirit. Everything listed here ships: **no TODOs,\n18\t  placeholders, locked \"coming soon\" slots or stubbed features.**\n19\t- **Names (with this TASK.md):** dev folder `Olympiyikes-OlympicGames-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174837/`, deliverable\n20\t  `Olympiyikes-OlympicGames-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174837.html` in the root (beside TASK.md), and\n21\t  `exit-interview.json` in the root. If your TASK.md's name pattern carries a different model/date, use your pattern\n22\t  with `Olympiyikes` and `OlympicGames`.\n23\t- **Shared machine:** read only the files you need (other agents share the parent directories, ports and processes).\n24\t  Prefer `file://` and the engine's headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), run\n25\t  `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` from your dev folder, read the port it prints, and confirm the served page\n26\t  is *your* game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by PID. Never `pkill`, `killall`,\n27\t  `fuser -k`. During planning `/tmp` was 100% full: if npm/Playwright fail with ENOSPC, set `TMPDIR=<dev>/.tmp`.\n28\t- **Engine:** my-3D2dge handoff package, **v0.85.2** at planning time\n29\t  (`https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/tree/main/dist/handoff`). We own our copy and may change it (§4.6).\n30\t- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client **1.4.0** (`https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub`).\n31\t- **No subagents/workflows to debate, review, judge or audit** (TASK.md). Tests are scripts.\n32\t- **Units used in this plan:** world units (u) are the engine's (one tile = 16 u, z is up). Distances shown to the\n33\t  player are meters; each event says its scale (default **M = 12 u per meter**). Times in seconds unless marked ms.\n34\t  The engine runs fixed steps of 1/120 s.\n35\t\n36\t### 0.1 Fetch what you build on (once, inside the dev folder)\n37\t\n38\t```sh\n39\tD=Olympiyikes-OlympicGames-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174837 && mkdir -p $D/{engine,src,tests,tools,vendor/hub,.tmp} && cd $D\n40\tgit clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git vendor/my-3d2dge\n41\tgit -C vendor/my-3d2dge sparse-checkout set dist/handoff\n42\tcp vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js engine/my-3d2dge.js          # our engine copy (we edit this one)\n43\tfor f in session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js README.md; do\n44\t  curl -fsSL -o vendor/hub/$f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f; done\n45\t(cd vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff && export TMPDIR=\"$(cd ../../../.. && pwd)/.tmp\" && npm install && npx playwright install chromium)\n46\t```\n47\t\n48\tRead whole: `vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/API.md`, `README.md`, `kits/README.md`, `docs/ASSETS.md`,\n49\t`vendor/hub/README.md`. Read as references (copy patterns, not whole files): `kits/sports.js` (hockey), `kits/road.js`\n50\t(downhill/bobsled), `kits/rhythm.js` (figure skating), `kits/pinball.js` + `modules/physics.js` (curling),\n51\t`kits/kart.js` (drawing a rig through a custom view), `modules/arcade.js` (record tables, initials), `game/test.mjs`\n52\tand `kits/test.mjs` (headless harness). Grep `API-INDEX.md` for names; don't read it whole.\n53\t\n54\t---\n55\t\n56\t## 1. The game\n57\t\n58\t### 1.1 Pitch\n59\t\n60\tFor the first time in history the Summer and Winter Games share one fortnight and one host: **Mount Glory–Sunny Bay**,\n61\twhere a ski jump towers over the beach and the swimming pool shares a wall with the ice rink. Eight fictional nations\n62\tsend their stars. You pick a nation and its athlete, light the cauldron, and chase gold across **12 events** that\n63\talternate summer and winter, while defending champion **Max Overdrive of Turbonia** insists, loudly, that it is all\n64\tpointless because he will win. Everything is broadcast like the real thing (parade of nations, \"Up Close & Personal\"\n65\tprofiles, photo finishes, medal ceremonies with anthems, a medal table) and played like an arcade cabinet (mashing,\n66\ttiming, aiming, steering, rhythm, physics; a HYPE meter that sets you on fire; world records that explode into\n67\tfireworks). When it goes wrong, it goes *gloriously* wrong: false starts, belly flops, ski-jump tumbles, bobsleds on\n68\ttheir roof. That's an **OLYMPIYIKES!**, and the game celebrates it.\n69\t\n70\t### 1.2 Pillars\n71\t\n72\t1. **Ten seconds to learn, a lifetime to perfect.** Each event teaches one verb (mash, time, aim, steer, keep the beat,\n73\t   sweep) on one card, and has a perfect-play ceiling with world records to chase.\n74\t2. **Broadcast spectacle.** Ceremonies, commentators, crowd, jumbotron, slow-mo, photo finishes, anthems, records.\n75\t3. **Failure is a show.** Every event has at least one comic \"Yikes\" moment that is funny, fast to recover from, and\n76\t   even pays a little hype (§5.8).\n77\t4. **Both seasons.** 6 summer + 6 winter events on alternating days; each venue has its own look, light and music.\n78\t5. **Couch first, online too.** 1–4 local players in every mode; AI Hub ghost heats when the hub launches the game.\n79\t\n80\t### 1.3 Genre and perspective (decisions)\n81\t\n82\t- **Genre:** arcade multi-event sports (Track & Field / Winter Games lineage) with a short campaign, local party\n83\t  play and online ghost heats. Each event is a compact mini-game built on one shared event framework.\n84\t- **Perspective:** per event, all on the engine's native 2D views (pixel art at `res: 'ps1'`, `expand: true`):\n85\t  - **2.5D side-on lanes** (`'brawler'` view, pitch 25): 100m Dash, Javelin, 50m Freestyle, Weightlifting.\n86\t  - **Pure side view** (`'side'`): 10m Diving, Ski Jump, the archer's inset.\n87\t  - **Target close-up overlay:** Archery's main view.\n88\t  - **Pseudo-3D behind the athlete** (the `road` module, `E.Road`): Downhill, Bobsled.\n89\t  - **Three-quarter** (`'threequarter'`): Figure Skating, Ice Hockey.\n90\t  - Ceremonies, podiums and the title use `'brawler'` in their venue.\n91\t  - **Top-down** (`'topdown'`): Curling.\n92\t  Rationale: each event gets the camera its classic arcade ancestors used, and the engine has a native, tested view\n93\t  for every one of them.\n94\t\n95\t### 1.4 Core loop\n96\t\n97\tPick nation → (ceremony) → **day card** (who, where, a human-interest segment) → **event card** (one screen: goal and\n98\tcontrols with button glyphs) → **compete** (live vs CPU rivals and friends) → **results** (records, qualifying) →\n99\t**medal ceremony** → **medal table** (story beat) → next day. 12 days, then the closing ceremony and an ending that\n100\tdepends on your nation's rank.\n101\t\n102\t### 1.5 Modes (main menu, in this order)\n103\t\n104\t| Item | What it is |\n105\t|---|---|\n106\t| CONTINUE GAMES | only when an autosave exists: resumes The Games at the next day |\n107\t| THE GAMES | the campaign: opening ceremony, 12 days (all 12 events), story beats, halftime report, closing ceremony, ending; or, chosen on its setup screen, **Quick Games**: 4 events (playlists *Track & Pool*, *Snow & Ice*, *Greatest Hits*, *Random 4*) with mini ceremonies and party points. 1–4 players |\n108\t| SINGLE EVENT | any of the 12 events, vs CPU or practice (no rivals); 1–4 players |\n109\t| RECORDS | world records and top-5 tables per event (initials), the Laurel cabinet, the Medal cabinet |\n110\t| HOW TO PLAY | Basics (mash, timing, hype & turbo, yikes) + every event's card |\n111\t| SETTINGS | the engine's settings screen plus the game's own (§2.5) |\n112\t| ABOUT & CREDITS | Source Information, Testing/Engine/Prompt Feedback, credits, engine changes, controls |\n113\t\n114\tOnline play is not a menu item: it starts only when the AI Hub launches the page (§12.2).\n115\t\n116\t---\n117\t\n118\t## 2. Controls and input (controller-first, keyboard and mouse native)\n119\t\n120\t### 2.1 The action map (custom preset `OLY_KEYS`, replaces the engine presets for the whole game)\n121\t\n122\t| Action | Meaning | DualSense (default glyphs) | Xbox glyphs (setting) | Keyboard | Mouse |\n123\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n124\t| `up/down/left/right` | move, steer, aim, balance, menu focus | left stick, d-pad | left stick, d-pad | WASD, arrows | — |\n125\t| `mashL` | \"left\": left foot/arm, push, pass, tuck (diving), in-turn | □ and L1 | X and LB | **J** | — |\n126\t| `mashR` | \"right\": right foot/arm, push, check, pike (diving), out-turn | ○ and R1 | B and RB | **K** | — |\n127\t| `action` | jump, throw, release, start, take-off, shoot | ✕ | A | **Space** | Left button (aim events only) |\n128\t| `turbo` | fire the YIKES TURBO when the hype flame is full | △ | Y | **Shift** | — |\n129\t| `alt` | hold: tuck, breathe, hold breath, skate burst | R2 (and L2) | RT (and LT) | **L** | Right button (aim events only) |\n130\t| `pause` | pause menu | Options | Menu | Esc, P | — |\n131\t| `confirm` | menus: choose | ✕ | A | Enter, Space | click |\n132\t| `cancel` | menus: back | ○ | B | Esc, Backspace | — |\n133\t\n134\tRules:\n135\t- **`confirm`/`cancel` deliberately do not include J or K** (the engine's DEFAULT preset has them): a sprinter mashing J/K\n136\t  must never skip a results screen. Every screen entered after play has a **0.6 s input lockout** and calls\n137\t  `input.consumeAll()` on enter.\n138\t- **Mash = alternate `mashL` and `mashR`.** PC players mash J/K with the right hand; pad players rock □/○ with a thumb\n139\t  or alternate L1/R1 with index fingers (both pairs are bound). Mash assist (§2.5) offers one-button and hold modes.\n140\t- **Mouse:** menus everywhere (hover moves the focus, click picks; `E.Menu` does this, our widgets copy it). In-world\n141\t  only where the genre uses it: Archery (pointer aims, hold left to draw/release to shoot, hold right to hold breath),\n142\t  Curling (pointer aims the broom target, left button = `action`), Hockey (left: hold/release shoot toward the\n143\t  cursor, right: pass toward the cursor), plus clicking flags on Nation Select and tiles on Single Event. Those event\n144\t  scenes set their own `input` preset that adds `Mouse0`/`Mouse2`; other scenes leave the mouse unbound in play.\n145\t- **Pause and the hub:** in an AI Hub session, \"Create + Options\" belongs to the hub: while pad button 8 (Create) is\n146\t  held, suppress `pause` *before* the engine reads it (needs the exported input hook, §4.6 change 1).\n147\t- Two players on one keyboard: the engine's `game.allowJoin` splits it (P1 WASD + F G H R T Y, P2 arrows + `.` `/` `,`\n148\t  and numpad); our actions map onto the halves in preset order (`mashL, mashR, action, turbo, alt`). Prompts follow\n149\t  automatically because every prompt comes from `input.label(action)`.\n150\t\n151\t### 2.2 Per-event use of the actions\n152\t\n153\t| Event | stick / WASD | mashL □ J | mashR ○ K | action ✕ Space | turbo △ Shift | alt R2 L | mouse |\n154\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n155\t| 100m Dash | — | left foot | right foot | react at the gun; dip at the line | turbo | — | — |\n156\t| Javelin | — | run | run | hold: angle rises; release: throw | turbo | — | — |\n157\t| 50m Freestyle | — | left arm (on the beat) | right arm (on the beat) | start dive, flip turn, touch | turbo | breathe | — |\n158\t| 10m Diving | tap ←/→: half twist | hold: tuck | hold: pike | take-off timing | turbo | — | — |\n159\t| Archery | aim | — | — | hold: draw; release: shoot | turbo | hold: hold breath | pointer aims, L draw, R breath |\n160\t| Weightlifting | ←/→ balance | lift | lift | jerk timing | turbo | — | — |\n161\t| Ski Jump | ↑/↓ balance, body angle | — | — | push off, take-off, telemark | turbo | — | — |\n162\t| Downhill | steer | — | — | pre-jump | turbo | hold: tuck | — |\n163\t| Bobsled | steer | push | push | jump in (load) | turbo | — | — |\n164\t| Figure Skating | ← ↓ ↑ → notes | — | — | hold/release jump notes | turbo | — | — |\n165\t| Curling | aim | in-turn; sweep | out-turn; sweep | start slide; release | turbo | — | pointer aims, L = action |\n166\t| Ice Hockey | skate | pass | check / switch skater | hold: charge, release: shoot | ON FIRE | skate burst | L shoot at cursor, R pass at cursor |\n167\t\n168\t### 2.3 Button prompts and glyphs (a must-build: the pixel font has no ✕ ○ □ △)\n169\t\n170\t`input.label(action)` already returns the right *text* for the player's last device and bindings ('J', 'Space',\n171\t'Left click', '✕', 'A'...), and the engine's `glyphs` setting picks the controller family. But the engine's 5×7 pixel\n172\tfont has no ✕ ○ □ △ (they render as `?`). Build **`O.Prompt`** (src/02-prompts.js):\n173\t\n174\t- `O.Prompt.draw(g, x, y, action, { input = player's input, size: 1|2, label: 'RUN', align })` resolves the code\n175\t  for that player's `lastDevice` from `input.map`/`input.bindings`, then draws an **icon**, never plain text:\n176\t  - PlayStation face buttons: a 9×9 (size 1) / 17×17 (size 2) dark disc with a light rim and the symbol drawn in pixels\n177\t    in its traditional color (✕ blue `#7fb2ff`, ○ red `#ff6b6b`, □ pink `#ff8fd8`, △ green `#4fe0a8`).\n178\t  - Xbox face buttons: disc with the letter (A green `#5bc236`, B red `#e8443a`, X blue `#3a7cf0`, Y yellow `#f2c21b`).\n179\t  - Shoulders/triggers: rounded tab \"L1/R1/L2/R2\" or \"LB/RB/LT/RT\"; Options/Menu: small pill; sticks: a ring with an\n180\t    arrow; d-pad: a cross with the pressed arm lit.\n181\t  - Keyboard: a keycap (rounded rect, 1 px darker bottom edge) with the key's label; Space and Shift are wide caps.\n182\t  - Mouse: a mouse outline with the left/right half filled.\n183\t  - A pair prompt for mashing (`O.Prompt.pair(g, x, y, 'mashL', 'mashR')`) alternates highlight at the player's\n184\t    current mash rhythm (teaches the alternation).\n185\t- Prompts follow the **last input used, per player** (`input.lastDevice`); in multiplayer each lane/turn shows its\n186\t  own player's glyphs.\n187\t- **Default glyph family for controllers: PlayStation.** On first boot, if `game.settings.glyphs` is `'auto'` (never\n188\t  chosen) set it to `'playstation'` (engine change 4). The Settings → Game screen has **Controller prompts:\n189\t  PlayStation / Xbox** (key `promptStyle`) whose `apply` calls `game.settings.set('glyphs', v)`.\n190\t- Also add pixel glyphs for ✕ ○ □ △ to the engine's 5×7 and 3×5 fonts (engine change 3) so any stray label text\n191\t  still reads correctly.\n192\t\n193\t### 2.4 Menus\n194\t\n195\tStick/d-pad/WASD/arrows move the focus (with `input.repeat`); ✕/Enter/Space/click choose; ○/Esc/Backspace go back;\n196\tL1/R1 or Q/E switch tabs (also clickable); hovering with the mouse moves the focus. Every screen shows its prompt strip\n197\tat the bottom (`✕ Select  ○ Back`) with glyph icons.\n198\t\n199\t### 2.5 The game's settings (Settings → Game group, via `new E.Game({ menu: { settings: [...] } })`)\n200\t\n201\t| Key | Label | Options (default **bold**) |\n202\t|---|---|---|\n203\t| `difficulty` | Difficulty | Easy / **Normal** / Hard (CPU skill offset −0.12 / 0 / +0.06; timing windows ×1.25 / 1 / 0.85; qualifying standards per event) |\n204\t| `promptStyle` | Controller prompts | **PlayStation** / Xbox |\n205\t| `mashAssist` | Mash assist | **Off** / One button (any mash button counts as an alternation) / Hold (holding either = steady 72% pace) |\n206\t| `timingAssist` | Timing assist | **Off** / On (all timing windows ×1.4) |\n207\t| `commentary` | Commentary | **Voices + subtitles** / Subtitles only / Off |\n208\t| `textSize` | Text size | **Large** / Huge (×1.5 for subtitles, cards and HUD labels) |\n209\t| `hints` | Hints | **On** / Off (contextual tips, e.g. \"Alternate □ and ○!\") |\n210\t| `voices` | Voices volume (Sound group) | slider 0–1, **0.8** (engine change 6) |\n211\t| `crowd` | Crowd volume (Sound group) | slider 0–1, **0.7** |\n212\t\n213\tThe engine's own Display/Sound/Comfort/Controller/Touch settings, rebinding and full screen stay as they are\n214\t(TASK.md: don't rebuild standard features).\n215\t\n216\t---\n217\t\n218\t## 3. UI and UX (10-foot)\n219\t\n220\t### 3.1 Rules\n221\t\n222\t- **Base resolution** `res: 'ps1'` with `expand: true` (a 16:9 TV shows ~427×240 game pixels, scaled ×4.5 at 1080p).\n223\t  Primary text uses `E.font` at **scale 2** (≈63 px tall on a 1080p TV), secondary at scale 1 (≈31 px); never the\n224\t  `tiny` font for anything a player must read. Titles use `E.font.title` scale 4–5.\n225\t- **At most 7 items per list; at most 8 rows per table** (8 nations / 8 lanes). No scrolling tables, no web-style\n226\t  dense screens; long content is paged (L1/R1, ←/→ or clickable page dots).\n227\t- **Focus is loud:** the focused item has a gold bar, a ▸ cursor, a 1 px glow and a gentle scale pulse; a `select`\n228\t  blip on move, `confirm` on choose.\n229\t- **TV-safe margins:** keep HUD and text ≥ 12 game px from every edge; keep the top-right clear of\n230\t  `game.cornerArea()` (the engine's menu/full-screen buttons).\n231\t- **Anchoring:** every HUD element anchors to `r.W`/`r.H`; wide screens show more venue (more stands, more slope).\n232\t- **Information never in color alone:** players are P1–P4 tags plus color (`E.PLAYER_COLORS`), medals carry 1/2/3.\n233\t- **The engine's HTML screens** (pause, settings, controls) must be TV-readable: inject a stylesheet (no engine change)\n234\t  after the engine creates its shell, e.g. `.esh{font-size:clamp(16px,1.55vw,30px)} .esh button{font-size:1.15em;min-height:2.9em;padding:.7em 1em}\n235\t  .esh h2{font-size:2.2em} .esh-mod{width:min(820px,94vw)} .esh input[type=range]{width:min(320px,30vw);height:2.2em}`\n236\t  and theme it gold-on-navy via `E.Shell` theme variables (`accent: '#f2b632'`, `paper: 'rgba(12,16,40,.92)'`).\n237\t  Check with a 1920×1080 screenshot.\n238\t\n239\t### 3.2 Screens (all pixel art unless marked HTML)\n240\t\n241\t| # | Screen | Layout essentials |\n242\t|---|---|---|\n243\t| 1 | Boot (engine) | `boot: { title: 'OLYMPIYIKES!', steps: [...], messages: ['Inflating the blimp', 'Waxing the skis', 'Teaching the crowd to wave', 'Calming the mascot'] }` |\n244\t| 2 | Title | stadium at sunset (summer half) beside a floodlit ski jump (winter half), cauldron burning, blimp, the 8 athletes warming up in a row, logo `OLYMPIYIKES!` (E.font.title scale 5, gold→orange, red outline, depth 3), emblem, tagline, pulsing \"PRESS ✕\" (glyph by device), engine version tiny bottom-right. Idle 10 s → attract |\n245\t| 3 | Main menu | left: big list (§1.5); right: a live vignette for the focused item (parade / pictogram wheel / trophy / the mascot); bottom: description + prompt strip |\n246\t| 4 | Touch-only notice | replaces \"PRESS ✕\": panel **\"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\"**, one line \"Connect a controller or keyboard to play.\", a big **SETTINGS** button (tap → `game.menu('settings')`). Attract still runs |\n247\t| 5 | Games setup | rows: Length (Full 12 / Quick 4 + playlist), Difficulty, Qualifying (On for 1P / Off), START |\n248\t| 6 | Nation select + join | 4×2 grid of big flags (48×32) with codes; each player's cursor in its color with a P-tag; right panel: the focused nation's athlete (live rig cheering), name, 3 specialty pictograms, one-line bio; \"P2–P4: press ✕ on another controller, or 2 on the keyboard\" |\n249\t| 7 | Opening ceremony | cinematic (§7.4), hold ✕ for 1 s to skip |\n250\t| 8 | Day card (\"broadcast bumper\") | `DAY 3 · 50m FREESTYLE` / venue / weather; lower third: **UP CLOSE & PERSONAL** with a big portrait and 2–3 subtitle lines; optional rival line |\n251\t| 9 | Event card | pictogram + name; GOAL line; 3–4 rows of glyph icon(s) + verb; Qualifying standard, World record; prompts `✕ Start  ○ Back` (+ `△ Practice` in Single Event) |\n252\t| 10 | Event HUD | per event (§6); common: top-left event + pictogram, top-right clock/score (big digits), bottom: per-player prompt strip and the hype flame |\n253\t| 11 | Turn card | \"P2 — YOUR TURN\" in player color / \"ROUND 2 OF 3\" + top-4 standings |\n254\t| 12 | Results | ≤ 8 rows: rank, medal icon, flag, athlete, performance, notes (WR, GR, PB, Q, DNF, DQ); humans' rows in player color; records burst; `✕ Continue` |\n255\t| 13 | Initials entry | `E.Arcade` letter wheel when a human makes a top-5 table (skipped in hub) |\n256\t| 14 | Medal ceremony | podium in the venue, medals, three flags rising, the winner's procedural anthem, fireworks |\n257\t| 15 | Medal table | 8 nation rows (flag, code, G S B, total), yours highlighted; a ticker of the day's highlights |\n258\t| 16 | Story beat | day-card layout with one or two portraits (halftime report, incidents, rival) |\n259\t| 17 | Torch lost / Games over | \"YIKES! NO QUALIFYING MARK — TORCHES ●●○\" → retry; at 0: \"GAMES OVER — CONTINUE? 9\" |\n260\t| 18 | Closing + ending + credits | cinematic, ending text by rank, credits roll (paged, skippable) |\n261\t| 19 | Single Event select | 4×3 grid of event tiles (pictogram, name, season color, your best medal); bottom: description |\n262\t| 20 | Records | tabs per event (←/→ or L1/R1): top-5 rows; tabs LAURELS (12 tiles) and CABINET (nation × event medals as icons) |\n263\t| 21 | How to play | Basics pages + list of 12 event cards (read-only) |\n264\t| 22 | Settings / Controls / Pause | engine HTML (scaled, themed) |\n265\t| 23 | About & Credits | paged: Source Information · Testing Feedback · Engine Feedback · Prompt Feedback · Credits & engine changes · Controls |\n266\t| 24 | Dev panel | pixel overlay (§13) |\n267\t| 25 | Hub card / hub splash | §12.2 |\n268\t\n269\tTransitions: `game.go(scene, data, { fade: 'wipe' })` between menu screens, `'iris'` into events, `'white'` into\n270\tceremonies (reduce-motion turns them into plain fades by itself).\n271\t\n272\t### 3.3 Touch-only devices\n273\t\n274\t`touchOnly = matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches\n275\t&& navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0` **and** no key press or gamepad has been seen this visit. While true: show screen 4,\n276\thide engine touch buttons (scenes declare `touch: []`; set the engine's `touch` setting to `'off'` at boot),\n277\tlet the attract mode run after 10 s; a tap during attract returns to the notice. A `gamepadconnected` event or any key\n278\tpress flips `touchOnly` to false at once and shows the normal title.\n279\t\n280\t---\n281\t\n282\t## 4. Architecture\n283\t\n284\t### 4.1 Tech stack\n285\t\n286\t- **Engine:** our copy of the my-3D2dge v0.85.2 full engine (`engine/my-3d2dge.js`: the core plus every module; we use\n287\t  the `road`, `rhythm`, `physics`, `arcade` and `songs` modules from it). Plain JavaScript, no libraries, no CDN, no\n288\t  network at runtime.\n289\t- **Online:** AI Hub `session.js` 1.4.0, unmodified, first script in `<head>`.\n290\t- **Tooling:** Node (headless tests via `vm`, as `game/test.mjs` does), Playwright 1.63.0 + Chromium (browser checks,\n291\t  hub harness, screenshots), the handoff's `tools/check.mjs` and `tools/filmstrip.mjs`.\n292\t- **Deliverable:** one self-contained HTML (engine + session client + game inlined), ~1.8 MB, works from `file://`.\n293\t\n294\t### 4.2 Folder layout\n295\t\n296\t```\n297\tOlympiyikes-OlympicGames-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174837/\n298\t  index.html                 dev page: same <head> as the bundle; loads engine + src files in order (the list is the bundle's source of truth)\n299\t  engine/my-3d2dge.js        the engine + our changes, each marked  // OLY: <why>\n300\t  vendor/hub/                session.js (bundled, unmodified) + harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, README.md (tests only)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b1b95e-beb5-4384-ba72-665ccf7128b3","uuid":"36e1895f-e0fa-4a2b-906c-09e2c8f8902c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:41:27.601Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-074118__x0e4b02/work/PLAN.md","content":"# Olympiyikes!\n\n**Tagline:** *Faster. Higher. Yikes.*\n**One line:** the complete Summer *and* Winter Games, held in the same fortnight in one twin-city host, played as\nan over-the-top arcade multi-event: 12 events, 8 nations, ceremonies, a rival, two hyperventilating commentators,\n1–4 players on the couch and AI Hub ghost heats online.\n\n> **How the title was picked (TASK.md rule):** 50 riffs on \"Olympic Games\" were brainstormed silently, then\n> `secrets.randbelow(50)` (Python, OS CSPRNG) returned **16 → \"Olympiyikes!\"**. Do not re-roll it. Its file-name\n> form is `Olympiyikes`; the SOURCE token is `OlympicGames`.\n\n---\n\n## 0. Read this first (ground rules for the builders)\n\n- **Inputs:** `TASK.md` (requirements) + this plan. If they disagree, TASK.md wins. Where this plan is silent, follow\n  the engine's own docs (`API.md`, `AI_GUIDE.md`) and the plan's spirit. Everything listed here ships: **no TODOs,\n  placeholders, locked \"coming soon\" slots or stubbed features.**\n- **Names (with this TASK.md):** dev folder `Olympiyikes-OlympicGames-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174837/`, deliverable\n  `Olympiyikes-OlympicGames-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174837.html` in the root (beside TASK.md), and\n  `exit-interview.json` in the root. If your TASK.md's name pattern carries a different model/date, use your pattern\n  with `Olympiyikes` and `OlympicGames`.\n- **Shared machine:** read only the files you need (other agents share the parent directories, ports and processes).\n  Prefer `file://` and the engine's headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), run\n  `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` from your dev folder, read the port it prints, and confirm the served page\n  is *your* game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by PID. Never `pkill`, `killall`,\n  `fuser -k`. During planning `/tmp` was 100% full: if npm/Playwright fail with ENOSPC, set `TMPDIR=<dev>/.tmp`.\n- **Engine:** my-3D2dge handoff package, **v0.85.2** at planning time\n  (`https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge/tree/main/dist/handoff`). We own our copy and may change it (§4.6).\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, client **1.4.0** (`https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub`).\n- **No subagents/workflows to debate, review, judge or audit** (TASK.md). Tests are scripts.\n- **Units used in this plan:** world units (u) are the engine's (one tile = 16 u, z is up). Distances shown to the\n  player are meters; each event says its scale (default **M = 12 u per meter**). Times in seconds unless marked ms.\n  The engine runs fixed steps of 1/120 s.\n\n### 0.1 Fetch what you build on (once, inside the dev folder)\n\n```sh\nD=Olympiyikes-OlympicGames-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174837 && mkdir -p $D/{engine,src,tests,tools,vendor/hub,.tmp} && cd $D\ngit clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git vendor/my-3d2dge\ngit -C vendor/my-3d2dge sparse-checkout set dist/handoff\ncp vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js engine/my-3d2dge.js          # our engine copy (we edit this one)\nfor f in session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js README.md; do\n  curl -fsSL -o vendor/hub/$f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/$f; done\n(cd vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff && export TMPDIR=\"$(cd ../../../.. && pwd)/.tmp\" && npm install && npx playwright install chromium)\n```\n\nRead whole: `vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/API.md`, `README.md`, `kits/README.md`, `docs/ASSETS.md`,\n`vendor/hub/README.md`. Read as references (copy patterns, not whole files): `kits/sports.js` (hockey), `kits/road.js`\n(downhill/bobsled), `kits/rhythm.js` (figure skating), `kits/pinball.js` + `modules/physics.js` (curling),\n`kits/kart.js` (drawing a rig through a custom view), `modules/arcade.js` (record tables, initials), `game/test.mjs`\nand `kits/test.mjs` (headless harness). Grep `API-INDEX.md` for names; don't read it whole.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The game\n\n### 1.1 Pitch\n\nFor the first time in history the Summer and Winter Games share one fortnight and one host: **Mount Glory–Sunny Bay**,\nwhere a ski jump towers over the beach and the swimming pool shares a wall with the ice rink. Eight fictional nations\nsend their stars. You pick a nation and its athlete, light the cauldron, and chase gold across **12 events** that\nalternate summer and winter, while defending champion **Max Overdrive of Turbonia** insists, loudly, that it is all\npointless because he will win. Everything is broadcast like the real thing (parade of nations, \"Up Close & Personal\"\nprofiles, photo finishes, medal ceremonies with anthems, a medal table) and played like an arcade cabinet (mashing,\ntiming, aiming, steering, rhythm, physics; a HYPE meter that sets you on fire; world records that explode into\nfireworks). When it goes wrong, it goes *gloriously* wrong: false starts, belly flops, ski-jump tumbles, bobsleds on\ntheir roof. That's an **OLYMPIYIKES!**, and the game celebrates it.\n\n### 1.2 Pillars\n\n1. **Ten seconds to learn, a lifetime to perfect.** Each event teaches one verb (mash, time, aim, steer, keep the beat,\n   sweep) on one card, and has a perfect-play ceiling with world records to chase.\n2. **Broadcast spectacle.** Ceremonies, commentators, crowd, jumbotron, slow-mo, photo finishes, anthems, records.\n3. **Failure is a show.** Every event has at least one comic \"Yikes\" moment that is funny, fast to recover from, and\n   even pays a little hype (§5.8).\n4. **Both seasons.** 6 summer + 6 winter events on alternating days; each venue has its own look, light and music.\n5. **Couch first, online too.** 1–4 local players in every mode; AI Hub ghost heats when the hub launches the game.\n\n### 1.3 Genre and perspective (decisions)\n\n- **Genre:** arcade multi-event sports (Track & Field / Winter Games lineage) with a short campaign, local party\n  play and online ghost heats. Each event is a compact mini-game built on one shared event framework.\n- **Perspective:** per event, all on the engine's native 2D views (pixel art at `res: 'ps1'`, `expand: true`):\n  - **2.5D side-on lanes** (`'brawler'` view, pitch 25): 100m Dash, Javelin, 50m Freestyle, Weightlifting.\n  - **Pure side view** (`'side'`): 10m Diving, Ski Jump, the archer's inset.\n  - **Target close-up overlay:** Archery's main view.\n  - **Pseudo-3D behind the athlete** (the `road` module, `E.Road`): Downhill, Bobsled.\n  - **Three-quarter** (`'threequarter'`): Figure Skating, Ice Hockey.\n  - Ceremonies, podiums and the title use `'brawler'` in their venue.\n  - **Top-down** (`'topdown'`): Curling.\n  Rationale: each event gets the camera its classic arcade ancestors used, and the engine has a native, tested view\n  for every one of them.\n\n### 1.4 Core loop\n\nPick nation → (ceremony) → **day card** (who, where, a human-interest segment) → **event card** (one screen: goal and\ncontrols with button glyphs) → **compete** (live vs CPU rivals and friends) → **results** (records, qualifying) →\n**medal ceremony** → **medal table** (story beat) → next day. 12 days, then the closing ceremony and an ending that\ndepends on your nation's rank.\n\n### 1.5 Modes (main menu, in this order)\n\n| Item | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| CONTINUE GAMES | only when an autosave exists: resumes The Games at the next day |\n| THE GAMES | the campaign: opening ceremony, 12 days (all 12 events), story beats, halftime report, closing ceremony, ending; or, chosen on its setup screen, **Quick Games**: 4 events (playlists *Track & Pool*, *Snow & Ice*, *Greatest Hits*, *Random 4*) with mini ceremonies and party points. 1–4 players |\n| SINGLE EVENT | any of the 12 events, vs CPU or practice (no rivals); 1–4 players |\n| RECORDS | world records and top-5 tables per event (initials), the Laurel cabinet, the Medal cabinet |\n| HOW TO PLAY | Basics (mash, timing, hype & turbo, yikes) + every event's card |\n| SETTINGS | the engine's settings screen plus the game's own (§2.5) |\n| ABOUT & CREDITS | Source Information, Testing/Engine/Prompt Feedback, credits, engine changes, controls |\n\nOnline play is not a menu item: it starts only when the AI Hub launches the page (§12.2).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Controls and input (controller-first, keyboard and mouse native)\n\n### 2.1 The action map (custom preset `OLY_KEYS`, replaces the engine presets for the whole game)\n\n| Action | Meaning | DualSense (default glyphs) | Xbox glyphs (setting) | Keyboard | Mouse |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `up/down/left/right` | move, steer, aim, balance, menu focus | left stick, d-pad | left stick, d-pad | WASD, arrows | — |\n| `mashL` | \"left\": left foot/arm, push, pass, tuck (diving), in-turn | □ and L1 | X and LB | **J** | — |\n| `mashR` | \"right\": right foot/arm, push, check, pike (diving), out-turn | ○ and R1 | B and RB | **K** | — |\n| `action` | jump, throw, release, start, take-off, shoot | ✕ | A | **Space** | Left button (aim events only) |\n| `turbo` | fire the YIKES TURBO when the hype flame is full | △ | Y | **Shift** | — |\n| `alt` | hold: tuck, breathe, hold breath, skate burst | R2 (and L2) | RT (and LT) | **L** | Right button (aim events only) |\n| `pause` | pause menu | Options | Menu | Esc, P | — |\n| `confirm` | menus: choose | ✕ | A | Enter, Space | click |\n| `cancel` | menus: back | ○ | B | Esc, Backspace | — |\n\nRules:\n- **`confirm`/`cancel` deliberately do not include J or K** (the engine's DEFAULT preset has them): a sprinter mashing J/K\n  must never skip a results screen. Every screen entered after play has a **0.6 s input lockout** and calls\n  `input.consumeAll()` on enter.\n- **Mash = alternate `mashL` and `mashR`.** PC players mash J/K with the right hand; pad players rock □/○ with a thumb\n  or alternate L1/R1 with index fingers (both pairs are bound). Mash assist (§2.5) offers one-button and hold modes.\n- **Mouse:** menus everywhere (hover moves the focus, click picks; `E.Menu` does this, our widgets copy it). In-world\n  only where the genre uses it: Archery (pointer aims, hold left to draw/release to shoot, hold right to hold breath),\n  Curling (pointer aims the broom target, left button = `action`), Hockey (left: hold/release shoot toward the\n  cursor, right: pass toward the cursor), plus clicking flags on Nation Select and tiles on Single Event. Those event\n  scenes set their own `input` preset that adds `Mouse0`/`Mouse2`; other scenes leave the mouse unbound in play.\n- **Pause and the hub:** in an AI Hub session, \"Create + Options\" belongs to the hub: while pad button 8 (Create) is\n  held, suppress `pause` *before* the engine reads it (needs the exported input hook, §4.6 change 1).\n- Two players on one keyboard: the engine's `game.allowJoin` splits it (P1 WASD + F G H R T Y, P2 arrows + `.` `/` `,`\n  and numpad); our actions map onto the halves in preset order (`mashL, mashR, action, turbo, alt`). Prompts follow\n  automatically because every prompt comes from `input.label(action)`.\n\n### 2.2 Per-event use of the actions\n\n| Event | stick / WASD | mashL □ J | mashR ○ K | action ✕ Space | turbo △ Shift | alt R2 L | mouse |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 100m Dash | — | left foot | right foot | react at the gun; dip at the line | turbo | — | — |\n| Javelin | — | run | run | hold: angle rises; release: throw | turbo | — | — |\n| 50m Freestyle | — | left arm (on the beat) | right arm (on the beat) | start dive, flip turn, touch | turbo | breathe | — |\n| 10m Diving | tap ←/→: half twist | hold: tuck | hold: pike | take-off timing | turbo | — | — |\n| Archery | aim | — | — | hold: draw; release: shoot | turbo | hold: hold breath | pointer aims, L draw, R breath |\n| Weightlifting | ←/→ balance | lift | lift | jerk timing | turbo | — | — |\n| Ski Jump | ↑/↓ balance, body angle | — | — | push off, take-off, telemark | turbo | — | — |\n| Downhill | steer | — | — | pre-jump | turbo | hold: tuck | — |\n| Bobsled | steer | push | push | jump in (load) | turbo | — | — |\n| Figure Skating | ← ↓ ↑ → notes | — | — | hold/release jump notes | turbo | — | — |\n| Curling | aim | in-turn; sweep | out-turn; sweep | start slide; release | turbo | — | pointer aims, L = action |\n| Ice Hockey | skate | pass | check / switch skater | hold: charge, release: shoot | ON FIRE | skate burst | L shoot at cursor, R pass at cursor |\n\n### 2.3 Button prompts and glyphs (a must-build: the pixel font has no ✕ ○ □ △)\n\n`input.label(action)` already returns the right *text* for the player's last device and bindings ('J', 'Space',\n'Left click', '✕', 'A'...), and the engine's `glyphs` setting picks the controller family. But the engine's 5×7 pixel\nfont has no ✕ ○ □ △ (they render as `?`). Build **`O.Prompt`** (src/02-prompts.js):\n\n- `O.Prompt.draw(g, x, y, action, { input = player's input, size: 1|2, label: 'RUN', align })` resolves the code\n  for that player's `lastDevice` from `input.map`/`input.bindings`, then draws an **icon**, never plain text:\n  - PlayStation face buttons: a 9×9 (size 1) / 17×17 (size 2) dark disc with a light rim and the symbol drawn in pixels\n    in its traditional color (✕ blue `#7fb2ff`, ○ red `#ff6b6b`, □ pink `#ff8fd8`, △ green `#4fe0a8`).\n  - Xbox face buttons: disc with the letter (A green `#5bc236`, B red `#e8443a`, X blue `#3a7cf0`, Y yellow `#f2c21b`).\n  - Shoulders/triggers: rounded tab \"L1/R1/L2/R2\" or \"LB/RB/LT/RT\"; Options/Menu: small pill; sticks: a ring with an\n    arrow; d-pad: a cross with the pressed arm lit.\n  - Keyboard: a keycap (rounded rect, 1 px darker bottom edge) with the key's label; Space and Shift are wide caps.\n  - Mouse: a mouse outline with the left/right half filled.\n  - A pair prompt for mashing (`O.Prompt.pair(g, x, y, 'mashL', 'mashR')`) alternates highlight at the player's\n    current mash rhythm (teaches the alternation).\n- Prompts follow the **last input used, per player** (`input.lastDevice`); in multiplayer each lane/turn shows its\n  own player's glyphs.\n- **Default glyph family for controllers: PlayStation.** On first boot, if `game.settings.glyphs` is `'auto'` (never\n  chosen) set it to `'playstation'` (engine change 4). The Settings → Game screen has **Controller prompts:\n  PlayStation / Xbox** (key `promptStyle`) whose `apply` calls `game.settings.set('glyphs', v)`.\n- Also add pixel glyphs for ✕ ○ □ △ to the engine's 5×7 and 3×5 fonts (engine change 3) so any stray label text\n  still reads correctly.\n\n### 2.4 Menus\n\nStick/d-pad/WASD/arrows move the focus (with `input.repeat`); ✕/Enter/Space/click choose; ○/Esc/Backspace go back;\nL1/R1 or Q/E switch tabs (also clickable); hovering with the mouse moves the focus. Every screen shows its prompt strip\nat the bottom (`✕ Select  ○ Back`) with glyph icons.\n\n### 2.5 The game's settings (Settings → Game group, via `new E.Game({ menu: { settings: [...] } })`)\n\n| Key | Label | Options (default **bold**) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `difficulty` | Difficulty | Easy / **Normal** / Hard (CPU skill offset −0.12 / 0 / +0.06; timing windows ×1.25 / 1 / 0.85; qualifying standards per event) |\n| `promptStyle` | Controller prompts | **PlayStation** / Xbox |\n| `mashAssist` | Mash assist | **Off** / One button (any mash button counts as an alternation) / Hold (holding either = steady 72% pace) |\n| `timingAssist` | Timing assist | **Off** / On (all timing windows ×1.4) |\n| `commentary` | Commentary | **Voices + subtitles** / Subtitles only / Off |\n| `textSize` | Text size | **Large** / Huge (×1.5 for subtitles, cards and HUD labels) |\n| `hints` | Hints | **On** / Off (contextual tips, e.g. \"Alternate □ and ○!\") |\n| `voices` | Voices volume (Sound group) | slider 0–1, **0.8** (engine change 6) |\n| `crowd` | Crowd volume (Sound group) | slider 0–1, **0.7** |\n\nThe engine's own Display/Sound/Comfort/Controller/Touch settings, rebinding and full screen stay as they are\n(TASK.md: don't rebuild standard features).\n\n---\n\n## 3. UI and UX (10-foot)\n\n### 3.1 Rules\n\n- **Base resolution** `res: 'ps1'` with `expand: true` (a 16:9 TV shows ~427×240 game pixels, scaled ×4.5 at 1080p).\n  Primary text uses `E.font` at **scale 2** (≈63 px tall on a 1080p TV), secondary at scale 1 (≈31 px); never the\n  `tiny` font for anything a player must read. Titles use `E.font.title` scale 4–5.\n- **At most 7 items per list; at most 8 rows per table** (8 nations / 8 lanes). No scrolling tables, no web-style\n  dense screens; long content is paged (L1/R1, ←/→ or clickable page dots).\n- **Focus is loud:** the focused item has a gold bar, a ▸ cursor, a 1 px glow and a gentle scale pulse; a `select`\n  blip on move, `confirm` on choose.\n- **TV-safe margins:** keep HUD and text ≥ 12 game px from every edge; keep the top-right clear of\n  `game.cornerArea()` (the engine's menu/full-screen buttons).\n- **Anchoring:** every HUD element anchors to `r.W`/`r.H`; wide screens show more venue (more stands, more slope).\n- **Information never in color alone:** players are P1–P4 tags plus color (`E.PLAYER_COLORS`), medals carry 1/2/3.\n- **The engine's HTML screens** (pause, settings, controls) must be TV-readable: inject a stylesheet (no engine change)\n  after the engine creates its shell, e.g. `.esh{font-size:clamp(16px,1.55vw,30px)} .esh button{font-size:1.15em;min-height:2.9em;padding:.7em 1em}\n  .esh h2{font-size:2.2em} .esh-mod{width:min(820px,94vw)} .esh input[type=range]{width:min(320px,30vw);height:2.2em}`\n  and theme it gold-on-navy via `E.Shell` theme variables (`accent: '#f2b632'`, `paper: 'rgba(12,16,40,.92)'`).\n  Check with a 1920×1080 screenshot.\n\n### 3.2 Screens (all pixel art unless marked HTML)\n\n| # | Screen | Layout essentials |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Boot (engine) | `boot: { title: 'OLYMPIYIKES!', steps: [...], messages: ['Inflating the blimp', 'Waxing the skis', 'Teaching the crowd to wave', 'Calming the mascot'] }` |\n| 2 | Title | stadium at sunset (summer half) beside a floodlit ski jump (winter half), cauldron burning, blimp, the 8 athletes warming up in a row, logo `OLYMPIYIKES!` (E.font.title scale 5, gold→orange, red outline, depth 3), emblem, tagline, pulsing \"PRESS ✕\" (glyph by device), engine version tiny bottom-right. Idle 10 s → attract |\n| 3 | Main menu | left: big list (§1.5); right: a live vignette for the focused item (parade / pictogram wheel / trophy / the mascot); bottom: description + prompt strip |\n| 4 | Touch-only notice | replaces \"PRESS ✕\": panel **\"CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED\"**, one line \"Connect a controller or keyboard to play.\", a big **SETTINGS** button (tap → `game.menu('settings')`). Attract still runs |\n| 5 | Games setup | rows: Length (Full 12 / Quick 4 + playlist), Difficulty, Qualifying (On for 1P / Off), START |\n| 6 | Nation select + join | 4×2 grid of big flags (48×32) with codes; each player's cursor in its color with a P-tag; right panel: the focused nation's athlete (live rig cheering), name, 3 specialty pictograms, one-line bio; \"P2–P4: press ✕ on another controller, or 2 on the keyboard\" |\n| 7 | Opening ceremony | cinematic (§7.4), hold ✕ for 1 s to skip |\n| 8 | Day card (\"broadcast bumper\") | `DAY 3 · 50m FREESTYLE` / venue / weather; lower third: **UP CLOSE & PERSONAL** with a big portrait and 2–3 subtitle lines; optional rival line |\n| 9 | Event card | pictogram + name; GOAL line; 3–4 rows of glyph icon(s) + verb; Qualifying standard, World record; prompts `✕ Start  ○ Back` (+ `△ Practice` in Single Event) |\n| 10 | Event HUD | per event (§6); common: top-left event + pictogram, top-right clock/score (big digits), bottom: per-player prompt strip and the hype flame |\n| 11 | Turn card | \"P2 — YOUR TURN\" in player color / \"ROUND 2 OF 3\" + top-4 standings |\n| 12 | Results | ≤ 8 rows: rank, medal icon, flag, athlete, performance, notes (WR, GR, PB, Q, DNF, DQ); humans' rows in player color; records burst; `✕ Continue` |\n| 13 | Initials entry | `E.Arcade` letter wheel when a human makes a top-5 table (skipped in hub) |\n| 14 | Medal ceremony | podium in the venue, medals, three flags rising, the winner's procedural anthem, fireworks |\n| 15 | Medal table | 8 nation rows (flag, code, G S B, total), yours highlighted; a ticker of the day's highlights |\n| 16 | Story beat | day-card layout with one or two portraits (halftime report, incidents, rival) |\n| 17 | Torch lost / Games over | \"YIKES! NO QUALIFYING MARK — TORCHES ●●○\" → retry; at 0: \"GAMES OVER — CONTINUE? 9\" |\n| 18 | Closing + ending + credits | cinematic, ending text by rank, credits roll (paged, skippable) |\n| 19 | Single Event select | 4×3 grid of event tiles (pictogram, name, season color, your best medal); bottom: description |\n| 20 | Records | tabs per event (←/→ or L1/R1): top-5 rows; tabs LAURELS (12 tiles) and CABINET (nation × event medals as icons) |\n| 21 | How to play | Basics pages + list of 12 event cards (read-only) |\n| 22 | Settings / Controls / Pause | engine HTML (scaled, themed) |\n| 23 | About & Credits | paged: Source Information · Testing Feedback · Engine Feedback · Prompt Feedback · Credits & engine changes · Controls |\n| 24 | Dev panel | pixel overlay (§13) |\n| 25 | Hub card / hub splash | §12.2 |\n\nTransitions: `game.go(scene, data, { fade: 'wipe' })` between menu screens, `'iris'` into events, `'white'` into\nceremonies (reduce-motion turns them into plain fades by itself).\n\n### 3.3 Touch-only devices\n\n`touchOnly = matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches\n&& navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0` **and** no key press or gamepad has been seen this visit. While true: show screen 4,\nhide engine touch buttons (scenes declare `touch: []`; set the engine's `touch` setting to `'off'` at boot),\nlet the attract mode run after 10 s; a tap during attract returns to the notice. A `gamepadconnected` event or any key\npress flips `touchOnly` to false at once and shows the normal title.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Architecture\n\n### 4.1 Tech stack\n\n- **Engine:** our copy of the my-3D2dge v0.85.2 full engine (`engine/my-3d2dge.js`: the core plus every module; we use\n  the `road`, `rhythm`, `physics`, `arcade` and `songs` modules from it). Plain JavaScript, no libraries, no CDN, no\n  network at runtime.\n- **Online:** AI Hub `session.js` 1.4.0, unmodified, first script in `<head>`.\n- **Tooling:** Node (headless tests via `vm`, as `game/test.mjs` does), Playwright 1.63.0 + Chromium (browser checks,\n  hub harness, screenshots), the handoff's `tools/check.mjs` and `tools/filmstrip.mjs`.\n- **Deliverable:** one self-contained HTML (engine + session client + game inlined), ~1.8 MB, works from `file://`.\n\n### 4.2 Folder layout\n\n```\nOlympiyikes-OlympicGames-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174837/\n  index.html                 dev page: same <head> as the bundle; loads engine + src files in order (the list is the bundle's source of truth)\n  engine/my-3d2dge.js        the engine + our changes, each marked  // OLY: <why>\n  vendor/hub/                session.js (bundled, unmodified) + harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, README.md (tests only)","numLines":300,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1723}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016Q3PfZHedr3GKwC7vxaf2X","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
