{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ULpKx46M2jo7YhcASfkW1Q","type":"tool_result","content":"300\t  vendor/hub/                session.js (bundled, unmodified) + harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, README.md (tests only)\n301\t  vendor/my-3d2dge/          sparse clone of the handoff: docs, kits, tools (reference + Playwright); never bundled\n302\t  src/                       the game: one IIFE per file, all attach to window.OLY (alias O)\n303\t  tests/                     run.mjs (the one command) + suites\n304\t  tools/bundle.mjs           builds the root HTML from index.html's script list\n305\t  tools/shots.mjs            screenshot/filmstrip helper around the handoff tools\n306\t```\n307\t\n308\t### 4.3 Source files (load order = bundle order)\n309\t\n310\t| File | Responsibility |\n311\t|---|---|\n312\t| `00-core.js` | creates `window.OLY`, defines `OLY_KEYS` and `GAME_SETTINGS`, then the `E.Game` (§4.4), constants (`M`, palettes), `O.def(kind, id, spec)` registries, `O.bus` (on/emit), `O.store` (E.store wrappers), `O.rng(label)` streams (§4.7), formatting helpers |\n313\t| `01-input.js` | per-scene presets (archery/curling/hockey add mouse), **pilots** (§5.2), `Mash` meter, `O.AutoPlayer` (bot intents → real `input.tap/hold`), idle/any-input tracker, touch-only detection, hub Create+Options guard |\n314\t| `02-prompts.js` | `O.Prompt` glyph renderer (§2.3) |\n315\t| `03-ui.js` | 10-foot widgets: `Menu10` (vertical list), `Grid10` (tile grid), `Tabs`, `Panel`, `Banner` (big stamped words), `Ticker`, `LowerThird`, `Toast`, page dots, number/time formatters; mouse hover/click via `input.pointer()`/`clicked()` |\n316\t| `04-audio.js` | SFX definitions (`audio.define`), songs (§9), `O.Voice` gibberish synth, `O.CrowdAudio`, `O.Anthem` generator, stings |\n317\t| `05-art.js` | palettes per venue, flag painter, pictograms, emblem, equipment sprites, stands + crowd painter, jumbotron (dot matrix), podium, fireworks/confetti helpers, mascot (Blob) |\n318\t| `06-pose.js` | `O.Pose` library and `O.Gear` (equipment drawn at joints), body rotation (§8.2) |\n319\t| `07-athletes.js` | `NATIONS` data (§7.1), teammates, `O.makeRig(nation, sport, opts)` outfits per sport, voice params |\n320\t| `08-commentary.js` | `O.Comms`: commentators, line banks (§7.6), cue rules, subtitles + voice + portraits |\n321\t| `09-hype.js` | `O.Hype` (meter, turbo), `O.Yikes` (stamp, count, sympathy hype), `O.Crowd` (visual excitement), slow-mo/photo helpers |\n322\t| `10-records.js` | world records seed table, games records, personal bests, top-5 tables via `E.Arcade`, points formulas, medal table, party points, laurels, cabinet |\n323\t| `11-ghosts.js` | ghost recording/playback (local turns + hub), compact samples |\n324\t| `12-eventkit.js` | the event contract, `O.defEvent`, the phase runner, formats (race / attempts / match / program), CPU simulation, results assembly, qualifying, timing widgets (`TimingBar`, `Ring`, `Balance`, `Sway`, `StrokeBeat`) |\n325\t| `20-ev-sprint.js` … `35-ev-hockey.js` | one file per event (§6), ids: `sprint javelin swim diving archery weights skijump downhill bobsled figure curling hockey` |\n326\t| `40-sc-title.js` | title, main menu, touch-only notice, attract director (§11) |\n327\t| `41-sc-games.js` | games setup, nation select/join, opening ceremony, day card, story beats, event card, turn card, results, initials, medal ceremony, medal table, torch/continue, closing + ending + credits |\n328\t| `42-sc-misc.js` | single event select, records, how to play, about & credits, pose lab |\n329\t| `43-dev.js` | dev panel, tuning sliders, cheats, overlays (§13) |\n330\t| `44-hub.js` | AI Hub session flow (§12.2) |\n331\t| `99-main.js` | registers scenes, deep links (`#ev/<id>`, `#scene/<name>`, `#attract`, `#poselab`, `#games/day/<n>`), `game.debug`, `window.__oly` for tests, `game.start({ scenes, scene, boot })` |\n332\t\n333\tEach file: `(() => { 'use strict'; const E = My3D2dge, O = OLY; ... })();`. Tests load exactly the same files in the same\n334\torder into a `vm` context (read the list from `index.html` so it can't drift).\n335\t\n336\t### 4.4 The game object\n337\t\n338\t```js\n339\tconst game = O.game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'brawler', input: OLY_KEYS,\n340\t  id: 'olympiyikes', bg: '#0b0f24',\n341\t  menu: { items: inHub ? [] : [['Restart event', () => O.restartEvent()], ['How to play', () => O.showEventCard()], ['Dev mode', () => O.Dev.open()]],\n342\t          settings: GAME_SETTINGS /* §2.5 */, quit: inHub ? false : 'title',\n343\t          controls: { mashL: 'Left (mash, pass, tuck)', mashR: 'Right (mash, check, pike)', action: 'Action (jump, throw, release)',\n344\t                      turbo: 'Yikes Turbo', alt: 'Hold (tuck, breathe, steady)' } } });\n345\t```\n346\t`inHub = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active)` (true from the client's first line). `OLY_KEYS` and `GAME_SETTINGS` are defined\n347\tin `00-core.js` above this call (the later files only add to them); the menu callbacks are arrows because their targets\n348\tare defined in later files. Menu items are static, so each item's\n349\tfunction is context-aware: outside an event \"Restart event\" and \"How to play\" show `game.note('Not in an event')`.\n350\t\n351\t### 4.5 Scenes\n352\t\n353\t`O.scene(name, def)` registers a wrapped engine scene. The wrapper: calls `input.consumeAll()` on enter; applies the\n354\t0.6 s lockout (`def.lock`); if the dev panel is open, runs `O.Dev.update()` instead of `def.update` and draws the panel\n355\tafter `def.draw`; draws global overlays (toasts, commentary lower third, attract banner, \"YIKES\" stamps, laurel toasts)\n356\tafter the scene; tracks idle time on menu scenes (`def.menu: true`) for the attract mode; routes `back()`.\n357\t\n358\tScenes: `title`, `menu`, `touchonly` (a state of `title`), `attract`, `gamesSetup`, `nations`, `opening`, `dayCard`,\n359\t`beat`, `eventCard`, `turnCard` (overlay state inside events), `ev:<id>` ×12, `results`, `initials`, `podium`,\n360\t`medals`, `torch`, `closing`, `credits`, `single`, `records`, `howto`, `about`, `poselab`, `hubCard`, `hubSplash`.\n361\t\n362\t`O.flow` is the state machine above them: it holds the current **meet** (§4.8) and decides the next scene after each\n363\tone ends (`O.flow.next(from, payload)`), for each mode (games, quick, single, hub, attract).\n364\t\n365\t### 4.6 Engine changes (all marked `// OLY:` in `engine/my-3d2dge.js`; list them on the About screen)\n366\t\n367\t1. **Export the hooks:** `E.HOOKS = HOOKS;` so the game can run code at the start of every step even while paused\n368\t   (`HOOKS.input`): hub Create+Options guard, global any-input detection.\n369\t2. **Cosmetic randomness off `Math.random`:** the Humanoid (`this.t` start phase, blink timer), `Particles` and\n370\t   `hitFx`'s number jitter draw from a module-level `const cosmetic = rng(0xC05E7)` instead of `Math.random`. Then\n371\t   cosmetics never shift gameplay randomness, the hub card draws no `Math.random` numbers, and tests stay\n372\t   deterministic.\n373\t3. **Font glyphs:** add ✕ ○ □ △ to the 5×7 (`G57`) and 3×5 (`GLYPHS`) tables.\n374\t4. **PlayStation by default:** the `glyphs` setting's default becomes `'playstation'`.\n375\t5. **Pose hook on the Humanoid:** at the end of `solvePose()`, if `this.post` is a function call `this.post(this, this.J)`;\n376\t   then, if `this.bodyPitch || this.bodyRoll`, rotate every joint (and cape/hair points, as `_roll` does) about\n377\t   `this.pivot` (default: hip centre) by pitch (forward–up plane) and roll (right–up plane), **without** `_roll`'s\n378\t   floor lift. This is what flips, dives, swims, tumbles and V-style flight need (§8.2).\n379\t6. **Voice bus:** `ChipAudio` gets a `_voiceBus` gain under the master, a `voiceVolume` field honored by\n380\t   `applyVolume()`, and the settings get `voices` (Sound group, default .8). `O.Voice` connects to it.\n381\t\n382\t### 4.7 Randomness and determinism\n383\t\n384\t- **Gameplay randomness only through labeled streams:** `O.rng(label)` returns a `[0,1)` generator. In a hub session\n385\t  it is `AIHub.rng(label)` (identical on every copy); otherwise `E.rng(hash(meet.seed + '|' + label))`. Labels are\n386\t  namespaced: `'sprint:gun'`, `'javelin:wind:r2'`, `'cpu:FRM:skijump:j1'`, `'judges:diving:SUN:d3'`.\n387\t- Cosmetics (particles, blinks, crowd bob) never touch `Math.random` (engine change 2) or the gameplay streams.\n388\t- `meet.seed` comes from the clock when a meet starts; tests and the dev panel can set it.\n389\t- Every event sim is a function of (state, intents, streams), independent of drawing, so a sim can run headless,\n390\t  twice, and hash the same (the kits' \"proof\" idea).\n391\t\n392\t### 4.8 Data model\n393\t\n394\t```\n395\tNation   { id: 'SUN', name: 'SUNVALE', colors: { a, b, c }, flag: { kind, ... }, athlete: { name, rig, bio, voice },\n396\t           team: [3 names], skills: { sprint: .92, ... }, anthem: { seed, key, bpm } }\n397\tAthlete  { id, nation, name, rig, gear, pilot, lane, human, player (0-3 | null), hype, turboT, state: {}, attempts: [],\n398\t           best, notes: [], ghost }\n399\tPilot    { kind: 'human' | 'bot' | 'ghost' | 'net', input?, skill, cheat?: 'perfect' | null }\n400\tIntent   { L, R, A, T (pressed this step), Lh, Rh, Ad, Au, X (held / released), mv: [x, y], aim: [x, y] | null }\n401\tMeet     { mode, seed, events: [ids], day, players: [{ input, nation, color }], difficulty, qualifying, torches,\n402\t           medals: { SUN: { g, s, b } }, party: { P1: pts }, results: { eventId: Results }, beats: Set, yikes: { SUN: n } }\n403\tResults  { event, rows: [{ athlete, perf, display, rank, medal, notes, points }], records: [], laurels: [] }\n404\tStore    'oly:records' (top-5 per event + WR), 'oly:laurels', 'oly:cabinet', 'oly:games' (autosave),\n405\t         'oly:ghost:<event>' (best local run), 'oly:seen' (first-time tips), 'oly:tune' (only if the dev opts in)\n406\t```\n407\t\n408\t### 4.9 Bundle\n409\t\n410\t`node tools/bundle.mjs` reads `index.html`'s `<script src>` list and writes the root HTML:\n411\t\n412\t```html\n413\t<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n414\t<script>/* vendor/hub/session.js, byte-for-byte */</script>\n415\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n416\t<title>Olympiyikes! — Faster. Higher. Yikes.</title>\n417\t<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Twelve over-the-top Summer and Winter events in one wild fortnight, for 1–4 players.\">\n418\t<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#f2b632\"><link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:image/svg+xml,...the emblem...\">\n419\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"><meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n420\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Score the most points across three Olympiyikes events\">\n421\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD move · □○ or J K mash · ✕/Space act · △/Shift turbo · R2/L hold\">\n422\t<meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"The Olympic Games\"><meta name=\"hub:model\" content=\"(the building model's id)\">\n423\t<style>/* page + 10-foot shell overrides */</style></head><body>\n424\t<!-- E.bootSplash('OLYMPIYIKES!') markup --><canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n425\t<script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js */</script><script>/* src/*.js concatenated */</script></body></html>\n426\t```\n427\tEscape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\/script`. The session client must stay unmodified and first after\n428\t`<meta charset>`. The bundle test (§16) checks all of this.\n429\t\n430\t---\n431\t\n432\t## 5. Shared gameplay systems\n433\t\n434\t### 5.1 The event contract (`O.defEvent`) and the phase runner\n435\t\n436\tEvery event is one call. The EventKit turns it into an engine scene `ev:<id>`, registers it in `O.EVENTS`, its\n437\ttunables in the tuning registry (§5.13), its card in How to Play, its segment in the attract playlist and, if\n438\t`hub.ok`, in the hub deal.\n439\t\n440\t```js\n441\tO.defEvent({\n442\t  id: 'sprint', name: '100m DASH', short: '100m', season: 'summer', venue: 'stadium', pictogram: 'sprint',\n443\t  music: 'sprint', view: 'brawler', input: OLY_KEYS, camera: { zoom: [.8, 1.6] }, M: 12,\n444\t  format: { type: 'race', attempts: 1, maxHumans: 4 },                  // race | attempts | match | program\n445\t  measure: { unit: 's', better: 'lower', fmt: v => v.toFixed(2) + ' s',\n446\t             wr: [9.48, 'TRB', 'MAX OVERDRIVE'], qualify: { Easy: 12.30, Normal: 11.40, Hard: 10.60 } },\n447\t  points: t => 25.4347 * Math.pow(Math.max(0, 18 - t), 1.81),          // ≈ 0..1250 (WR level ≈ 1100–1250), used by party + hub\n448\t  tune: { vMax: [11.6, 8, 16, .1, 'Top speed (m/s)'], ... },           // [default, min, max, step, label]\n449\t  howto: { goal: 'Fastest to the line wins.', rows: [[['mashL', 'mashR'], 'Alternate to run'], [['action'], 'React to the gun · dip at the line'], [['turbo'], 'Turbo when the flame is full']] },\n450\t  laurel: { id: 'rocket', name: 'ROCKET MAN', text: 'React in 0.120 s or less and win', test: (ctx, a, res) => ... },\n451\t  hub: { ok: true, attempts: 1, seconds: 35 }, attract: { seconds: 18, featured: 'perfect' },\n452\t  build(ctx) {},            // once per scene entry: venue, props, crowd, static data (heavy work: boot steps or here)\n453\t  intro(ctx, t) {},         // optional cinematic (lane introductions); returns true when finished; skippable\n454\t  start(ctx) {},            // per heat / attempt: place athletes, reset per-attempt state\n455\t  ready(ctx, dt) {},        // marks / countdown; returns true when play begins\n456\t  step(ctx, dt) {},         // the simulation: reads ctx.intent(a) for each active athlete; never reads game.input directly\n457\t  bot(ctx, a) {},           // returns an Intent for a CPU/attract/autopilot athlete (skill a.pilot.skill, cheat a.pilot.cheat)\n458\t  done(ctx) {},             // true when the heat / attempt is over\n459\t  perf(ctx, a) {},          // the performance number, or null (DNF / foul / DQ: put the reason in a.notes)\n460\t  draw(ctx, r) {}, hud(ctx, r) {}                                     // skipped headless\n461\t});\n462\t```\n463\t\n464\t**The runner's phases:** `intro` → `ready` → `play` (`step` until `done`) → `finish` (2–3 s celebration, slow-mo,\n465\t\"WORLD RECORD!\" bursts) → `between` (turn card / next round / standings) → back to `start` or → `done` → the flow\n466\tgets the `Results`. `intro` is skipped in hub, attract and on retries; any phase can be jumped to from the dev panel.\n467\t\n468\t**`ctx`** (what the runner gives every hook): `def, meet, game, athletes, humans, active` (those in the current\n469\theat/attempt), `round, attempt, phase, phaseT, t` (seconds of play), `rng(label)` (namespaced by event and attempt),\n470\t`T` (live tunables of this event: `ctx.T.vMax`), `G` (global tunables), `intent(a)`, `emit(name, data)` (bus: comms,\n471\tcrowd, hype, sfx, laurels, tests listen), `finish(a, perf, notes)`, `dnf(a, why)`, `dq(a, why)`, `slowmo(scale, s)`,\n472\t`cam` helpers, `ghosts`.\n473\t\n474\t**Sims are separable from scenes:** each event's state lives in plain objects created by `start`; `step` only touches\n475\tthem. The runner can create a **sandbox ctx** (no scene, no drawing, its own stream labels) to simulate unseen CPU\n476\tattempts by running `start`/`ready`/`step` with bot pilots until `done` (§5.3). Tests use the same sandbox.\n477\t\n478\t### 5.2 Pilots, intents and the autoplayer\n479\t\n480\t- A **pilot** fills an athlete's `Intent` each step: `human` (from its `game.players[i]` input: `pressed('mashL')`,\n481\t  `down('alt')`, `move()`, pointer for aim), `bot` (from `def.bot(ctx, a)`), `ghost` (replays a recording, §5.9),\n482\t  `net` (a hub ghost: drawn only, never simulated).\n483\t- Mash assist is applied in the human pilot (§2.5): One button → every `mashL`/`mashR` press is reported as the\n484\t  alternation the meter expects; Hold → while either is held, synthesize alternations at 72% of `G.mashRateMax`.\n485\t- **`O.AutoPlayer`** drives a *human* athlete through the real input path: each step it asks `def.bot` for an intent\n486\t  and turns it into `input.tap`/`input.hold` calls on that player's input. Used by the dev \"Autopilot\" cheat and by\n487\t  the scripted playthrough test (so menus, prompts, lockouts and the human pilot all get exercised).\n488\t- Cheats are pilot flags: `cheat: 'perfect'` makes `bot` return frame-perfect inputs and keeps hype full (attract,\n489\t  dev \"God mode\").\n490\t- **Fresh presses only:** a human intent ignores buttons still held from before the current phase began (`Ad`, `Lh`,\n491\t  `Rh`, `X` become true only after a press inside the phase), so Space or ✕ held through the event card never starts\n492\t  a javelin's angle or a dive's tuck.\n493\t\n494\t### 5.3 Formats\n495\t\n496\t| Format | Used by | How the runner plays it |\n497\t|---|---|---|\n498\t| `race` | 100m, 50m Free | one heat, all 8 athletes live (humans in the middle lanes 3–6, CPUs fill) |\n499\t| `attempts` | Javelin (3), Diving (3), Archery (6 arrows as 2 ends), Weightlifting (3), Ski Jump (2), Downhill (1), Bobsled (2) | rounds × athletes in start order. Humans play live. CPU attempts: per round the **2 most relevant** (current leader, the rival, or whoever can overtake a human) play live as **highlights** at 1.5× game speed (✕ skips to the result); the rest are simulated instantly in a sandbox and appear on the standings board |\n500\t| `program` | Figure Skating | like `attempts` with 1 attempt; CPU programs are simulated (score cards shown in the kiss & cry) |\n501\t| `match` | Curling, Ice Hockey | the event runs its own match vs one CPU (or human) nation; the other placings come from `O.Sim.placings(eventId, nations)` (skill-weighted draws from a stream), so all 8 nations get a rank |\n502\t\n503\tTurn order: humans in join order, CPUs by ascending skill (best last, like a real final). Between rounds the standings\n504\tboard shows the top 4 and every human.\n505\t\n506\t### 5.4 Input widgets (src/12-eventkit.js; each has `update`, `press`/`read` and a 10-foot `draw`)\n507\t\n508\t- **`Mash`** (`window: .5 s`): counts *alternations* (a press of the other button than the last one). `rate` = EMA of\n509\t  alternations per second; a same-button press counts 0.25 and grows `same` (the streak resets on a true\n510\t  alternation). Events map `rate` to power with `power = clamp((rate - G.mashRateMin) / (G.mashRateMax - G.mashRateMin), 0, 1) ** .75`\n511\t  (defaults: `mashRateMin 2`, `mashRateMax 10.5` Hz). HUD: the two glyphs pulsing alternately + a 10-segment rate bar.\n512\t- **`TimingBar`**: a needle sweeping a bar (ping-pong, `hz`), zones `[{ from, to, name, q }]`; `press()` → `{ q, zone }`.\n513\t  Windows scale with difficulty and Timing assist.\n514\t- **`Ring`**: a ring shrinking onto a target ring over `dur`; `press()` → signed error in ms → PERFECT ≤ 60 ms,\n515\t  GOOD ≤ 140 ms (×window scale), else BAD.\n516\t- **`Balance`**: a needle `b ∈ [-1, 1]` with drift `b'' = noise(t) * drift - b' * damp`, corrected by the stick axis\n517\t  (`b' += -axis * k * dt`); out of `[-1, 1]` = lost. Noise from the event's stream (deterministic).\n518\t- **`Sway`**: archery reticle: Lissajous + value noise, amplitude driven by the event (§6.5).\n519\t- **`StrokeBeat`**: swimming: alternating expected buttons on a tempo that follows speed; judged like `Ring`.\n520\t\n521\t### 5.5 Hype and YIKES TURBO\n522\t\n523\t- Each athlete has `hype ∈ [0, 1]`, shown as a **flame meter** beside its name (fills orange → white-hot; full = the\n524\t  turbo glyph flashes: \"△ TURBO!\"). Gains come from the event (perfect starts, perfect timing, clean gates, combos),\n525\t  scaled by `G.hypeGain` (1.0); decay `G.hypeDecay` (0.02/s) when not full.\n526\t- Pressing `turbo` with a full flame fires **YIKES TURBO** for `G.turboTime` (3 s): the event's own effect\n527\t  (listed per event), the athlete bursts into (harmless, cartoon) flames (`particles.fire` at the feet/hands + glow\n528\t  light), the music's `hype` layer fades in (`audio.layer('hype', 1, .3)`), the crowd surges, commentary cue\n529\t  `turbo`. `G.turboPower` (1.0) scales every event's turbo multiplier.\n530\t- CPU bots fire turbo at their event's best moment with probability = skill.\n531\t\n532\t### 5.6 CPU rivals and difficulty\n533\t\n534\t- Every nation's athlete has a skill per event (§7.1). Effective skill = `clamp(skill * G.cpuSkillScale + offset, .05, .99)`\n535\t  with offset −0.12 / 0 / +0.06 for Easy / Normal / Hard (all three offsets are dev sliders).\n536\t- Bots play **the same rules through intents** (no pre-rolled results): mash rate, reaction time, timing error,\n537\t  aim error, steering noise, turbo use all derive from skill plus noise from the event's stream. This keeps balance\n538\t  honest and lets tests measure it.\n539\t- The rival (Turbonia's Max Overdrive; if a human picked Turbonia, the CPU nation with the highest average skill) gets\n540\t  +0.03 and always plays live highlights.\n541\t\n542\t### 5.7 Results, qualifying, points, records, medals\n543\t\n544\t- **Ranking** by best performance (`better`), ties by the event's tie rule (stated per event), then by earlier\n545\t  attempt. Nulls (DNF/foul/DQ) rank last in their order.\n546\t- **Medals** to ranks 1–3 (match events: winner gold, loser silver, simulated bronze match).\n547\t- **Qualifying (The Games, 1 player, Qualifying On):** a human result worse than `qualify[difficulty]` → \"YIKES! NO\n548\t  QUALIFYING MARK\" → lose a torch (3 per Games) and retry the event (CPU results stand; the retry replaces yours).\n549\t  0 torches → GAMES OVER → CONTINUE? (10 s countdown): yes restores 3 torches and retries; no → title (records and\n550\t  laurels are kept). Match events have no qualifying check. Multi-human Games default Qualifying Off.\n551\t- **Points** (≈ 0–1250, per event formula; a world-record performance is worth ≈ 1100–1250 in every event): party totals in Quick Games / multi-human Games and the hub score.\n552\t- **Party points** (multi-human): 10 8 6 5 4 3 2 1 by rank among all 8; the overall champion is crowned at the end.\n553\t- **Records:** in-world World Records (seed table in §7.5), Games Records (best ever on this device, `oly:records`),\n554\t  Personal Bests per nation. A beaten WR → \"WORLD RECORD!\" banner, fireworks, WR sting, commentary, the jumbotron.\n555\t  Top-5 tables per event with **initials** (`E.Arcade`: `cab.qualifies`, `cab.enter`, `cab.table`), skipped in hub.\n556\t- **Medal table:** gold, then silver, then bronze, then nation name.\n557\t\n558\t### 5.8 Yikes moments\n559\t\n560\t`O.Yikes.trigger(a, kind, at)`: a giant comic stamp **\"OLYMPIYIKES!\"** (or the kind's own word: \"FALSE START!\",\n561\t\"BELLY FLOP!\", \"BONK!\", \"FOUL!\") with shake, the descending-trombone sting, crowd gasp + \"OOOH\", a commentary cue,\n562\t`yikes[nation]++` (shown at the closing ceremony as the \"Yikes reel\"), and **sympathy hype +0.15** (`G.yikesHype`), so\n563\ta comeback is always possible. Reduce-motion keeps the stamp still. Each event lists its yikes kinds; every one must\n564\tbe reachable by ordinary bad play (tests force each).\n565\t\n566\t### 5.9 Ghosts\n567\t\n568\t`O.Ghost.rec(a)` samples `[t, x, y, z, facing, poseCode, extra]` at 20 Hz into a compact array; `O.Ghost.at(track, t)`\n569\tinterpolates; `O.Ghost.draw(ctx, r, state, { tint, name })` draws a translucent rig (`r.actor(..., { alpha: .45 })`\n570\ttinted with the player/seat color) plus a name tag. Uses: the leader's run in Downhill/Bobsled, the previous\n571\tplayer's attempt in turn-based multiplayer, your best local run per event (stored, ≤ 3000 samples), and hub ghosts\n572\t(§12.2) which arrive as the same samples over the network.\n573\t\n574\t### 5.10 Commentary\n575\t\n576\t- Two commentators plus the stadium PA (§7.6): **CHIP BELLOWS** (play-by-play, booming hyperbole), **DAME VERA\n577\t  VELOCITY** (seven-time champion turned colour commentator, dry and sentimental), and the PA announcer (echo).\n578\t- `O.Comms.cue(key, vars, { prio })`: picks a line from the event bank, falling back to the generic bank; never two\n579\t  lines within 3.5 s, each key has a cooldown, higher priority interrupts (WR > yikes > photo finish > lead change >\n580\t  filler). Lines may be two-speaker exchanges.\n581\t- Display: a **lower third** with the speaker's live portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`), name, and up to 2 lines of\n582\t  subtitles at scale 2 (Text size Huge = larger), above the prompt strip and clear of the touch area. Voice: `O.Voice`\n583\t  gibberish (§9.3); the portrait's mouth moves while it speaks. Setting \"Commentary\" picks voices+subs / subs / off.\n584\t- Vars: `{name}`, `{nation}`, `{time}`, `{dist}`, `{rival}`, `{place}`.\n585\t\n586\t### 5.11 Crowd, jumbotron, camera, slow-mo\n587\t\n588\t- **Stands** are TileMap tiers (or painted bands in side views) with a crowd painter: one `r.queue` per stand section\n589\t  draws hundreds of 3×5 px spectators (head + shirt in nation colors), bobbing by `O.Crowd.level` (0..1), waving flags,\n590\t  camera-flash glints, doing **the wave** when hype turbo fires or a record falls. The crowd audio follows the same\n591\t  level.\n592\t- **Jumbotron** (stadium, arena, pools): a dot-matrix panel (like the pinball kit's display) showing the event, the\n593\t  clock, the leader, \"WORLD RECORD!\" and a live portrait of the leader.\n594\t- **Camera:** `game.focus` on the human leader (or `cam.frame` on all humans, `zoom: [.6, 1]`) in races; event-\n595\t  specific shots elsewhere. `ctx.slowmo(scale, seconds)` sets `game.timeScale` (photo finish .25, landings .35) and\n596\t  restores it; reduce motion shortens it.\n597\t\n598\t### 5.12 Laurels\n599\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b1b95e-beb5-4384-ba72-665ccf7128b3","uuid":"b759b269-6440-4944-95b5-10ee93258db6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:41:30.877Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-074118__x0e4b02/work/PLAN.md","content":"  vendor/hub/                session.js (bundled, unmodified) + harness.html, bridge.js, round.js, README.md (tests only)\n  vendor/my-3d2dge/          sparse clone of the handoff: docs, kits, tools (reference + Playwright); never bundled\n  src/                       the game: one IIFE per file, all attach to window.OLY (alias O)\n  tests/                     run.mjs (the one command) + suites\n  tools/bundle.mjs           builds the root HTML from index.html's script list\n  tools/shots.mjs            screenshot/filmstrip helper around the handoff tools\n```\n\n### 4.3 Source files (load order = bundle order)\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `00-core.js` | creates `window.OLY`, defines `OLY_KEYS` and `GAME_SETTINGS`, then the `E.Game` (§4.4), constants (`M`, palettes), `O.def(kind, id, spec)` registries, `O.bus` (on/emit), `O.store` (E.store wrappers), `O.rng(label)` streams (§4.7), formatting helpers |\n| `01-input.js` | per-scene presets (archery/curling/hockey add mouse), **pilots** (§5.2), `Mash` meter, `O.AutoPlayer` (bot intents → real `input.tap/hold`), idle/any-input tracker, touch-only detection, hub Create+Options guard |\n| `02-prompts.js` | `O.Prompt` glyph renderer (§2.3) |\n| `03-ui.js` | 10-foot widgets: `Menu10` (vertical list), `Grid10` (tile grid), `Tabs`, `Panel`, `Banner` (big stamped words), `Ticker`, `LowerThird`, `Toast`, page dots, number/time formatters; mouse hover/click via `input.pointer()`/`clicked()` |\n| `04-audio.js` | SFX definitions (`audio.define`), songs (§9), `O.Voice` gibberish synth, `O.CrowdAudio`, `O.Anthem` generator, stings |\n| `05-art.js` | palettes per venue, flag painter, pictograms, emblem, equipment sprites, stands + crowd painter, jumbotron (dot matrix), podium, fireworks/confetti helpers, mascot (Blob) |\n| `06-pose.js` | `O.Pose` library and `O.Gear` (equipment drawn at joints), body rotation (§8.2) |\n| `07-athletes.js` | `NATIONS` data (§7.1), teammates, `O.makeRig(nation, sport, opts)` outfits per sport, voice params |\n| `08-commentary.js` | `O.Comms`: commentators, line banks (§7.6), cue rules, subtitles + voice + portraits |\n| `09-hype.js` | `O.Hype` (meter, turbo), `O.Yikes` (stamp, count, sympathy hype), `O.Crowd` (visual excitement), slow-mo/photo helpers |\n| `10-records.js` | world records seed table, games records, personal bests, top-5 tables via `E.Arcade`, points formulas, medal table, party points, laurels, cabinet |\n| `11-ghosts.js` | ghost recording/playback (local turns + hub), compact samples |\n| `12-eventkit.js` | the event contract, `O.defEvent`, the phase runner, formats (race / attempts / match / program), CPU simulation, results assembly, qualifying, timing widgets (`TimingBar`, `Ring`, `Balance`, `Sway`, `StrokeBeat`) |\n| `20-ev-sprint.js` … `35-ev-hockey.js` | one file per event (§6), ids: `sprint javelin swim diving archery weights skijump downhill bobsled figure curling hockey` |\n| `40-sc-title.js` | title, main menu, touch-only notice, attract director (§11) |\n| `41-sc-games.js` | games setup, nation select/join, opening ceremony, day card, story beats, event card, turn card, results, initials, medal ceremony, medal table, torch/continue, closing + ending + credits |\n| `42-sc-misc.js` | single event select, records, how to play, about & credits, pose lab |\n| `43-dev.js` | dev panel, tuning sliders, cheats, overlays (§13) |\n| `44-hub.js` | AI Hub session flow (§12.2) |\n| `99-main.js` | registers scenes, deep links (`#ev/<id>`, `#scene/<name>`, `#attract`, `#poselab`, `#games/day/<n>`), `game.debug`, `window.__oly` for tests, `game.start({ scenes, scene, boot })` |\n\nEach file: `(() => { 'use strict'; const E = My3D2dge, O = OLY; ... })();`. Tests load exactly the same files in the same\norder into a `vm` context (read the list from `index.html` so it can't drift).\n\n### 4.4 The game object\n\n```js\nconst game = O.game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'brawler', input: OLY_KEYS,\n  id: 'olympiyikes', bg: '#0b0f24',\n  menu: { items: inHub ? [] : [['Restart event', () => O.restartEvent()], ['How to play', () => O.showEventCard()], ['Dev mode', () => O.Dev.open()]],\n          settings: GAME_SETTINGS /* §2.5 */, quit: inHub ? false : 'title',\n          controls: { mashL: 'Left (mash, pass, tuck)', mashR: 'Right (mash, check, pike)', action: 'Action (jump, throw, release)',\n                      turbo: 'Yikes Turbo', alt: 'Hold (tuck, breathe, steady)' } } });\n```\n`inHub = !!(window.AIHub && AIHub.active)` (true from the client's first line). `OLY_KEYS` and `GAME_SETTINGS` are defined\nin `00-core.js` above this call (the later files only add to them); the menu callbacks are arrows because their targets\nare defined in later files. Menu items are static, so each item's\nfunction is context-aware: outside an event \"Restart event\" and \"How to play\" show `game.note('Not in an event')`.\n\n### 4.5 Scenes\n\n`O.scene(name, def)` registers a wrapped engine scene. The wrapper: calls `input.consumeAll()` on enter; applies the\n0.6 s lockout (`def.lock`); if the dev panel is open, runs `O.Dev.update()` instead of `def.update` and draws the panel\nafter `def.draw`; draws global overlays (toasts, commentary lower third, attract banner, \"YIKES\" stamps, laurel toasts)\nafter the scene; tracks idle time on menu scenes (`def.menu: true`) for the attract mode; routes `back()`.\n\nScenes: `title`, `menu`, `touchonly` (a state of `title`), `attract`, `gamesSetup`, `nations`, `opening`, `dayCard`,\n`beat`, `eventCard`, `turnCard` (overlay state inside events), `ev:<id>` ×12, `results`, `initials`, `podium`,\n`medals`, `torch`, `closing`, `credits`, `single`, `records`, `howto`, `about`, `poselab`, `hubCard`, `hubSplash`.\n\n`O.flow` is the state machine above them: it holds the current **meet** (§4.8) and decides the next scene after each\none ends (`O.flow.next(from, payload)`), for each mode (games, quick, single, hub, attract).\n\n### 4.6 Engine changes (all marked `// OLY:` in `engine/my-3d2dge.js`; list them on the About screen)\n\n1. **Export the hooks:** `E.HOOKS = HOOKS;` so the game can run code at the start of every step even while paused\n   (`HOOKS.input`): hub Create+Options guard, global any-input detection.\n2. **Cosmetic randomness off `Math.random`:** the Humanoid (`this.t` start phase, blink timer), `Particles` and\n   `hitFx`'s number jitter draw from a module-level `const cosmetic = rng(0xC05E7)` instead of `Math.random`. Then\n   cosmetics never shift gameplay randomness, the hub card draws no `Math.random` numbers, and tests stay\n   deterministic.\n3. **Font glyphs:** add ✕ ○ □ △ to the 5×7 (`G57`) and 3×5 (`GLYPHS`) tables.\n4. **PlayStation by default:** the `glyphs` setting's default becomes `'playstation'`.\n5. **Pose hook on the Humanoid:** at the end of `solvePose()`, if `this.post` is a function call `this.post(this, this.J)`;\n   then, if `this.bodyPitch || this.bodyRoll`, rotate every joint (and cape/hair points, as `_roll` does) about\n   `this.pivot` (default: hip centre) by pitch (forward–up plane) and roll (right–up plane), **without** `_roll`'s\n   floor lift. This is what flips, dives, swims, tumbles and V-style flight need (§8.2).\n6. **Voice bus:** `ChipAudio` gets a `_voiceBus` gain under the master, a `voiceVolume` field honored by\n   `applyVolume()`, and the settings get `voices` (Sound group, default .8). `O.Voice` connects to it.\n\n### 4.7 Randomness and determinism\n\n- **Gameplay randomness only through labeled streams:** `O.rng(label)` returns a `[0,1)` generator. In a hub session\n  it is `AIHub.rng(label)` (identical on every copy); otherwise `E.rng(hash(meet.seed + '|' + label))`. Labels are\n  namespaced: `'sprint:gun'`, `'javelin:wind:r2'`, `'cpu:FRM:skijump:j1'`, `'judges:diving:SUN:d3'`.\n- Cosmetics (particles, blinks, crowd bob) never touch `Math.random` (engine change 2) or the gameplay streams.\n- `meet.seed` comes from the clock when a meet starts; tests and the dev panel can set it.\n- Every event sim is a function of (state, intents, streams), independent of drawing, so a sim can run headless,\n  twice, and hash the same (the kits' \"proof\" idea).\n\n### 4.8 Data model\n\n```\nNation   { id: 'SUN', name: 'SUNVALE', colors: { a, b, c }, flag: { kind, ... }, athlete: { name, rig, bio, voice },\n           team: [3 names], skills: { sprint: .92, ... }, anthem: { seed, key, bpm } }\nAthlete  { id, nation, name, rig, gear, pilot, lane, human, player (0-3 | null), hype, turboT, state: {}, attempts: [],\n           best, notes: [], ghost }\nPilot    { kind: 'human' | 'bot' | 'ghost' | 'net', input?, skill, cheat?: 'perfect' | null }\nIntent   { L, R, A, T (pressed this step), Lh, Rh, Ad, Au, X (held / released), mv: [x, y], aim: [x, y] | null }\nMeet     { mode, seed, events: [ids], day, players: [{ input, nation, color }], difficulty, qualifying, torches,\n           medals: { SUN: { g, s, b } }, party: { P1: pts }, results: { eventId: Results }, beats: Set, yikes: { SUN: n } }\nResults  { event, rows: [{ athlete, perf, display, rank, medal, notes, points }], records: [], laurels: [] }\nStore    'oly:records' (top-5 per event + WR), 'oly:laurels', 'oly:cabinet', 'oly:games' (autosave),\n         'oly:ghost:<event>' (best local run), 'oly:seen' (first-time tips), 'oly:tune' (only if the dev opts in)\n```\n\n### 4.9 Bundle\n\n`node tools/bundle.mjs` reads `index.html`'s `<script src>` list and writes the root HTML:\n\n```html\n<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>/* vendor/hub/session.js, byte-for-byte */</script>\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>Olympiyikes! — Faster. Higher. Yikes.</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Twelve over-the-top Summer and Winter events in one wild fortnight, for 1–4 players.\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#f2b632\"><link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:image/svg+xml,...the emblem...\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"><meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Score the most points across three Olympiyikes events\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD move · □○ or J K mash · ✕/Space act · △/Shift turbo · R2/L hold\">\n<meta name=\"hub:source\" content=\"The Olympic Games\"><meta name=\"hub:model\" content=\"(the building model's id)\">\n<style>/* page + 10-foot shell overrides */</style></head><body>\n<!-- E.bootSplash('OLYMPIYIKES!') markup --><canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n<script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js */</script><script>/* src/*.js concatenated */</script></body></html>\n```\nEscape every `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\/script`. The session client must stay unmodified and first after\n`<meta charset>`. The bundle test (§16) checks all of this.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Shared gameplay systems\n\n### 5.1 The event contract (`O.defEvent`) and the phase runner\n\nEvery event is one call. The EventKit turns it into an engine scene `ev:<id>`, registers it in `O.EVENTS`, its\ntunables in the tuning registry (§5.13), its card in How to Play, its segment in the attract playlist and, if\n`hub.ok`, in the hub deal.\n\n```js\nO.defEvent({\n  id: 'sprint', name: '100m DASH', short: '100m', season: 'summer', venue: 'stadium', pictogram: 'sprint',\n  music: 'sprint', view: 'brawler', input: OLY_KEYS, camera: { zoom: [.8, 1.6] }, M: 12,\n  format: { type: 'race', attempts: 1, maxHumans: 4 },                  // race | attempts | match | program\n  measure: { unit: 's', better: 'lower', fmt: v => v.toFixed(2) + ' s',\n             wr: [9.48, 'TRB', 'MAX OVERDRIVE'], qualify: { Easy: 12.30, Normal: 11.40, Hard: 10.60 } },\n  points: t => 25.4347 * Math.pow(Math.max(0, 18 - t), 1.81),          // ≈ 0..1250 (WR level ≈ 1100–1250), used by party + hub\n  tune: { vMax: [11.6, 8, 16, .1, 'Top speed (m/s)'], ... },           // [default, min, max, step, label]\n  howto: { goal: 'Fastest to the line wins.', rows: [[['mashL', 'mashR'], 'Alternate to run'], [['action'], 'React to the gun · dip at the line'], [['turbo'], 'Turbo when the flame is full']] },\n  laurel: { id: 'rocket', name: 'ROCKET MAN', text: 'React in 0.120 s or less and win', test: (ctx, a, res) => ... },\n  hub: { ok: true, attempts: 1, seconds: 35 }, attract: { seconds: 18, featured: 'perfect' },\n  build(ctx) {},            // once per scene entry: venue, props, crowd, static data (heavy work: boot steps or here)\n  intro(ctx, t) {},         // optional cinematic (lane introductions); returns true when finished; skippable\n  start(ctx) {},            // per heat / attempt: place athletes, reset per-attempt state\n  ready(ctx, dt) {},        // marks / countdown; returns true when play begins\n  step(ctx, dt) {},         // the simulation: reads ctx.intent(a) for each active athlete; never reads game.input directly\n  bot(ctx, a) {},           // returns an Intent for a CPU/attract/autopilot athlete (skill a.pilot.skill, cheat a.pilot.cheat)\n  done(ctx) {},             // true when the heat / attempt is over\n  perf(ctx, a) {},          // the performance number, or null (DNF / foul / DQ: put the reason in a.notes)\n  draw(ctx, r) {}, hud(ctx, r) {}                                     // skipped headless\n});\n```\n\n**The runner's phases:** `intro` → `ready` → `play` (`step` until `done`) → `finish` (2–3 s celebration, slow-mo,\n\"WORLD RECORD!\" bursts) → `between` (turn card / next round / standings) → back to `start` or → `done` → the flow\ngets the `Results`. `intro` is skipped in hub, attract and on retries; any phase can be jumped to from the dev panel.\n\n**`ctx`** (what the runner gives every hook): `def, meet, game, athletes, humans, active` (those in the current\nheat/attempt), `round, attempt, phase, phaseT, t` (seconds of play), `rng(label)` (namespaced by event and attempt),\n`T` (live tunables of this event: `ctx.T.vMax`), `G` (global tunables), `intent(a)`, `emit(name, data)` (bus: comms,\ncrowd, hype, sfx, laurels, tests listen), `finish(a, perf, notes)`, `dnf(a, why)`, `dq(a, why)`, `slowmo(scale, s)`,\n`cam` helpers, `ghosts`.\n\n**Sims are separable from scenes:** each event's state lives in plain objects created by `start`; `step` only touches\nthem. The runner can create a **sandbox ctx** (no scene, no drawing, its own stream labels) to simulate unseen CPU\nattempts by running `start`/`ready`/`step` with bot pilots until `done` (§5.3). Tests use the same sandbox.\n\n### 5.2 Pilots, intents and the autoplayer\n\n- A **pilot** fills an athlete's `Intent` each step: `human` (from its `game.players[i]` input: `pressed('mashL')`,\n  `down('alt')`, `move()`, pointer for aim), `bot` (from `def.bot(ctx, a)`), `ghost` (replays a recording, §5.9),\n  `net` (a hub ghost: drawn only, never simulated).\n- Mash assist is applied in the human pilot (§2.5): One button → every `mashL`/`mashR` press is reported as the\n  alternation the meter expects; Hold → while either is held, synthesize alternations at 72% of `G.mashRateMax`.\n- **`O.AutoPlayer`** drives a *human* athlete through the real input path: each step it asks `def.bot` for an intent\n  and turns it into `input.tap`/`input.hold` calls on that player's input. Used by the dev \"Autopilot\" cheat and by\n  the scripted playthrough test (so menus, prompts, lockouts and the human pilot all get exercised).\n- Cheats are pilot flags: `cheat: 'perfect'` makes `bot` return frame-perfect inputs and keeps hype full (attract,\n  dev \"God mode\").\n- **Fresh presses only:** a human intent ignores buttons still held from before the current phase began (`Ad`, `Lh`,\n  `Rh`, `X` become true only after a press inside the phase), so Space or ✕ held through the event card never starts\n  a javelin's angle or a dive's tuck.\n\n### 5.3 Formats\n\n| Format | Used by | How the runner plays it |\n|---|---|---|\n| `race` | 100m, 50m Free | one heat, all 8 athletes live (humans in the middle lanes 3–6, CPUs fill) |\n| `attempts` | Javelin (3), Diving (3), Archery (6 arrows as 2 ends), Weightlifting (3), Ski Jump (2), Downhill (1), Bobsled (2) | rounds × athletes in start order. Humans play live. CPU attempts: per round the **2 most relevant** (current leader, the rival, or whoever can overtake a human) play live as **highlights** at 1.5× game speed (✕ skips to the result); the rest are simulated instantly in a sandbox and appear on the standings board |\n| `program` | Figure Skating | like `attempts` with 1 attempt; CPU programs are simulated (score cards shown in the kiss & cry) |\n| `match` | Curling, Ice Hockey | the event runs its own match vs one CPU (or human) nation; the other placings come from `O.Sim.placings(eventId, nations)` (skill-weighted draws from a stream), so all 8 nations get a rank |\n\nTurn order: humans in join order, CPUs by ascending skill (best last, like a real final). Between rounds the standings\nboard shows the top 4 and every human.\n\n### 5.4 Input widgets (src/12-eventkit.js; each has `update`, `press`/`read` and a 10-foot `draw`)\n\n- **`Mash`** (`window: .5 s`): counts *alternations* (a press of the other button than the last one). `rate` = EMA of\n  alternations per second; a same-button press counts 0.25 and grows `same` (the streak resets on a true\n  alternation). Events map `rate` to power with `power = clamp((rate - G.mashRateMin) / (G.mashRateMax - G.mashRateMin), 0, 1) ** .75`\n  (defaults: `mashRateMin 2`, `mashRateMax 10.5` Hz). HUD: the two glyphs pulsing alternately + a 10-segment rate bar.\n- **`TimingBar`**: a needle sweeping a bar (ping-pong, `hz`), zones `[{ from, to, name, q }]`; `press()` → `{ q, zone }`.\n  Windows scale with difficulty and Timing assist.\n- **`Ring`**: a ring shrinking onto a target ring over `dur`; `press()` → signed error in ms → PERFECT ≤ 60 ms,\n  GOOD ≤ 140 ms (×window scale), else BAD.\n- **`Balance`**: a needle `b ∈ [-1, 1]` with drift `b'' = noise(t) * drift - b' * damp`, corrected by the stick axis\n  (`b' += -axis * k * dt`); out of `[-1, 1]` = lost. Noise from the event's stream (deterministic).\n- **`Sway`**: archery reticle: Lissajous + value noise, amplitude driven by the event (§6.5).\n- **`StrokeBeat`**: swimming: alternating expected buttons on a tempo that follows speed; judged like `Ring`.\n\n### 5.5 Hype and YIKES TURBO\n\n- Each athlete has `hype ∈ [0, 1]`, shown as a **flame meter** beside its name (fills orange → white-hot; full = the\n  turbo glyph flashes: \"△ TURBO!\"). Gains come from the event (perfect starts, perfect timing, clean gates, combos),\n  scaled by `G.hypeGain` (1.0); decay `G.hypeDecay` (0.02/s) when not full.\n- Pressing `turbo` with a full flame fires **YIKES TURBO** for `G.turboTime` (3 s): the event's own effect\n  (listed per event), the athlete bursts into (harmless, cartoon) flames (`particles.fire` at the feet/hands + glow\n  light), the music's `hype` layer fades in (`audio.layer('hype', 1, .3)`), the crowd surges, commentary cue\n  `turbo`. `G.turboPower` (1.0) scales every event's turbo multiplier.\n- CPU bots fire turbo at their event's best moment with probability = skill.\n\n### 5.6 CPU rivals and difficulty\n\n- Every nation's athlete has a skill per event (§7.1). Effective skill = `clamp(skill * G.cpuSkillScale + offset, .05, .99)`\n  with offset −0.12 / 0 / +0.06 for Easy / Normal / Hard (all three offsets are dev sliders).\n- Bots play **the same rules through intents** (no pre-rolled results): mash rate, reaction time, timing error,\n  aim error, steering noise, turbo use all derive from skill plus noise from the event's stream. This keeps balance\n  honest and lets tests measure it.\n- The rival (Turbonia's Max Overdrive; if a human picked Turbonia, the CPU nation with the highest average skill) gets\n  +0.03 and always plays live highlights.\n\n### 5.7 Results, qualifying, points, records, medals\n\n- **Ranking** by best performance (`better`), ties by the event's tie rule (stated per event), then by earlier\n  attempt. Nulls (DNF/foul/DQ) rank last in their order.\n- **Medals** to ranks 1–3 (match events: winner gold, loser silver, simulated bronze match).\n- **Qualifying (The Games, 1 player, Qualifying On):** a human result worse than `qualify[difficulty]` → \"YIKES! NO\n  QUALIFYING MARK\" → lose a torch (3 per Games) and retry the event (CPU results stand; the retry replaces yours).\n  0 torches → GAMES OVER → CONTINUE? (10 s countdown): yes restores 3 torches and retries; no → title (records and\n  laurels are kept). Match events have no qualifying check. Multi-human Games default Qualifying Off.\n- **Points** (≈ 0–1250, per event formula; a world-record performance is worth ≈ 1100–1250 in every event): party totals in Quick Games / multi-human Games and the hub score.\n- **Party points** (multi-human): 10 8 6 5 4 3 2 1 by rank among all 8; the overall champion is crowned at the end.\n- **Records:** in-world World Records (seed table in §7.5), Games Records (best ever on this device, `oly:records`),\n  Personal Bests per nation. A beaten WR → \"WORLD RECORD!\" banner, fireworks, WR sting, commentary, the jumbotron.\n  Top-5 tables per event with **initials** (`E.Arcade`: `cab.qualifies`, `cab.enter`, `cab.table`), skipped in hub.\n- **Medal table:** gold, then silver, then bronze, then nation name.\n\n### 5.8 Yikes moments\n\n`O.Yikes.trigger(a, kind, at)`: a giant comic stamp **\"OLYMPIYIKES!\"** (or the kind's own word: \"FALSE START!\",\n\"BELLY FLOP!\", \"BONK!\", \"FOUL!\") with shake, the descending-trombone sting, crowd gasp + \"OOOH\", a commentary cue,\n`yikes[nation]++` (shown at the closing ceremony as the \"Yikes reel\"), and **sympathy hype +0.15** (`G.yikesHype`), so\na comeback is always possible. Reduce-motion keeps the stamp still. Each event lists its yikes kinds; every one must\nbe reachable by ordinary bad play (tests force each).\n\n### 5.9 Ghosts\n\n`O.Ghost.rec(a)` samples `[t, x, y, z, facing, poseCode, extra]` at 20 Hz into a compact array; `O.Ghost.at(track, t)`\ninterpolates; `O.Ghost.draw(ctx, r, state, { tint, name })` draws a translucent rig (`r.actor(..., { alpha: .45 })`\ntinted with the player/seat color) plus a name tag. Uses: the leader's run in Downhill/Bobsled, the previous\nplayer's attempt in turn-based multiplayer, your best local run per event (stored, ≤ 3000 samples), and hub ghosts\n(§12.2) which arrive as the same samples over the network.\n\n### 5.10 Commentary\n\n- Two commentators plus the stadium PA (§7.6): **CHIP BELLOWS** (play-by-play, booming hyperbole), **DAME VERA\n  VELOCITY** (seven-time champion turned colour commentator, dry and sentimental), and the PA announcer (echo).\n- `O.Comms.cue(key, vars, { prio })`: picks a line from the event bank, falling back to the generic bank; never two\n  lines within 3.5 s, each key has a cooldown, higher priority interrupts (WR > yikes > photo finish > lead change >\n  filler). Lines may be two-speaker exchanges.\n- Display: a **lower third** with the speaker's live portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`), name, and up to 2 lines of\n  subtitles at scale 2 (Text size Huge = larger), above the prompt strip and clear of the touch area. Voice: `O.Voice`\n  gibberish (§9.3); the portrait's mouth moves while it speaks. Setting \"Commentary\" picks voices+subs / subs / off.\n- Vars: `{name}`, `{nation}`, `{time}`, `{dist}`, `{rival}`, `{place}`.\n\n### 5.11 Crowd, jumbotron, camera, slow-mo\n\n- **Stands** are TileMap tiers (or painted bands in side views) with a crowd painter: one `r.queue` per stand section\n  draws hundreds of 3×5 px spectators (head + shirt in nation colors), bobbing by `O.Crowd.level` (0..1), waving flags,\n  camera-flash glints, doing **the wave** when hype turbo fires or a record falls. The crowd audio follows the same\n  level.\n- **Jumbotron** (stadium, arena, pools): a dot-matrix panel (like the pinball kit's display) showing the event, the\n  clock, the leader, \"WORLD RECORD!\" and a live portrait of the leader.\n- **Camera:** `game.focus` on the human leader (or `cam.frame` on all humans, `zoom: [.6, 1]`) in races; event-\n  specific shots elsewhere. `ctx.slowmo(scale, seconds)` sets `game.timeScale` (photo finish .25, landings .35) and\n  restores it; reduce motion shortens it.\n\n### 5.12 Laurels\n","numLines":300,"startLine":300,"totalLines":1723}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01ULpKx46M2jo7YhcASfkW1Q","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi4bqnByJyuLK5xV8yCS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017ePRVWFJc1g5Bfuc9V1zV5","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-074118__x0e4b02/work/PLAN.md","offset":600,"limit":300},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10838,"cache_read_input_tokens":22643,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10838},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b1b95e-beb5-4384-ba72-665ccf7128b3","uuid":"607cd95d-98f7-47e3-8e7b-b639845d3560","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:41:31.687Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi4bqVaHhUf9bqcq8gxF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017ePRVWFJc1g5Bfuc9V1zV5":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-074118__x0e4b02/work/PLAN.md","offset":600,"limit":300}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017ePRVWFJc1g5Bfuc9V1zV5","type":"tool_result","content":"600\tOne per event (listed in §6), checked when an attempt ends; awarding shows a toast **\"LAUREL EARNED: ROCKET MAN\"**\n601\twith a golden laurel sprite, saved in `oly:laurels`, shown in Records → Laurels (12 tiles: earned gold / unearned\n602\toutline with its hint text).\n603\t\n604\t### 5.13 Tuning registry (the dev sliders' data)\n605\t\n606\t`O.tune.def(group, key, [default, min, max, step, label])`, `O.tune.get(group)` → live object (events read `ctx.T.key`\n607\tevery step, so a slider change applies immediately), `O.tune.reset(group?)`, `O.tune.changed()`,\n608\t`O.tune.json()`. Global group `G` (defaults): `cpuSkillScale 1`, `cpuOffsetEasy -.12`, `cpuOffsetNormal 0`,\n609\t`cpuOffsetHard .06`, `windowScale 1`, `hypeGain 1`, `hypeDecay .02`, `turboTime 3`, `turboPower 1`,\n610\t`mashRateMin 2`, `mashRateMax 10.5`, `mashHoldRate .72`, `yikesHype .15`, `slowmoScale .3`, `qualifyScale 1`,\n611\t`gameSpeed 1`. Every event defines **at least 6** of its own (listed per event).\n612\t\n613\t### 5.14 Saves\n614\t\n615\t`O.store` over `E.store`: records, laurels, cabinet (best medal per nation per event), the Games autosave (written\n616\tafter each day's medal table: meet minus runtime objects), best local ghost per event, first-time tips seen. Settings\n617\tare the engine's. Storage blocked → everything still works for the visit. In a hub session the client gives an empty\n618\tstorage (nothing to do).\n619\t\n620\t---\n621\t\n622\t## 6. The twelve events\n623\t\n624\tDay order in The Games alternates seasons: **1 100m Dash (S) · 2 Ski Jump (W) · 3 50m Freestyle (S) · 4 Curling (W) ·\n625\t5 Javelin (S) · 6 Downhill (W) · halftime · 7 Archery (S) · 8 Figure Skating (W) · 9 Weightlifting (S) ·\n626\t10 Bobsled (W) · 11 Diving (S) · 12 Ice Hockey Final (W)**.\n627\t\n628\tNumbers below are **starting values for tuning**, each one a dev slider where marked *(T)*. The *targets* are what\n629\ttests check (§16.3); retune freely as long as the targets hold.\n630\t\n631\t### 6.1 100m DASH — summer · Glory Stadium · mash\n632\t\n633\t- **View:** `'brawler'`, M = 12. Track along x: start line x = 0, finish x = 1200, run-out to 1500. 8 lanes at\n634\t  y = 20 + (lane−1)·14 (lane 1 nearest the camera). Stands (3 tiers + crowd) behind lane 8, advertising boards\n635\t  (cut low) in front of lane 1, the finish gantry with a clock, the jumbotron at the far end, the blimp above. Day,\n636\t  sunny; `lights` ambient .85 with sun-warm tint.\n637\t- **Format:** race, 8 athletes, 1 heat. Humans in lanes 4, 5, 3, 6; with one human, the rival takes lane 5 beside them.\n638\t- **Flow:** *intro* (camera pans lane 8 → 1 while the PA names each athlete and nation: 6 s, skippable) → \"ON YOUR\n639\t  MARKS\" (athletes crouch in the blocks) → \"SET\" (hips up; the gun comes after `1.0–2.2 s` from `rng('sprint:gun')`) →\n640\t  **BANG** (smoke puff, flash, sound) → race → photo finish → finish.\n641\t- **Reaction:** the first `mashL`/`mashR`/`action` press after the gun starts the athlete; reaction = press − gun.\n642\t  A press between SET and the gun, or a reaction < 0.100 s, is a **FALSE START**: everyone resets; the athlete gets a\n643\t  yellow card; a second one by the same athlete is a **DQ** (result null, note DQ).\n644\t- **Speed:** `vTarget = vMax · power(rate)` (§5.4); `v` approaches it at `accel` 9 m/s² *(T)* up and `decel` 5 m/s²\n645\t  *(T)* down; during the first 30 m accel is ×(0.6 + 0.4·d/30). `vMax` 11.6 m/s *(T)* (139 u/s). Turbo: `vMax` ×1.12\n646\t  *(T)*. Same-button streak 3 → **stumble** (v ×0.85 for 0.3 s); streak 5 → **FACEPLANT** (yikes: roll + down, 1.4 s\n647\t  on the ground, `faceplantTime` *(T)*).\n648\t- **Dip:** `action` within the last 2.5 m starts a lean; the torso (which is what crosses the line) leads by 0.35 m\n649\t  *(T)* if the dip lands in the last 1.2 m; earlier dips cost 10% speed for 0.3 s.\n650\t- **Finish:** time when the torso crosses x = 1200, to 0.001 (shown 0.01). Top two within 0.05 s → **PHOTO FINISH**:\n651\t  slow-mo .25 for 1 s, then a frozen sepia frame with the finish line and the two torsos, then the result.\n652\t- **Scoring:** lower time; ties by thousandths, then reaction. WR **9.48 s (MAX OVERDRIVE, TRB)**. Qualify Easy 12.30 /\n653\t  Normal 11.40 / Hard 10.60. Points `25.4347·(18 − t)^1.81`.\n654\t- **CPU:** rate `6.5 + 4.2·skill` Hz ± stream noise, reaction `0.24 − 0.11·skill ± .03`, false-start chance 2% (Normal),\n655\t  dip success = skill, turbo at 50 m.\n656\t- **Hype:** reaction < 0.15 s +0.35; each second at > 85% power +0.08; good dip +0.1.\n657\t- **Tunables:** vMax, accel, decel, turboMult, dipLead, faceplantTime, stumbleStreak, falseStartMin (0.100).\n658\t- **Yikes:** FALSE START!, FACEPLANT. **Laurel:** ROCKET MAN (reaction ≤ 0.120 s and win).\n659\t- **HUD:** per human: lane tag, mash-pair prompt pulsing, power bar, hype flame; top-right race clock; split board at\n660\t  50 m (times) on the jumbotron; reaction times shown under each lane after the start.\n661\t- **Targets (tests):** perfect bot 9.40–9.70 s (with turbo ≤ 9.55); skill .9 bot ≈ 9.8–10.2; skill .5 ≈ 10.8–11.4;\n662\t  idle human = DNF after 30 s; a press before the gun = false start; skill .9 beats .3 in ≥ 95% of 40 seeds.\n663\t- **Multiplayer:** up to 4 humans live; **hub:** yes (1 heat, ghosts in lanes).\n664\t\n665\t### 6.2 JAVELIN THROW — summer · Glory Stadium infield · mash + angle\n666\t\n667\t- **View:** `'brawler'`, M = 12. Runway x 0 → 360 (30 m), foul line (white arc) at x = 360, landing sector to\n668\t  x = 360 + 1440 (120 m) with lines every 10 m and numbers, the stadium wall at 120 m and a parking lot beyond it.\n669\t  Windsock, distance board, judges with flags. The blimp crosses above (see Over the top).\n670\t- **Format:** attempts × 3 rounds, best counts; ties by second-best.\n671\t- **Flow per attempt:** athlete at x = 0 with the javelin over the shoulder (pose `javCarry`) → run-up (mash, `vMax`\n672\t  9.0 m/s *(T)*) → **hold `action`**: the angle needle rises 0 → 80° at 55°/s *(T)* (and back down if held on,\n673\t  ping-pong) → **release** throws at the current angle → flight → landing → a judge jogs to the mark with a tape\n674\t  (1.2 s) → the distance pops up.\n675\t- **Foul:** crossing x = 360 before release → FOUL (the athlete trips over the line and rolls: yikes), red flag, no mark.\n676\t- **Physics (meters):** release speed `vRel = 13 + 1.9·vRun` m/s *(T coefficients)* at the chosen angle, from 2.0 m up;\n677\t  `a = (0, −9.81) − kD·|v_air|·v_air` with `v_air = v − (wind, 0)`, `kD = 0.0011` *(T)*. Wind per throw from\n678\t  `rng('javelin:wind:<round>:<athlete>')` in −2.0…+3.0 m/s *(T range)*. Tip-first landing requires release angle in\n679\t  20°–60°; outside → **FLAT!** (the javelin bounces, \"BOING\", no mark).\n680\t- **Camera:** follow the athlete; at release `cam.frame([javelin, predictedLanding], { zoom: [.5, 1] })`; slow-mo .35\n681\t  for the last 0.6 s; then a close shot of the javelin quivering in the turf.\n682\t- **Scoring:** higher distance (0.01 m). WR **101.20 m (BLAZE CINDERHART, VOL)**. Qualify 58 / 72 / 82 m. Points\n683\t  `10.14·(d − 7)^1.05` (WR ≈ 1200).\n684\t- **CPU:** run rate by skill; release angle ~ N(38°, 7° − 5°·skill); foul chance (1 − skill)·12%; turbo on the run.\n685\t- **Turbo:** HYPER ARM: release speed ×1.12 *(T)* and the javelin trails fire.\n686\t- **Over the top:** > 120 m → OUT OF THE STADIUM: the javelin clears the wall, a car alarm whoops, the mark is\n687\t  measured at the landing point in the parking lot (counts!). The blimp (at 55–70 m altitude, crossing at a random\n688\t  x per round) can be popped by a steep, fast throw: confetti, \"BLIMP BUSTER!\", the javelin drops and its landing\n689\t  counts.\n690\t- **Tunables:** vMaxRun, angleRate, vRelBase, vRelPerRun, drag, windMax, turboMult.\n691\t- **Yikes:** FOUL!, FLAT!. **Laurel:** OUT OF THE STADIUM (> 120 m).\n692\t- **HUD:** angle gauge (a big quarter-circle dial with a green band 34°–42°), wind (arrow + m/s), run power, best mark,\n693\t  standings strip.\n694\t- **Targets:** perfect bot (38°, full run) 88–93 m; perfect + turbo + 3 m/s tailwind > 120 m possible; skill .5 ≈ 65–75 m;\n695\t  release at 10° → flat; crossing the line → foul.\n696\t- **Multiplayer:** humans alternate (the previous thrower's javelin flight shows as a ghost); **hub:** yes (2 throws).\n697\t\n698\t### 6.3 50m FREESTYLE (short course) — summer · Splash Palace · rhythm + breath\n699\t\n700\t- **View:** `'brawler'`, M = 12. A 25 m pool (x 0 → 300) with 8 lanes 2.5 m wide (30 u), animated water floor\n701\t  (`E.tex.water` + caustics), lane ropes as rows of colored floats, backstroke flags, starting blocks, a deck, stands\n702\t  and big windows to the beach; indoor bright light. 2 lengths with a turn at x = 300.\n703\t- **Flow:** \"TAKE YOUR MARKS\" → beep after `0.8–1.6 s` → **start** (reaction as in the sprint; early = false start) →\n704\t  **dive:** holding `action` 0.2–0.6 s then releasing gives the best glide (4 + 3·q m); holding past 0.75 s →\n705\t  **BELLY FLOP START** (yikes, glide 2 m) → strokes → **turn** → strokes → **touch**.\n706\t- **Strokes (`StrokeBeat`):** expected buttons alternate `mashL`, `mashR` on a beat whose tempo follows speed\n707\t  (`50 + 50·v/vMax` strokes/min). A press within ±70 ms *(T)* of the beat is PERFECT, ±150 ms GOOD, else MISS (wasted,\n708\t  splash, −5% speed); the wrong button is a MISS. Quality `q` = EMA (1.5 s) of 1 / .6 / 0;\n709\t  `vTarget = vMax·(0.45 + 0.55·q)`, `vMax` 2.45 m/s *(T)*.\n710\t- **Breathing:** O2 drains 0.11/s *(T)*; `alt` within 0.25 s after a stroke breathes (+0.45 O2, that stroke ×0.7).\n711\t  O2 < .25 caps strokes at GOOD; O2 = 0 → **GASP!** (yikes: 1.2 s stop, cough, O2 back to .6).\n712\t- **Turn:** inside 1.6 m of the wall the prompt \"✕ TURN\" appears: press at 0.6–1.1 m → PERFECT FLIP TURN (push-off at\n713\t  1.25·vMax, hype +0.2); 1.1–1.6 m early (weak push); < 0.6 m late (normal); not pressed by the wall → **BONK!**\n714\t  (yikes, +1.0 s).\n715\t- **Touch:** `action` within the last 0.8 m reaches (−0.05 s); otherwise an automatic glide-in.\n716\t- **Scoring:** lower time. WR **19.62 s (MARINA SPLASHWORTH, WAV)**. Qualify 25.5 / 23.2 / 21.6. Points\n717\t  `18.9·(35 − t)^1.5`.\n718\t- **CPU:** P(perfect) = .35 + .55·skill, P(good) the rest minus a miss rate (1 − skill)·.15; breathes every 3–4\n719\t  strokes; turn quality by skill.\n720\t- **Turbo:** DOLPHIN MODE: 3 s of automatic PERFECT strokes, vMax ×1.1, a cartoon dolphin leaps in the next lane.\n721\t- **Tunables:** vMax, perfectWindow, goodWindow, o2Drain, breathGain, turnPush, diveGlide.\n722\t- **Yikes:** FALSE START!, BELLY FLOP START, GASP!, BONK!. **Laurel:** TORPEDO (reaction < 0.15, perfect dive and\n723\t  perfect turn in one race).\n724\t- **HUD:** per human: the stroke ring with the next expected glyph, O2 bubble meter, hype flame; lap/turn indicator.\n725\t- **Targets:** perfect bot 19.4–19.9 s; skill .5 ≈ 22.5–24; never breathing → at least one GASP; missing the turn →\n726\t  BONK.\n727\t- **Multiplayer:** up to 4 live; **hub:** yes.\n728\t\n729\t### 6.4 10m PLATFORM DIVING — summer · Splash Palace · tricks + entry timing\n730\t\n731\t- **View:** `'side'`, M = 12. Tower at the left (platforms at 1, 3, 5, 7.5, 10 m; the 10 m edge at x = 30, z = 120),\n732\t  pool cross-section below (surface z = 0, depth to z = −60 drawn translucent with light shafts and bubbles), the 5\n733\t  judges' table, the scoreboard, stands. Camera frames the diver and the water; slow-mo .35 at entry.\n734\t- **Format:** 3 rounds; each round the diver picks 1 of 3 dives (one easy, one medium, one hard, never repeating a\n735\t  dive). Total = sum of dive scores.\n736\t- **Dive list:** Forward 2½ Pike (105B, DD 2.8, 5 half-somersaults, pike); Back 2½ Tuck (205C, DD 3.0, 5, tuck, back\n737\t  take-off); Forward 3½ Tuck (107C, DD 3.3, 7, tuck); Inward 3½ Tuck (407C, DD 3.2, 7, tuck); Forward 2½ with 2 Twists\n738\t  Pike (5154B, DD 3.6, 5 half-somersaults + 4 half-twists); **YIKES! Armstand Quintuple** (DD 4.8, 10, tuck: the\n739\t  over-the-top dive).\n740\t- **Take-off:** `TimingBar` (1.4 Hz): `vz = 4.2 + 1.6·q` m/s up, `vx = 1.0` m/s; airtime ≈ 1.9–2.1 s.\n741\t- **In the air:** hold `mashL` = TUCK (ω 12.5 rad/s *(T)*), hold `mashR` = PIKE (ω 9 rad/s *(T)*), neither = OPEN\n742\t  (1.5 rad/s *(T)*). A dial shows half-somersaults done vs required. Twist dives: each tap ←/→ while open or piked\n743\t  adds a half twist (0.25 s each). The body rotation is drawn with the Pose module's `bodyPitch` (+ yaw for twists).\n744\t- **Entry judgement:** at the surface, error `e` = |body angle − vertical (head first)| in degrees: ≤ 8 RIP (no\n745\t  splash) base 9.5; ≤ 15 → 8.5; ≤ 25 → 7.0; ≤ 45 → 5.0; ≤ 75 → 3.0; > 75 → **BELLY FLOP / BACK SLAP** (yikes) 1.0.\n746\t  Adjust: take-off +0…+0.5; wrong position −1.0; each missing/extra half-somersault −2.0; each missing half-twist −1.5;\n747\t  judge noise ±0.5 per judge from `rng('judges:...')`; clamp 0–10, round to 0.5. 5 judges, drop high and low,\n748\t  dive score = middle three × DD.\n749\t- **Scoring:** higher total. WR **338.40 (COCO BONBON, BON)** (the maximum possible is 351: three perfect dives of DD 4.8, 3.6, 3.3). Qualify 150 / 195 / 240. Points `3.4·total`.\n750\t- **CPU:** take-off q ~ skill; release error σ = (1 − skill)·35°; picks hard dives when skill > .8.\n751\t- **Turbo:** SLOW-MO SUPREMACY: time ×0.5 for 2.5 s of the dive (more control), sparkle trail.\n752\t- **Tunables:** tuckSpin, pikeSpin, openSpin, takeoffVz, ripTolerance, judgeNoise, twistTime.\n753\t- **Yikes:** BELLY FLOP (the judges hold up 0.5 cards; the splash soaks them), WRONG WAY (back slap). **Laurel:**\n754\t  PERFECT 10s (all five judges 10).\n755\t- **HUD:** dive name + DD, rotation dial, position prompt (glyph □ TUCK / ○ PIKE), twist counter, judges' cards on\n756\t  entry.\n757\t- **Targets:** perfect bot on the 4.8 dive → five 10s (score ≥ 140); skill .5 average ≈ 60–70 per dive; holding tuck\n758\t  to the water from a 2½ → over-rotation penalty or belly flop.\n759\t- **Multiplayer:** alternate; **hub:** yes (2 dives, the options dealt from `AIHub.rng`).\n760\t\n761\t### 6.5 ARCHERY — summer · Bullseye Lawn (seaside) · aim under sway\n762\t\n763\t- **View:** main = the **target close-up** (a 122 cm face, 10 rings + X, drawn ~200 px across: readable at 10 feet);\n764\t  inset (bottom-left, ~30% height) = the archer in `'side'` view at the line drawing the bow, palm trees and the sea\n765\t  behind, wind flags. During flight the inset shows the arrow leaving; the target view zooms 1.1× toward the impact.\n766\t- **Format:** attempts: 6 arrows in 2 ends of 3 (a 20 s shot clock per arrow; 12 s in hub heats). Score 0–60; ties by X count, then 10s.\n767\t- **Draw:** hold `action` 0.9 s *(T)* to full draw (string tension bar). Release before full draw → weak arrow\n768\t  (25 cm low + spread).\n769\t- **Aim:** stick/WASD moves the aim at 40 cm/s *(T)*; mouse: the pointer sets the aim directly. **Sway** adds\n770\t  `A·(sin 1.3t·cos 0.7t, sin(1.7t + 1))` + value noise, `A = A0·(1 + 0.6·max(0, held − 2.5 s))·hr`, `A0` 7 cm *(T)*,\n771\t  heart rate `hr` 1.0 → 1.6 (rises after a bad arrow and on the final arrow of the match).\n772\t- **Hold breath:** hold `alt` (L, R2 or right mouse) at full draw: sway ×0.25 for up to 2.5 s *(T)*; when the breath\n773\t  bar empties, sway ×2 for 2 s (gasping).\n774\t- **Wind:** per arrow from `rng('archery:wind:<n>')` in −4…+4 m/s; impact shift 4.5 cm per m/s *(T)* sideways. Shown\n775\t  as a flag, an arrow and a number. Aim off to compensate.\n776\t- **Release:** let go of `action` at full draw → flight 0.75 s → impact = aim + sway at release + wind shift + release\n777\t  jitter (more if the aim was moving) → ring score; X ring → \"BULLSEYE!\". An impact within 1.0 cm of an earlier arrow\n778\t  → **ROBIN HOOD** (the old arrow splits; same score).\n779\t- **Scoring:** WR **60 (6 X) — PIXEL VANCE (NEO)**. Qualify 40 / 48 / 53. Points `20·score`.\n780\t- **CPU:** aim error σ = (1 − skill)·12 + 2 cm, wind compensation accuracy = skill; CPU arrows show on a mini target\n781\t  on the standings board.\n782\t- **Turbo:** EAGLE EYE: game time ×0.4 and sway ×0.1 for 3 s of real time.\n783\t- **Tunables:** drawTime, swayA0, swayGrowth, breathTime, windMax, windShift.\n784\t- **Yikes:** STRING SLAP (releasing while gasping: \"OW!\", the arrow flies wide). **Laurel:** ROBIN HOOD.\n785\t- **Targets:** perfect bot = 60; a no-breath, no-wind-compensation bot at 4 m/s wind averages < 8 per arrow.\n786\t- **Multiplayer:** alternate per arrow; **hub:** yes (3 arrows, 12 s shot clock).\n787\t\n788\t### 6.6 WEIGHTLIFTING (clean & jerk) — summer · Iron Hall · mash + balance + timing\n789\t\n790\t- **View:** `'brawler'`; the lifter (bulky build, singlet, belt, chalked hands) faces the camera on a wooden platform;\n791\t  spotlights in a dark hall (`lights` ambient .35 + two warm spots); 3 referees with white/red lights; the bar bends\n792\t  with load; plates colored by mass (25 red, 20 blue, 15 yellow, 10 green, 5 white, 2.5 black, collars). Chalk dust.\n793\t- **Format:** attempts × 3. Pick the opening weight from 5 offered (Normal 200/210/220/230/240 kg), then +5 / +10 / +15\n794\t  for the next; the third attempt may take the **YIKES BAR** (WR + 10 kg). Best good lift counts; ties go to whoever made\n795\t  that weight first.\n796\t- **Load factor** `w = (kg − 150)/120`.\n797\t- **CLEAN (4.0 s *(T)*):** bar height `h` 0 → 1 (floor → shoulders): `h += (rate − 0.7·rReq)·0.12·dt` *(T)*,\n798\t  `rReq = 5.5 + 4.5·w` Hz; the bar sinks if rate < 0.5·rReq; time out → no lift.\n799\t- **RACK:** `Balance` (drift ×(1 + w)); keep |b| < .35 for 1.2 s *(T)*; |b| > 1 → drop.\n800\t- **JERK:** `Ring` (0.9 s): PERFECT → overhead wobble ×0.5; GOOD ×1; BAD → 50% fail, else wobble ×1.8.\n801\t- **HOLD:** `Balance` overhead for 2.0 s *(T)*, drift grows with w → three white lights \"GOOD LIFT!\" (a WR cracks the\n802\t  floor), else the bar drops.\n803\t- **Scoring:** WR **270 kg (BLAZE CINDERHART, VOL)**. Qualify 200 / 225 / 245 kg. Points `min(1200, 9.5·(kg − 150))`.\n804\t- **CPU:** success probability `1/(1 + e^((kg − (190 + 80·skill))/6))`; picks weights like a cautious coach.\n805\t- **Turbo:** IRON WILL: balance drift ×0.2 and lift power ×1.4 for 3 s.\n806\t- **Tunables:** cleanTime, liftGain, rReqBase, rReqPerW, rackTime, holdTime, driftBase.\n807\t- **Yikes:** DROP (the bar bounces twice and the lifter sits down hard, \"OOF\"). **Laurel:** YIKES WEIGHT (lift the\n808\t  YIKES BAR).\n809\t- **HUD:** big kg number, phase name, the mash pair, the balance needle (huge, center-bottom), the jerk ring, the 3\n810\t  lights.\n811\t- **Targets:** perfect bot lifts 280; skill .5 tops out ≈ 220–230; idle → no lift; |b| > 1 → drop.\n812\t- **Multiplayer:** alternate attempts; **hub:** yes (2 attempts: 220 then 240 kg).\n813\t\n814\t### 6.7 SKI JUMP (large hill, K-125, HS-140) — winter · Mount Glory Jumping Hill · timing + flight balance\n815\t\n816\t- **View:** `'side'`, **M = 8** (the hill is big). Night, floodlights (`lights.add` along the in-run and the landing\n817\t  hill), light snow (`game.weather = { kind: 'snow', amount: .3 }`), alpine backdrop (custom `E.Backdrop` layers:\n818\t  mountains, pine forest, a starry sky), the jump tower, the K-point and HS lines, distance boards every 10 m,\n819\t  cowbell crowd and flags in the out-run.\n820\t- **Hill profile (meters, origin at the take-off edge):** in-run 95 m at 35° from the start gate, table −11°; landing\n821\t  hill: knoll `z = −3·(x/15)²` for x < 15, then a 30° slope `z = −3 − 0.58·(x − 15)` to x = 125, then easing out with\n822\t  `+0.0045·(x − 125)²` into the flat out-run. Distance is measured along the slope from the edge (precompute a\n823\t  polyline with arc lengths).\n824\t- **Format:** attempts × 2 jumps. Score per jump = distance points + style points.\n825\t- **Flow:** start gate (`action` pushes off) → **in-run:** a `Balance` needle on ↑/↓ (keep the tuck): speed ×(0.94…1.0)\n826\t  by average balance quality; `a = g·sin35° − μ·g·cos35° − kAir·v²` (μ .02, kAir .0016 *(T)*) → ≈ 25.5 m/s at the\n827\t  table with a perfect tuck. → **take-off:** press `action` in the last 4 m before the edge: last 1.0 m q = 1, 1–2.5 m\n828\t  .7, 2.5–4 m .4; no press → **FELL OFF THE TABLE** (q .1, yikes hop). Adds `vz += 2.4·q` m/s. → **flight:** body\n829\t  angle α (to the airflow) changed by ↑/↓ at 40°/s; gusts from `rng('skijump:gust')` push α; lift `aL = cL(α)·v²`\n830\t  (⊥ velocity), drag `aD = cD(α)·v²`, with `cL(α) = cL0·max(.1, 1 − ((α − 12)/30)²)`, `cL0` .00095 *(T)*,\n831\t  `cD(α) = .0006 + .00002·α` *(T)*. → **landing:** within 2.5 m above the slope the prompt \"✕ TELEMARK!\" appears;\n832\t  press within 0.35 s before contact → telemark; later/none → two-footed; landing with |α| > 40° *(T)*, or beyond\n833\t  HS + 10 m without a telemark → **CRASH** (tumble down the out-run: Pose tumble, skis fly as sprites, snow spray).\n834\t- **Scoring:** distance points `60 + (d − 125)·1.8`; style: 5 judges, telemark 17.5–19.5, two-footed 15–17, crash 6–9\n835\t  (minus wobble in flight), drop high/low, sum 3 (max 60). Event = 2 jumps. Hill record **148.0 m (INGRID\n836\t  SNOWCASTLE, FRM)**, event WR **296.4**. Qualify 160 / 210 / 245 (2-jump total). Points `3.9·total`.\n837\t- **CPU:** balance and take-off q by skill, flight α error (1 − skill)·15°, telemark chance = skill.\n838\t- **Turbo:** ROCKET SKIS: lift ×1.1 and +3 m/s² thrust for 2 s, flames from the ski tails.\n839\t- **Tunables:** kAir, takeoffBoost, cL0, cDBase, gust, telemarkWindow, crashAngle.\n840\t- **Yikes:** FELL OFF THE TABLE, CRASH. **Laurel:** OFF THE CHART (land > 150 m without crashing).\n841\t- **HUD:** speed (km/h) in the in-run, take-off zone bar, the flight angle gauge (a skier silhouette rotating over a\n842\t  green band), distance counter following the jumper, telemark prompt, judges' style cards.\n843\t- **Targets:** perfect bot 132–140 m; perfect + turbo ≥ 150 m; skill .5 ≈ 112–122 m; no take-off press → < 80 m.\n844\t- **Multiplayer:** alternate jumps; **hub:** yes (1 jump).\n845\t\n846\t### 6.8 DOWNHILL — winter · \"The Yikes Face\" · steering + tuck + gates\n847\t\n848\t- **View:** pseudo-3D `E.Road` (`segment: 200`, 1 m = 100 road units; `width: 1600`, `lanes: 0`, `draw: 220`), the\n849\t  skier drawn from behind at the bottom center through a custom rear view (§8.2: `new E.View('rear', 'Rear', 0, 18,\n850\t  1.6, 1)`, rig facing +y, skis and poles projected with the view's `ax ay bx by bz`), snow colors (road\n851\t  `#f4f8ff/#e8f0fb`, grass `#dfe9f6/#d3e0f0` deep snow, rumble = orange netting `#ff7a2a/#f05a1a`), pines,\n852\t  spectators with flags and cowbells, banners, start hut, ice tunnel (`tunnel: true`, blue-white walls), sun glare\n853\t  (an additive flare overlay), light snow.\n854\t- **Course (≈1,440 m, 24 gates):**\n855\t\n856\t| # | Section | Length | Slope | Curves | Gates | Feature |\n857\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n858\t| 1 | Start Schuss | 150 m | 28° | 0 | 1 | start hut, crowd |\n859\t| 2 | The Corkscrew | 220 m | 22° | +4, −4, +3 | 5 | S-bends |\n860\t| 3 | Kangaroo Kicker | 60 m | 10° → 32° | 0 | 1 | crest jump |\n861\t| 4 | Pine Alley | 200 m | 20° | −2 | 3 | fences at x = ±1.05 (narrow) |\n862\t| 5 | Ice Tunnel | 120 m | 18° | +2 | 1 | tunnel, grip ×0.6 |\n863\t| 6 | The Yikes Face | 180 m | 38° | 0 | 3 | big crest jump at its top |\n864\t| 7 | Glory Bend | 260 m | 18° | +5 (long) | 4 | strong outward push |\n865\t| 8 | Finish Schuss | 250 m | 15° | ±1 | 6 | Victory Hop jump, finish arch, grandstand |\n866\t\n867\t  Build: for each section `road.add(len/2, { curve, hill: -len·tan(slope)·100 })` (in road units) and keep a parallel\n868\t  meter-based table for physics (slope per segment, features, gate list `{ s, xc }`).\n869\t- **Physics:** speed `v` along the course: `a = g·sin(slope) − (tuck ? dTuck : dUp)·v² − μ·g − carve·|steer|·v`\n870\t  (dTuck .0028, dUp .0062, μ .03, carve .18 — all *(T)*). Lateral `x` (half-roads, piste |x| ≤ 1): `x' = steer·turn(v) −\n871\t  push·curveAt(z)·v²·k`; `turn` ×0.55 while tucking. 1 < |x| < 1.25 deep snow (drag ×3); |x| ≥ 1.25 → **CRASH into the\n872\t  netting** (yikes tumble 2.0 s, respawn |x| = 1, v = 10 m/s). **Jumps:** when the slope falls away faster than a\n873\t  ballistic arc, the skier is airborne (`h'' = −g`, shadow on the snow); `action` 0.2–0.5 s before a crest = PRE-JUMP\n874\t  (half the airtime: faster). Landing with |steer| > .6 or |x| > 1 → crash. **Gates:** passing |x − xc| ≤ .32 → +2%\n875\t  speed (whoosh) and hype +0.05; missing → +0.50 s penalty (red \"+0.50\").\n876\t- **Splits:** 3 checkpoints vs the current leader (green −, red +). The leader's run is a ghost skier.\n877\t- **Scoring:** lower time incl. penalties. Course record **47.62 s (ROCKY SUMMIT, MTP)**. Qualify 58.0 / 52.5 / 49.0.\n878\t  Points `8.5·(80 − t)^1.4`.\n879\t- **CPU:** simulated runs with steering toward the next gate center, tuck on straights, noise and crash chance\n880\t  (1 − skill)·15% at the Yikes Face; the top CPU run becomes the ghost.\n881\t- **Turbo:** AVALANCHE: speed ×1.18 for 3 s with a cartoon avalanche cloud chasing behind.\n882\t- **Tunables:** dTuck, dUp, turnRate, curvePush, gateBoost, missPenalty, crashSteer.\n883\t- **Yikes:** CRASH (netting), CRASH (landing). **Laurel:** CLEAN SWEEP (all 24 gates).\n884\t- **HUD:** time, speed (km/h), split popups, gate counter (n/24), a course strip (progress line with the leader's\n885\t  dot), tuck indicator, hype flame.\n886\t- **Targets:** perfect bot 46.5–48.5 s; skill .5 ≈ 53–56 s; steering hard into the netting → crash; all gates\n887\t  possible.\n888\t- **Multiplayer:** humans take turns, each seeing the best run so far as a ghost; **hub:** yes (1 run; other\n889\t  players' skiers as ghosts drawn as road \"cars\").\n890\t\n891\t### 6.9 TWO-MAN BOBSLED — winter · Glory Ice Track (dusk) · push + load + banked steering\n892\t\n893\t- **View:** `E.Road` again (1 m = 100 units, `width` ≈ 400: a narrow channel; tune for the look), the track as an ice channel: road = ice (`#d8eef8/#cfe6f2`),\n894\t  rumble = blue-white walls, grass = snow banks, tunnel roofs on covered sections, dusk sky with floodlights placed as\n895\t  glowing scenery, timing boards. The sled (drawn with `px.poly` boxes through the rear view, in the nation's colors,\n896\t  number on the cowl) with two rigs seated (Pose `bobPilot`, `bobBrake`), tilted by its wall height.\n897\t- **Track (≈1,300 m, 15 named curves):** Sunny Start, Glory Kink, The Twins (2), Shark Fin, Kreisel (long +6),\n898\t  Labyrinth (3, S-S-S), Omega (+6/−6), The Washing Machine, Double Trouble (2), Last Gasp, Finish Curve.\n899\t- **Flow:** **push** (first 50 m): mash; `dv/dt = 6·power·(1 − v/11)` m/s² *(T)*; the start time at 50 m is shown"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b1b95e-beb5-4384-ba72-665ccf7128b3","uuid":"0727aeae-d9ad-4d1b-96fd-f918435efe44","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:41:31.855Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-074118__x0e4b02/work/PLAN.md","content":"One per event (listed in §6), checked when an attempt ends; awarding shows a toast **\"LAUREL EARNED: ROCKET MAN\"**\nwith a golden laurel sprite, saved in `oly:laurels`, shown in Records → Laurels (12 tiles: earned gold / unearned\noutline with its hint text).\n\n### 5.13 Tuning registry (the dev sliders' data)\n\n`O.tune.def(group, key, [default, min, max, step, label])`, `O.tune.get(group)` → live object (events read `ctx.T.key`\nevery step, so a slider change applies immediately), `O.tune.reset(group?)`, `O.tune.changed()`,\n`O.tune.json()`. Global group `G` (defaults): `cpuSkillScale 1`, `cpuOffsetEasy -.12`, `cpuOffsetNormal 0`,\n`cpuOffsetHard .06`, `windowScale 1`, `hypeGain 1`, `hypeDecay .02`, `turboTime 3`, `turboPower 1`,\n`mashRateMin 2`, `mashRateMax 10.5`, `mashHoldRate .72`, `yikesHype .15`, `slowmoScale .3`, `qualifyScale 1`,\n`gameSpeed 1`. Every event defines **at least 6** of its own (listed per event).\n\n### 5.14 Saves\n\n`O.store` over `E.store`: records, laurels, cabinet (best medal per nation per event), the Games autosave (written\nafter each day's medal table: meet minus runtime objects), best local ghost per event, first-time tips seen. Settings\nare the engine's. Storage blocked → everything still works for the visit. In a hub session the client gives an empty\nstorage (nothing to do).\n\n---\n\n## 6. The twelve events\n\nDay order in The Games alternates seasons: **1 100m Dash (S) · 2 Ski Jump (W) · 3 50m Freestyle (S) · 4 Curling (W) ·\n5 Javelin (S) · 6 Downhill (W) · halftime · 7 Archery (S) · 8 Figure Skating (W) · 9 Weightlifting (S) ·\n10 Bobsled (W) · 11 Diving (S) · 12 Ice Hockey Final (W)**.\n\nNumbers below are **starting values for tuning**, each one a dev slider where marked *(T)*. The *targets* are what\ntests check (§16.3); retune freely as long as the targets hold.\n\n### 6.1 100m DASH — summer · Glory Stadium · mash\n\n- **View:** `'brawler'`, M = 12. Track along x: start line x = 0, finish x = 1200, run-out to 1500. 8 lanes at\n  y = 20 + (lane−1)·14 (lane 1 nearest the camera). Stands (3 tiers + crowd) behind lane 8, advertising boards\n  (cut low) in front of lane 1, the finish gantry with a clock, the jumbotron at the far end, the blimp above. Day,\n  sunny; `lights` ambient .85 with sun-warm tint.\n- **Format:** race, 8 athletes, 1 heat. Humans in lanes 4, 5, 3, 6; with one human, the rival takes lane 5 beside them.\n- **Flow:** *intro* (camera pans lane 8 → 1 while the PA names each athlete and nation: 6 s, skippable) → \"ON YOUR\n  MARKS\" (athletes crouch in the blocks) → \"SET\" (hips up; the gun comes after `1.0–2.2 s` from `rng('sprint:gun')`) →\n  **BANG** (smoke puff, flash, sound) → race → photo finish → finish.\n- **Reaction:** the first `mashL`/`mashR`/`action` press after the gun starts the athlete; reaction = press − gun.\n  A press between SET and the gun, or a reaction < 0.100 s, is a **FALSE START**: everyone resets; the athlete gets a\n  yellow card; a second one by the same athlete is a **DQ** (result null, note DQ).\n- **Speed:** `vTarget = vMax · power(rate)` (§5.4); `v` approaches it at `accel` 9 m/s² *(T)* up and `decel` 5 m/s²\n  *(T)* down; during the first 30 m accel is ×(0.6 + 0.4·d/30). `vMax` 11.6 m/s *(T)* (139 u/s). Turbo: `vMax` ×1.12\n  *(T)*. Same-button streak 3 → **stumble** (v ×0.85 for 0.3 s); streak 5 → **FACEPLANT** (yikes: roll + down, 1.4 s\n  on the ground, `faceplantTime` *(T)*).\n- **Dip:** `action` within the last 2.5 m starts a lean; the torso (which is what crosses the line) leads by 0.35 m\n  *(T)* if the dip lands in the last 1.2 m; earlier dips cost 10% speed for 0.3 s.\n- **Finish:** time when the torso crosses x = 1200, to 0.001 (shown 0.01). Top two within 0.05 s → **PHOTO FINISH**:\n  slow-mo .25 for 1 s, then a frozen sepia frame with the finish line and the two torsos, then the result.\n- **Scoring:** lower time; ties by thousandths, then reaction. WR **9.48 s (MAX OVERDRIVE, TRB)**. Qualify Easy 12.30 /\n  Normal 11.40 / Hard 10.60. Points `25.4347·(18 − t)^1.81`.\n- **CPU:** rate `6.5 + 4.2·skill` Hz ± stream noise, reaction `0.24 − 0.11·skill ± .03`, false-start chance 2% (Normal),\n  dip success = skill, turbo at 50 m.\n- **Hype:** reaction < 0.15 s +0.35; each second at > 85% power +0.08; good dip +0.1.\n- **Tunables:** vMax, accel, decel, turboMult, dipLead, faceplantTime, stumbleStreak, falseStartMin (0.100).\n- **Yikes:** FALSE START!, FACEPLANT. **Laurel:** ROCKET MAN (reaction ≤ 0.120 s and win).\n- **HUD:** per human: lane tag, mash-pair prompt pulsing, power bar, hype flame; top-right race clock; split board at\n  50 m (times) on the jumbotron; reaction times shown under each lane after the start.\n- **Targets (tests):** perfect bot 9.40–9.70 s (with turbo ≤ 9.55); skill .9 bot ≈ 9.8–10.2; skill .5 ≈ 10.8–11.4;\n  idle human = DNF after 30 s; a press before the gun = false start; skill .9 beats .3 in ≥ 95% of 40 seeds.\n- **Multiplayer:** up to 4 humans live; **hub:** yes (1 heat, ghosts in lanes).\n\n### 6.2 JAVELIN THROW — summer · Glory Stadium infield · mash + angle\n\n- **View:** `'brawler'`, M = 12. Runway x 0 → 360 (30 m), foul line (white arc) at x = 360, landing sector to\n  x = 360 + 1440 (120 m) with lines every 10 m and numbers, the stadium wall at 120 m and a parking lot beyond it.\n  Windsock, distance board, judges with flags. The blimp crosses above (see Over the top).\n- **Format:** attempts × 3 rounds, best counts; ties by second-best.\n- **Flow per attempt:** athlete at x = 0 with the javelin over the shoulder (pose `javCarry`) → run-up (mash, `vMax`\n  9.0 m/s *(T)*) → **hold `action`**: the angle needle rises 0 → 80° at 55°/s *(T)* (and back down if held on,\n  ping-pong) → **release** throws at the current angle → flight → landing → a judge jogs to the mark with a tape\n  (1.2 s) → the distance pops up.\n- **Foul:** crossing x = 360 before release → FOUL (the athlete trips over the line and rolls: yikes), red flag, no mark.\n- **Physics (meters):** release speed `vRel = 13 + 1.9·vRun` m/s *(T coefficients)* at the chosen angle, from 2.0 m up;\n  `a = (0, −9.81) − kD·|v_air|·v_air` with `v_air = v − (wind, 0)`, `kD = 0.0011` *(T)*. Wind per throw from\n  `rng('javelin:wind:<round>:<athlete>')` in −2.0…+3.0 m/s *(T range)*. Tip-first landing requires release angle in\n  20°–60°; outside → **FLAT!** (the javelin bounces, \"BOING\", no mark).\n- **Camera:** follow the athlete; at release `cam.frame([javelin, predictedLanding], { zoom: [.5, 1] })`; slow-mo .35\n  for the last 0.6 s; then a close shot of the javelin quivering in the turf.\n- **Scoring:** higher distance (0.01 m). WR **101.20 m (BLAZE CINDERHART, VOL)**. Qualify 58 / 72 / 82 m. Points\n  `10.14·(d − 7)^1.05` (WR ≈ 1200).\n- **CPU:** run rate by skill; release angle ~ N(38°, 7° − 5°·skill); foul chance (1 − skill)·12%; turbo on the run.\n- **Turbo:** HYPER ARM: release speed ×1.12 *(T)* and the javelin trails fire.\n- **Over the top:** > 120 m → OUT OF THE STADIUM: the javelin clears the wall, a car alarm whoops, the mark is\n  measured at the landing point in the parking lot (counts!). The blimp (at 55–70 m altitude, crossing at a random\n  x per round) can be popped by a steep, fast throw: confetti, \"BLIMP BUSTER!\", the javelin drops and its landing\n  counts.\n- **Tunables:** vMaxRun, angleRate, vRelBase, vRelPerRun, drag, windMax, turboMult.\n- **Yikes:** FOUL!, FLAT!. **Laurel:** OUT OF THE STADIUM (> 120 m).\n- **HUD:** angle gauge (a big quarter-circle dial with a green band 34°–42°), wind (arrow + m/s), run power, best mark,\n  standings strip.\n- **Targets:** perfect bot (38°, full run) 88–93 m; perfect + turbo + 3 m/s tailwind > 120 m possible; skill .5 ≈ 65–75 m;\n  release at 10° → flat; crossing the line → foul.\n- **Multiplayer:** humans alternate (the previous thrower's javelin flight shows as a ghost); **hub:** yes (2 throws).\n\n### 6.3 50m FREESTYLE (short course) — summer · Splash Palace · rhythm + breath\n\n- **View:** `'brawler'`, M = 12. A 25 m pool (x 0 → 300) with 8 lanes 2.5 m wide (30 u), animated water floor\n  (`E.tex.water` + caustics), lane ropes as rows of colored floats, backstroke flags, starting blocks, a deck, stands\n  and big windows to the beach; indoor bright light. 2 lengths with a turn at x = 300.\n- **Flow:** \"TAKE YOUR MARKS\" → beep after `0.8–1.6 s` → **start** (reaction as in the sprint; early = false start) →\n  **dive:** holding `action` 0.2–0.6 s then releasing gives the best glide (4 + 3·q m); holding past 0.75 s →\n  **BELLY FLOP START** (yikes, glide 2 m) → strokes → **turn** → strokes → **touch**.\n- **Strokes (`StrokeBeat`):** expected buttons alternate `mashL`, `mashR` on a beat whose tempo follows speed\n  (`50 + 50·v/vMax` strokes/min). A press within ±70 ms *(T)* of the beat is PERFECT, ±150 ms GOOD, else MISS (wasted,\n  splash, −5% speed); the wrong button is a MISS. Quality `q` = EMA (1.5 s) of 1 / .6 / 0;\n  `vTarget = vMax·(0.45 + 0.55·q)`, `vMax` 2.45 m/s *(T)*.\n- **Breathing:** O2 drains 0.11/s *(T)*; `alt` within 0.25 s after a stroke breathes (+0.45 O2, that stroke ×0.7).\n  O2 < .25 caps strokes at GOOD; O2 = 0 → **GASP!** (yikes: 1.2 s stop, cough, O2 back to .6).\n- **Turn:** inside 1.6 m of the wall the prompt \"✕ TURN\" appears: press at 0.6–1.1 m → PERFECT FLIP TURN (push-off at\n  1.25·vMax, hype +0.2); 1.1–1.6 m early (weak push); < 0.6 m late (normal); not pressed by the wall → **BONK!**\n  (yikes, +1.0 s).\n- **Touch:** `action` within the last 0.8 m reaches (−0.05 s); otherwise an automatic glide-in.\n- **Scoring:** lower time. WR **19.62 s (MARINA SPLASHWORTH, WAV)**. Qualify 25.5 / 23.2 / 21.6. Points\n  `18.9·(35 − t)^1.5`.\n- **CPU:** P(perfect) = .35 + .55·skill, P(good) the rest minus a miss rate (1 − skill)·.15; breathes every 3–4\n  strokes; turn quality by skill.\n- **Turbo:** DOLPHIN MODE: 3 s of automatic PERFECT strokes, vMax ×1.1, a cartoon dolphin leaps in the next lane.\n- **Tunables:** vMax, perfectWindow, goodWindow, o2Drain, breathGain, turnPush, diveGlide.\n- **Yikes:** FALSE START!, BELLY FLOP START, GASP!, BONK!. **Laurel:** TORPEDO (reaction < 0.15, perfect dive and\n  perfect turn in one race).\n- **HUD:** per human: the stroke ring with the next expected glyph, O2 bubble meter, hype flame; lap/turn indicator.\n- **Targets:** perfect bot 19.4–19.9 s; skill .5 ≈ 22.5–24; never breathing → at least one GASP; missing the turn →\n  BONK.\n- **Multiplayer:** up to 4 live; **hub:** yes.\n\n### 6.4 10m PLATFORM DIVING — summer · Splash Palace · tricks + entry timing\n\n- **View:** `'side'`, M = 12. Tower at the left (platforms at 1, 3, 5, 7.5, 10 m; the 10 m edge at x = 30, z = 120),\n  pool cross-section below (surface z = 0, depth to z = −60 drawn translucent with light shafts and bubbles), the 5\n  judges' table, the scoreboard, stands. Camera frames the diver and the water; slow-mo .35 at entry.\n- **Format:** 3 rounds; each round the diver picks 1 of 3 dives (one easy, one medium, one hard, never repeating a\n  dive). Total = sum of dive scores.\n- **Dive list:** Forward 2½ Pike (105B, DD 2.8, 5 half-somersaults, pike); Back 2½ Tuck (205C, DD 3.0, 5, tuck, back\n  take-off); Forward 3½ Tuck (107C, DD 3.3, 7, tuck); Inward 3½ Tuck (407C, DD 3.2, 7, tuck); Forward 2½ with 2 Twists\n  Pike (5154B, DD 3.6, 5 half-somersaults + 4 half-twists); **YIKES! Armstand Quintuple** (DD 4.8, 10, tuck: the\n  over-the-top dive).\n- **Take-off:** `TimingBar` (1.4 Hz): `vz = 4.2 + 1.6·q` m/s up, `vx = 1.0` m/s; airtime ≈ 1.9–2.1 s.\n- **In the air:** hold `mashL` = TUCK (ω 12.5 rad/s *(T)*), hold `mashR` = PIKE (ω 9 rad/s *(T)*), neither = OPEN\n  (1.5 rad/s *(T)*). A dial shows half-somersaults done vs required. Twist dives: each tap ←/→ while open or piked\n  adds a half twist (0.25 s each). The body rotation is drawn with the Pose module's `bodyPitch` (+ yaw for twists).\n- **Entry judgement:** at the surface, error `e` = |body angle − vertical (head first)| in degrees: ≤ 8 RIP (no\n  splash) base 9.5; ≤ 15 → 8.5; ≤ 25 → 7.0; ≤ 45 → 5.0; ≤ 75 → 3.0; > 75 → **BELLY FLOP / BACK SLAP** (yikes) 1.0.\n  Adjust: take-off +0…+0.5; wrong position −1.0; each missing/extra half-somersault −2.0; each missing half-twist −1.5;\n  judge noise ±0.5 per judge from `rng('judges:...')`; clamp 0–10, round to 0.5. 5 judges, drop high and low,\n  dive score = middle three × DD.\n- **Scoring:** higher total. WR **338.40 (COCO BONBON, BON)** (the maximum possible is 351: three perfect dives of DD 4.8, 3.6, 3.3). Qualify 150 / 195 / 240. Points `3.4·total`.\n- **CPU:** take-off q ~ skill; release error σ = (1 − skill)·35°; picks hard dives when skill > .8.\n- **Turbo:** SLOW-MO SUPREMACY: time ×0.5 for 2.5 s of the dive (more control), sparkle trail.\n- **Tunables:** tuckSpin, pikeSpin, openSpin, takeoffVz, ripTolerance, judgeNoise, twistTime.\n- **Yikes:** BELLY FLOP (the judges hold up 0.5 cards; the splash soaks them), WRONG WAY (back slap). **Laurel:**\n  PERFECT 10s (all five judges 10).\n- **HUD:** dive name + DD, rotation dial, position prompt (glyph □ TUCK / ○ PIKE), twist counter, judges' cards on\n  entry.\n- **Targets:** perfect bot on the 4.8 dive → five 10s (score ≥ 140); skill .5 average ≈ 60–70 per dive; holding tuck\n  to the water from a 2½ → over-rotation penalty or belly flop.\n- **Multiplayer:** alternate; **hub:** yes (2 dives, the options dealt from `AIHub.rng`).\n\n### 6.5 ARCHERY — summer · Bullseye Lawn (seaside) · aim under sway\n\n- **View:** main = the **target close-up** (a 122 cm face, 10 rings + X, drawn ~200 px across: readable at 10 feet);\n  inset (bottom-left, ~30% height) = the archer in `'side'` view at the line drawing the bow, palm trees and the sea\n  behind, wind flags. During flight the inset shows the arrow leaving; the target view zooms 1.1× toward the impact.\n- **Format:** attempts: 6 arrows in 2 ends of 3 (a 20 s shot clock per arrow; 12 s in hub heats). Score 0–60; ties by X count, then 10s.\n- **Draw:** hold `action` 0.9 s *(T)* to full draw (string tension bar). Release before full draw → weak arrow\n  (25 cm low + spread).\n- **Aim:** stick/WASD moves the aim at 40 cm/s *(T)*; mouse: the pointer sets the aim directly. **Sway** adds\n  `A·(sin 1.3t·cos 0.7t, sin(1.7t + 1))` + value noise, `A = A0·(1 + 0.6·max(0, held − 2.5 s))·hr`, `A0` 7 cm *(T)*,\n  heart rate `hr` 1.0 → 1.6 (rises after a bad arrow and on the final arrow of the match).\n- **Hold breath:** hold `alt` (L, R2 or right mouse) at full draw: sway ×0.25 for up to 2.5 s *(T)*; when the breath\n  bar empties, sway ×2 for 2 s (gasping).\n- **Wind:** per arrow from `rng('archery:wind:<n>')` in −4…+4 m/s; impact shift 4.5 cm per m/s *(T)* sideways. Shown\n  as a flag, an arrow and a number. Aim off to compensate.\n- **Release:** let go of `action` at full draw → flight 0.75 s → impact = aim + sway at release + wind shift + release\n  jitter (more if the aim was moving) → ring score; X ring → \"BULLSEYE!\". An impact within 1.0 cm of an earlier arrow\n  → **ROBIN HOOD** (the old arrow splits; same score).\n- **Scoring:** WR **60 (6 X) — PIXEL VANCE (NEO)**. Qualify 40 / 48 / 53. Points `20·score`.\n- **CPU:** aim error σ = (1 − skill)·12 + 2 cm, wind compensation accuracy = skill; CPU arrows show on a mini target\n  on the standings board.\n- **Turbo:** EAGLE EYE: game time ×0.4 and sway ×0.1 for 3 s of real time.\n- **Tunables:** drawTime, swayA0, swayGrowth, breathTime, windMax, windShift.\n- **Yikes:** STRING SLAP (releasing while gasping: \"OW!\", the arrow flies wide). **Laurel:** ROBIN HOOD.\n- **Targets:** perfect bot = 60; a no-breath, no-wind-compensation bot at 4 m/s wind averages < 8 per arrow.\n- **Multiplayer:** alternate per arrow; **hub:** yes (3 arrows, 12 s shot clock).\n\n### 6.6 WEIGHTLIFTING (clean & jerk) — summer · Iron Hall · mash + balance + timing\n\n- **View:** `'brawler'`; the lifter (bulky build, singlet, belt, chalked hands) faces the camera on a wooden platform;\n  spotlights in a dark hall (`lights` ambient .35 + two warm spots); 3 referees with white/red lights; the bar bends\n  with load; plates colored by mass (25 red, 20 blue, 15 yellow, 10 green, 5 white, 2.5 black, collars). Chalk dust.\n- **Format:** attempts × 3. Pick the opening weight from 5 offered (Normal 200/210/220/230/240 kg), then +5 / +10 / +15\n  for the next; the third attempt may take the **YIKES BAR** (WR + 10 kg). Best good lift counts; ties go to whoever made\n  that weight first.\n- **Load factor** `w = (kg − 150)/120`.\n- **CLEAN (4.0 s *(T)*):** bar height `h` 0 → 1 (floor → shoulders): `h += (rate − 0.7·rReq)·0.12·dt` *(T)*,\n  `rReq = 5.5 + 4.5·w` Hz; the bar sinks if rate < 0.5·rReq; time out → no lift.\n- **RACK:** `Balance` (drift ×(1 + w)); keep |b| < .35 for 1.2 s *(T)*; |b| > 1 → drop.\n- **JERK:** `Ring` (0.9 s): PERFECT → overhead wobble ×0.5; GOOD ×1; BAD → 50% fail, else wobble ×1.8.\n- **HOLD:** `Balance` overhead for 2.0 s *(T)*, drift grows with w → three white lights \"GOOD LIFT!\" (a WR cracks the\n  floor), else the bar drops.\n- **Scoring:** WR **270 kg (BLAZE CINDERHART, VOL)**. Qualify 200 / 225 / 245 kg. Points `min(1200, 9.5·(kg − 150))`.\n- **CPU:** success probability `1/(1 + e^((kg − (190 + 80·skill))/6))`; picks weights like a cautious coach.\n- **Turbo:** IRON WILL: balance drift ×0.2 and lift power ×1.4 for 3 s.\n- **Tunables:** cleanTime, liftGain, rReqBase, rReqPerW, rackTime, holdTime, driftBase.\n- **Yikes:** DROP (the bar bounces twice and the lifter sits down hard, \"OOF\"). **Laurel:** YIKES WEIGHT (lift the\n  YIKES BAR).\n- **HUD:** big kg number, phase name, the mash pair, the balance needle (huge, center-bottom), the jerk ring, the 3\n  lights.\n- **Targets:** perfect bot lifts 280; skill .5 tops out ≈ 220–230; idle → no lift; |b| > 1 → drop.\n- **Multiplayer:** alternate attempts; **hub:** yes (2 attempts: 220 then 240 kg).\n\n### 6.7 SKI JUMP (large hill, K-125, HS-140) — winter · Mount Glory Jumping Hill · timing + flight balance\n\n- **View:** `'side'`, **M = 8** (the hill is big). Night, floodlights (`lights.add` along the in-run and the landing\n  hill), light snow (`game.weather = { kind: 'snow', amount: .3 }`), alpine backdrop (custom `E.Backdrop` layers:\n  mountains, pine forest, a starry sky), the jump tower, the K-point and HS lines, distance boards every 10 m,\n  cowbell crowd and flags in the out-run.\n- **Hill profile (meters, origin at the take-off edge):** in-run 95 m at 35° from the start gate, table −11°; landing\n  hill: knoll `z = −3·(x/15)²` for x < 15, then a 30° slope `z = −3 − 0.58·(x − 15)` to x = 125, then easing out with\n  `+0.0045·(x − 125)²` into the flat out-run. Distance is measured along the slope from the edge (precompute a\n  polyline with arc lengths).\n- **Format:** attempts × 2 jumps. Score per jump = distance points + style points.\n- **Flow:** start gate (`action` pushes off) → **in-run:** a `Balance` needle on ↑/↓ (keep the tuck): speed ×(0.94…1.0)\n  by average balance quality; `a = g·sin35° − μ·g·cos35° − kAir·v²` (μ .02, kAir .0016 *(T)*) → ≈ 25.5 m/s at the\n  table with a perfect tuck. → **take-off:** press `action` in the last 4 m before the edge: last 1.0 m q = 1, 1–2.5 m\n  .7, 2.5–4 m .4; no press → **FELL OFF THE TABLE** (q .1, yikes hop). Adds `vz += 2.4·q` m/s. → **flight:** body\n  angle α (to the airflow) changed by ↑/↓ at 40°/s; gusts from `rng('skijump:gust')` push α; lift `aL = cL(α)·v²`\n  (⊥ velocity), drag `aD = cD(α)·v²`, with `cL(α) = cL0·max(.1, 1 − ((α − 12)/30)²)`, `cL0` .00095 *(T)*,\n  `cD(α) = .0006 + .00002·α` *(T)*. → **landing:** within 2.5 m above the slope the prompt \"✕ TELEMARK!\" appears;\n  press within 0.35 s before contact → telemark; later/none → two-footed; landing with |α| > 40° *(T)*, or beyond\n  HS + 10 m without a telemark → **CRASH** (tumble down the out-run: Pose tumble, skis fly as sprites, snow spray).\n- **Scoring:** distance points `60 + (d − 125)·1.8`; style: 5 judges, telemark 17.5–19.5, two-footed 15–17, crash 6–9\n  (minus wobble in flight), drop high/low, sum 3 (max 60). Event = 2 jumps. Hill record **148.0 m (INGRID\n  SNOWCASTLE, FRM)**, event WR **296.4**. Qualify 160 / 210 / 245 (2-jump total). Points `3.9·total`.\n- **CPU:** balance and take-off q by skill, flight α error (1 − skill)·15°, telemark chance = skill.\n- **Turbo:** ROCKET SKIS: lift ×1.1 and +3 m/s² thrust for 2 s, flames from the ski tails.\n- **Tunables:** kAir, takeoffBoost, cL0, cDBase, gust, telemarkWindow, crashAngle.\n- **Yikes:** FELL OFF THE TABLE, CRASH. **Laurel:** OFF THE CHART (land > 150 m without crashing).\n- **HUD:** speed (km/h) in the in-run, take-off zone bar, the flight angle gauge (a skier silhouette rotating over a\n  green band), distance counter following the jumper, telemark prompt, judges' style cards.\n- **Targets:** perfect bot 132–140 m; perfect + turbo ≥ 150 m; skill .5 ≈ 112–122 m; no take-off press → < 80 m.\n- **Multiplayer:** alternate jumps; **hub:** yes (1 jump).\n\n### 6.8 DOWNHILL — winter · \"The Yikes Face\" · steering + tuck + gates\n\n- **View:** pseudo-3D `E.Road` (`segment: 200`, 1 m = 100 road units; `width: 1600`, `lanes: 0`, `draw: 220`), the\n  skier drawn from behind at the bottom center through a custom rear view (§8.2: `new E.View('rear', 'Rear', 0, 18,\n  1.6, 1)`, rig facing +y, skis and poles projected with the view's `ax ay bx by bz`), snow colors (road\n  `#f4f8ff/#e8f0fb`, grass `#dfe9f6/#d3e0f0` deep snow, rumble = orange netting `#ff7a2a/#f05a1a`), pines,\n  spectators with flags and cowbells, banners, start hut, ice tunnel (`tunnel: true`, blue-white walls), sun glare\n  (an additive flare overlay), light snow.\n- **Course (≈1,440 m, 24 gates):**\n\n| # | Section | Length | Slope | Curves | Gates | Feature |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Start Schuss | 150 m | 28° | 0 | 1 | start hut, crowd |\n| 2 | The Corkscrew | 220 m | 22° | +4, −4, +3 | 5 | S-bends |\n| 3 | Kangaroo Kicker | 60 m | 10° → 32° | 0 | 1 | crest jump |\n| 4 | Pine Alley | 200 m | 20° | −2 | 3 | fences at x = ±1.05 (narrow) |\n| 5 | Ice Tunnel | 120 m | 18° | +2 | 1 | tunnel, grip ×0.6 |\n| 6 | The Yikes Face | 180 m | 38° | 0 | 3 | big crest jump at its top |\n| 7 | Glory Bend | 260 m | 18° | +5 (long) | 4 | strong outward push |\n| 8 | Finish Schuss | 250 m | 15° | ±1 | 6 | Victory Hop jump, finish arch, grandstand |\n\n  Build: for each section `road.add(len/2, { curve, hill: -len·tan(slope)·100 })` (in road units) and keep a parallel\n  meter-based table for physics (slope per segment, features, gate list `{ s, xc }`).\n- **Physics:** speed `v` along the course: `a = g·sin(slope) − (tuck ? dTuck : dUp)·v² − μ·g − carve·|steer|·v`\n  (dTuck .0028, dUp .0062, μ .03, carve .18 — all *(T)*). Lateral `x` (half-roads, piste |x| ≤ 1): `x' = steer·turn(v) −\n  push·curveAt(z)·v²·k`; `turn` ×0.55 while tucking. 1 < |x| < 1.25 deep snow (drag ×3); |x| ≥ 1.25 → **CRASH into the\n  netting** (yikes tumble 2.0 s, respawn |x| = 1, v = 10 m/s). **Jumps:** when the slope falls away faster than a\n  ballistic arc, the skier is airborne (`h'' = −g`, shadow on the snow); `action` 0.2–0.5 s before a crest = PRE-JUMP\n  (half the airtime: faster). Landing with |steer| > .6 or |x| > 1 → crash. **Gates:** passing |x − xc| ≤ .32 → +2%\n  speed (whoosh) and hype +0.05; missing → +0.50 s penalty (red \"+0.50\").\n- **Splits:** 3 checkpoints vs the current leader (green −, red +). The leader's run is a ghost skier.\n- **Scoring:** lower time incl. penalties. Course record **47.62 s (ROCKY SUMMIT, MTP)**. Qualify 58.0 / 52.5 / 49.0.\n  Points `8.5·(80 − t)^1.4`.\n- **CPU:** simulated runs with steering toward the next gate center, tuck on straights, noise and crash chance\n  (1 − skill)·15% at the Yikes Face; the top CPU run becomes the ghost.\n- **Turbo:** AVALANCHE: speed ×1.18 for 3 s with a cartoon avalanche cloud chasing behind.\n- **Tunables:** dTuck, dUp, turnRate, curvePush, gateBoost, missPenalty, crashSteer.\n- **Yikes:** CRASH (netting), CRASH (landing). **Laurel:** CLEAN SWEEP (all 24 gates).\n- **HUD:** time, speed (km/h), split popups, gate counter (n/24), a course strip (progress line with the leader's\n  dot), tuck indicator, hype flame.\n- **Targets:** perfect bot 46.5–48.5 s; skill .5 ≈ 53–56 s; steering hard into the netting → crash; all gates\n  possible.\n- **Multiplayer:** humans take turns, each seeing the best run so far as a ghost; **hub:** yes (1 run; other\n  players' skiers as ghosts drawn as road \"cars\").\n\n### 6.9 TWO-MAN BOBSLED — winter · Glory Ice Track (dusk) · push + load + banked steering\n\n- **View:** `E.Road` again (1 m = 100 units, `width` ≈ 400: a narrow channel; tune for the look), the track as an ice channel: road = ice (`#d8eef8/#cfe6f2`),\n  rumble = blue-white walls, grass = snow banks, tunnel roofs on covered sections, dusk sky with floodlights placed as\n  glowing scenery, timing boards. The sled (drawn with `px.poly` boxes through the rear view, in the nation's colors,\n  number on the cowl) with two rigs seated (Pose `bobPilot`, `bobBrake`), tilted by its wall height.\n- **Track (≈1,300 m, 15 named curves):** Sunny Start, Glory Kink, The Twins (2), Shark Fin, Kreisel (long +6),\n  Labyrinth (3, S-S-S), Omega (+6/−6), The Washing Machine, Double Trouble (2), Last Gasp, Finish Curve.\n- **Flow:** **push** (first 50 m): mash; `dv/dt = 6·power·(1 − v/11)` m/s² *(T)*; the start time at 50 m is shown","numLines":300,"startLine":600,"totalLines":1723}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017ePRVWFJc1g5Bfuc9V1zV5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
