{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Likd9pdj3R4VWr4fEjciUo","type":"tool_result","content":"900\t  (good ≈ 4.9 s) → **load:** press `action` between 40 and 50 m (the \"LOAD\" zone flashes): in the zone no loss; early\n901\t  ×0.95 speed; missed by 50 m → automatic load with −1.5 m/s and a **YIKES** (the brakeman flails, one leg out) →\n902\t  **drive:** `a = g·sin(slope) − drag·v² − μ·g − scrape`; lateral `x'' = force·curveAt(z)·v² − steer·steerForce −\n903\t  damp·x'`; the **groove** (ideal x for this curve and speed) shows as a glowing band on a U-shaped cross-section gauge;\n904\t  |x − groove| > .25 → skid (−2%/s, sparks); |x| > 1.55 → **FLIP** (yikes: the sled slides on its roof for 2 s in\n905\t  slow-mo, then rights itself at −35% speed) → finish and braking zone.\n906\t- **Format:** attempts × 2 runs, combined time. Track record **40.11 s per run (MAX OVERDRIVE, TRB)**. Qualify (2 runs)\n907\t  92.0 / 86.0 / 82.0. Points `6.4·(120 − total)^1.4`.\n908\t- **CPU:** simulated; push rate by skill; groove error by skill.\n909\t- **Turbo:** JET SLED: speed ×1.15 and auto-groove for 3 s, a jet flame from the tail.\n910\t- **Tunables:** pushGain, loadZone, drag, curveForce, steerForce, grooveTolerance, flipHeight.\n911\t- **Yikes:** LATE LOAD, FLIP. **Laurel:** ICE DANCER (a run with no skid or wall contact).\n912\t- **Targets:** perfect bot 39.8–40.6 s per run; skill .5 ≈ 42.5–44; not steering in Omega → flip.\n913\t- **Multiplayer:** alternate runs with the best run as a ghost; **hub:** yes (1 run).\n914\t\n915\t### 6.10 FIGURE SKATING (free skate) — winter · Glory Ice Palace · rhythm\n916\t\n917\t- **View:** `'threequarter'`; a 60×30 m rink (ice texture with scratches and reflections), boards with sponsor-free\n918\t  banners, spotlights (ambient .45 + moving spots), the kiss & cry booth (bench, flowers, a giant plush mascot) where\n919\t  scores are read, stands. The skater follows a closed `E.Path` (a large loop with a figure-8 crossing) at a pace tied\n920\t  to the music.\n921\t- **Music/chart:** original **\"Waltz of the Yikes\"** in 3/4 at 138 bpm, ~64 s (§9.1), played through `E.Rhythm`\n922\t  (`lanes: ['left', 'down', 'up', 'right', 'action']`, holds on `action` are jumps). Windows perfect 45 / great 90 /\n923\t  good 135 ms (×1.4 with Timing assist). Chart parts: Intro 4 bars · Step Sequence A 8 · Jump Combo 1 4 (two holds) ·\n924\t  Spiral & Spin 8 · **Coach's Corner** 8 (4 bars of calls `c` from the coach, then you answer: PaRappa-style) · Step\n925\t  Sequence B 8 (denser) · Jump Combo 2 4 (the 4-beat **QUAD YIKES** hold) · Finale 4 + the final-pose note. About 140\n926\t  notes. Easy uses every other non-hold note.\n927\t- **Highway:** a horizontal highway along the bottom third (notes travel right → left to a target line), 5 lanes\n928\t  labeled with glyph icons (← ↓ ↑ → and ✕/Space), big notes (10 px), judgement words over the skater.\n929\t- **Moves:** each judged note triggers a move on the rig: ←/→ edge steps and leans; ↑ spiral (one leg high behind,\n930\t  arms out); ↓ sit spin (`rig.spin` accelerating); a hold = jump: take-off on the hold's head, airborne rotations\n931\t  (`rig.spin` 4 turns/s, arms crossed), landing on release (great/perfect → clean landing with the free leg back; a\n932\t  miss → **FALL**: slide on the backside, get up, combo lost).\n933\t- **Scoring:** TES = Σ note value × (1 / .8 / .5 / 0) scaled so a perfect program = 130; PCS = 5 components (skating\n934\t  skills, transitions, performance, composition, interpretation) 0–10 each from accuracy, max combo, falls and finish\n935\t  pose, ×2 → max 100; falls −1 each. WR **228.56 (COCO BONBON, BON)**. Qualify 120 / 150 / 180. Points\n936\t  `min(1200, 5.3·total)`.\n937\t- **CPU:** simulated accuracy ~ skill ± noise → TES/PCS; the top 2 rivals' scores revealed in the kiss & cry.\n938\t- **Turbo:** STAR POWER: 4 s, every judgement one level better, rainbow trail and glitter; afterwards the crowd throws\n939\t  plush mascots onto the ice.\n940\t- **Tunables:** perfectMs, greatMs, goodMs, lifeDrain, tesScale, pcsWeight.\n941\t- **Yikes:** FALL. **Laurel:** FULL COMBO (no misses).\n942\t- **Targets:** autoplay (`rh.hit` on every note) = full combo, ≈ 225–230; idle → life fails → program ends early with\n943\t  low score but still a result.\n944\t- **Multiplayer:** alternate programs; **hub:** no.\n945\t\n946\t### 6.11 CURLING (gold medal match) — winter · Glory Curling Club · aim + weight + sweep (physics)\n947\t\n948\t- **View:** `'topdown'`; an arcade sheet (meters): hack y = 0, near hog line 6, far hog line 22, tee (house center) 27,\n949\t  back line 28.8, width 4.75 (x ±2.375), house radius 1.83 with rings (blue/white/red), stones r = 0.30 (arcade-sized,\n950\t  granite with handles in the two nations' colors). M = 12; camera zoom 1.2 during the delivery, follows the stone,\n951\t  2.5 over the house; a house-cam inset (top-right) always shows the house. Warm club lights, a scoreboard with ends.\n952\t- **Match:** you vs one CPU nation (Mountopia unless you are Mountopia; then the best other curler), 2 ends × 4 stones\n953\t  per team, alternating; hammer to the team that did not score (end 1 by coin flip from `rng('curling:hammer')`).\n954\t- **Delivery:** (1) **AIM**: stick ←/→ (or the pointer) moves the skip's broom target across the house; (2) **CURL**:\n955\t  `mashL` in-turn, `mashR` out-turn (an arrow on the stone; the first ~30% of the predicted path shows as dots);\n956\t  (3) **WEIGHT**: `action` starts the slide; a weight meter oscillates 0 → 1 → 0 at 1.1 Hz *(T)* with bands GUARD\n957\t  .25–.45, DRAW .45–.65, TAKEOUT .65–1.0; `action` again releases at that weight (`v0 = 1.8 + 2.0·w` m/s); releasing at\n958\t  w ≥ .98 = over-throw slip (yikes, still delivered); (4) **SWEEP**: mash while the stone travels: sweep =\n959\t  rate/8 Hz (clamped) cuts friction `μ = .019·(1 − .35·sweep)` and curl ×(1 − .5·sweep).\n960\t- **Physics:** `E.Physics` with gravity 0 for collisions (`world.circle(..., { bounce: .85, friction: .1, bullet: true })`);\n961\t  each step the game applies the ice: deceleration `μ·g` along the velocity and curl `a = spin·κ/(v + .5)`\n962\t  (κ .05 *(T)*) across it. Stones that touch the side boards or pass the back line are removed; a stone that stops\n963\t  before the far hog line is removed. Collisions above 2 m/s make sparks and a CLACK.\n964\t- **Scoring per end:** the team with the stone nearest the button scores 1 per stone nearer than the opponent's\n965\t  nearest (stones touching the house only). Ties after 2 ends → an extra end.\n966\t- **CPU:** for its throw it evaluates 9 aims × 6 weights × 2 spins = 108 candidates, **each simulated in a sandbox\n967\t  physics world** (12 per frame, so no hitch), scores the outcome (own shot stone in the house +, opponent shot\n968\t  stones −, guards protecting own stones +), picks the best, then adds execution noise (aim ±.15 m, weight ±.06,\n969\t  × (1 − skill)) and sweeps by its own plan.\n970\t- **Turbo:** HYPER SWEEP: 3 s of maximum sweep regardless of mashing, glowing brooms and ice sparkles.\n971\t- **Medals:** winner gold, loser silver, bronze from a simulated match between the next two nations.\n972\t- **Tunables:** mu, sweepCut, curlK, weightHz, v0Base, v0Range, cpuNoise.\n973\t- **Yikes:** OVER-THROW SLIP; a stone you throw that knocks your own shot stone out → \"OWN GOAL!\". **Laurel:** DOUBLE\n974\t  TAKEOUT (two opponent stones removed by one throw).\n975\t- **Targets:** a draw-weight throw with no sweep stops in the house (±1.5 m of the button); takeout weight on a stone\n976\t  removes it; a .9-skill CPU beats a .3-skill CPU in ≥ 80% of 30 seeded matches; no frame spends > 8 ms on CPU sims.\n977\t- **Multiplayer:** versus (P1 and P2 skip opposing teams) or co-op (P1 throws, P2 sweeps); **hub:** no.\n978\t\n979\t### 6.12 ICE HOCKEY FINAL (2-on-2 + goalies) — winter · Glory Arena · team action\n980\t\n981\t- **Start from `kits/sports.js`** (its cage, ball-as-Body, passes led to the teammate, `E.arc` lobs, shot meter with\n982\t  aftertouch curl, formation AI, `game.allowJoin({ max: 4 })`) and turn it into hockey: the pitch becomes a rink\n983\t  (ice floor texture, red center line, blue lines, faceoff circles, creases), the boards get glass on top (`h` higher,\n984\t  translucent top band), nets 3 tiles wide with posts; the ball becomes a **puck** (flat sprite, `bounce` 0 on the\n985\t  ice, board restitution .65, low friction); players skate with momentum (accel 220 u/s², max 105 u/s, glide);\n986\t  add an **automatic goalie** per side (a Body on an arc in its crease that moves toward the puck–goal line at a\n987\t  skill-limited speed and saves on contact, sometimes freezing the puck for a faceoff). Arena: dark with spotlights,\n988\t  a center-hung jumbotron, goal lights and horn, organ music.\n989\t- **Match:** your nation vs the rival (Turbonia, or §5.6's rival if you are Turbonia), 2 periods × 90 s of running clock *(T)*, a resurfacing machine\n990\t  crossing at intermission, sudden-death overtime 90 s, then a **shootout** (3 rounds then sudden death: a skater\n991\t  starts at center with the puck, 6 s to shoot, vs the goalie).\n992\t- **Controls:** skate (stick), `mashL` pass (to the teammate the stick points at, led), `action` hold = shot meter,\n993\t  release = shoot (stick aims; push sideways just after = curl), `mashR` = **check** without the puck (a shoulder\n994\t  lunge: a hit knocks the opponent down 1 s, the puck squirts loose; into the boards → the glass shakes, crowd \"OOOH\")\n995\t  or switch to the teammate nearer the puck when far, `alt` = skate burst (stamina bar), `turbo` = **ON FIRE** (when\n996\t  the hype is full, or automatically after 3 straight good plays: the puck burns, shots ×1.4 speed, goalies react 50%\n997\t  slower, until a goal or 8 s). Mouse: left hold/release shoots toward the cursor, right passes toward it.\n998\t- **Hype:** completed passes, hits, shots on goal, saves avoided.\n999\t- **Medals:** winner gold, loser silver; bronze simulated.\n1000\t- **Tunables:** periodLength, skateAccel, skateMax, shotPower, puckFriction, goalieSpeed, checkPower.\n1001\t- **Yikes:** CHECKED INTO THE GLASS (when you get hit), OWN GOAL. **Laurel:** HAT TRICK (one skater scores 3).\n1002\t- **Targets:** bot vs bot (skill .9 vs .3) wins ≥ 80% of 30 seeded matches; goals happen (≥ 1 per period on average\n1003\t  at equal skill .7); a shot on an empty net scores; checks knock down.\n1004\t- **Multiplayer:** up to 4: 2v2 versus or co-op vs the CPU; **hub:** no.\n1005\t\n1006\t---\n1007\t\n1008\t## 7. Content\n1009\t\n1010\t**Originality rules:** fictional nations, athletes, venues and mascot; no Olympic rings or official emblems, no real\n1011\tanthems, fanfares or broadcast themes; in-game text says \"the Games\". The hub `source` meta may say \"The Olympic\n1012\tGames\" (it is descriptive).\n1013\t\n1014\t### 7.1 Nations and their star athletes (8 = 8 lanes)\n1015\t\n1016\t| Code | Nation | Colors (a / b / c) | Flag (drawn in code) | Athlete | Rig (`new E.Humanoid`) | Voice | Personality |\n1017\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1018\t| SUN | SUNVALE | `#f2b632` gold / `#2f7fe0` sky / `#ffffff` | sky field, gold sun disc with 8 rays | **DASH GOLDBERRY** | heroic, hair short `#3a2414`, skin `#8d5a3b` | pitch 1.0, speed 1.1 | sunny optimist |\n1019\t| FRM | FROSTMARK | `#f4f8ff` snow / `#2fa8d8` glacier / `#1a3a6a` navy | white field, glacier snowflake, navy border | **INGRID SNOWCASTLE** | heroic, ponytail `#f3e6c0`, skin `#f2d4c4` | 1.3, 0.9 | deadpan |\n1020\t| TRB | TURBONIA | `#e23b2e` red / `#1e2026` carbon / `#ffd23a` yellow | diagonal red/carbon split, yellow lightning bolt | **MAX OVERDRIVE** (the rival) | heroic, spiky `#141414`, skin `#c88a5e`, red headband (`hat: band`) | 0.9, 1.25 | arrogant, loud |\n1021\t| BON | BONBONIA | `#ff7fb8` pink / `#6fe0c0` mint / `#ffffff` | vertical candy stripes, small heart | **COCO BONBON** | heroic, long `#ff9ad0`, skin `#f5c9a8`, `face: { eyes: 'big' }` | 1.45, 1.05 | theatrical |\n1022\t| VOL | VOLCANICA | `#ff6a1a` lava / `#3a2e2e` basalt / `#ffd0a0` ember | basalt field, orange volcano, yellow eruption dot | **BLAZE CINDERHART** | **bulky**, bald, skin `#6a4028` | 0.7, 0.85 | gentle giant |\n1023\t| WAV | WAVELIA | `#1fa8a0` teal / `#0e4a6a` deep / `#e8fbf7` foam | teal field, three white waves | **MARINA SPLASHWORTH** | heroic, short `#24160e`, skin `#5a3420` | 1.25, 0.95 | calm poet |\n1024\t| MTP | MOUNTOPIA | `#6a3fc8` purple / `#c8ccd8` silver / `#ffffff` | purple field, white peak, 3 silver stars | **ROCKY SUMMIT** | heroic, short `#8a5a2a`, skin `#e0b090`, beanie (`hat: cap`) | 0.95, 1.0 | folksy |\n1025\t| NEO | NEON REPUBLIC | `#e83ae0` magenta / `#14102a` night / `#3ae8f0` cyan | night field, cyan ring, magenta star | **PIXEL VANCE** | heroic, spiky `#3ae8f0`, skin `#f0c8a8` | 1.15, 1.2 | gamer slang |\n1026\t\n1027\tOutfits come from `O.makeRig(nation, sport)`: singlet + shorts (track, weights: belt), swim cap + goggles (pool),\n1028\tracing suit + helmet + goggles (downhill, bobsled, ski jump bib with number), sparkly costume (figure skating: the\n1029\tnation's colors + `trim` sequins), sweater (curling), padded jersey + helmet (hockey), team tracksuit (ceremonies).\n1030\tEvery rig size 1.25 (bulky Blaze 1.3), with the nation's 4–6 colors (never engine defaults).\n1031\t\n1032\t**CPU skill per event** (0–1; effective skill per §5.6):\n1033\t\n1034\t| | 100m | Jav | Swim | Dive | Arch | Wts | SkiJ | Down | Bob | Fig | Curl | Hock |\n1035\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1036\t| SUN | .92 | .85 | .70 | .62 | .66 | .70 | .60 | .65 | .78 | .60 | .62 | .74 |\n1037\t| FRM | .70 | .74 | .66 | .68 | .80 | .66 | .94 | .92 | .74 | .76 | .80 | .78 |\n1038\t| TRB | .93 | .90 | .78 | .70 | .72 | .82 | .80 | .84 | .95 | .62 | .66 | .93 |\n1039\t| BON | .66 | .62 | .80 | .92 | .74 | .58 | .70 | .68 | .62 | .95 | .70 | .64 |\n1040\t| VOL | .72 | .88 | .62 | .55 | .64 | .95 | .62 | .70 | .86 | .52 | .82 | .88 |\n1041\t| WAV | .74 | .68 | .95 | .88 | .70 | .64 | .66 | .62 | .64 | .80 | .72 | .66 |\n1042\t| MTP | .68 | .72 | .64 | .60 | .86 | .74 | .82 | .88 | .80 | .66 | .93 | .80 |\n1043\t| NEO | .78 | .70 | .72 | .74 | .93 | .60 | .74 | .76 | .70 | .82 | .76 | .84 |\n1044\t\n1045\t**Teammates** (bobsled brakeman, hockey partner and goalie, curling team), generated rigs in team colors:\n1046\tSUN Sunny Ray, Bo Marigold, Lux Daybright · FRM Sven Driftholm, Liv Hailstrom, Nils Frostby · TRB Rev Throttleton,\n1047\tNitro Vex, Gigi Torque · BON Taffy Swirl, Praline Dupree, Nougat Fizz · VOL Ash Kindleton, Ember Stone, Obsidia Crag ·\n1048\tWAV Coral Finley, Tide Brennan, Kai Seaborne · MTP Edelweiss Vogt, Cliff Hangar, Scree Halvorsen · NEO Byte Ortega,\n1049\tGlitch Kowalski, Vector Nakamura.\n1050\t\n1051\t**\"Up Close & Personal\" bios** (one per day card, rotating; the player's own athlete gets one on Day 1):\n1052\t- **Dash Goldberry (SUN):** \"Dash grew up on a farm in rural Sunvale, chasing the family's prize ostrich to school\n1053\t  every morning. The ostrich never once let him win. Today, he runs for Daisy.\"\n1054\t- **Ingrid Snowcastle (FRM):** \"Ingrid's grandmother taught her to ski jump off the roof of the family sauna. The sauna\n1055\t  has since been rebuilt. Twice.\"\n1056\t- **Max Overdrive (TRB):** \"Defending champion in, quote, 'everything'. Max has never lost a race, a staring contest,\n1057\t  or an argument with a mirror. His hobbies include winning and describing winning.\"\n1058\t- **Coco Bonbon (BON):** \"Coco skates every program to the songs her grandfather whistled. She says she can still hear\n1059\t  him in the crowd. Usually slightly off-key.\"\n1060\t- **Blaze Cinderhart (VOL):** \"Every winter morning, Blaze lifts the family car out of a volcanic ash drift. The car is\n1061\t  fine. The car is extremely well-defined.\"\n1062\t- **Marina Splashworth (WAV):** \"Born on a houseboat, Marina didn't touch dry land until she was four. On land she still\n1063\t  walks like the deck is moving. In the water... poetry.\"\n1064\t- **Rocky Summit (MTP):** \"Rocky's village sits so high that the mail arrives by curling stone. He has been sweeping since\n1065\t  before he could walk. His first word was 'HARD!'\"\n1066\t- **Pixel Vance (NEO):** \"Pixel learned archery from an arcade cabinet and has never seen daylight without sunglasses.\n1067\t  Pixel's coach is a toaster named Gary. Gary believes in Pixel.\"\n1068\t\n1069\t### 7.2 Venues (levels)\n1070\t\n1071\t| Venue | Events / scenes | View | Light | Key art (all drawn in code; generic props from the engine library/asset store) |\n1072\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1073\t| **Glory Stadium** (Sunny Bay) | 100m, Javelin; opening & closing ceremonies; stadium podiums | brawler | day (events), night + fireworks (ceremonies) | red 8-lane track with lane numbers, infield grass with mown stripes, 3-tier stands + crowd, the cauldron tower, jumbotron, finish gantry & clock, flags of the 8 nations on the rim, the blimp, parking lot past the wall |\n1074\t| **Splash Palace** | 50m Free, Diving | brawler / side | indoor bright, caustics | pool, lane ropes, blocks, flags line, the dive tower, judges' table, windows onto the beach, jumbotron |\n1075\t| **Bullseye Lawn** | Archery | overlay + side inset | sunny, breezy | target faces, palms, the sea, wind flags, shade tent |\n1076\t| **Iron Hall** | Weightlifting | brawler | dark, two spotlights | platform, chalk bowl, referee lights, plate rack, dim crowd |\n1077\t| **Mount Glory Jumping Hill** | Ski Jump | side | night floodlights, light snow | tower, in-run, K/HS lines, distance boards, out-run crowd with cowbells and flags |\n1078\t| **The Yikes Face** | Downhill | E.Road | bright day, sun glare, light snow | piste, orange netting, pines, start hut, ice tunnel, jumps, finish arch, grandstand |\n1079\t| **Glory Ice Track** | Bobsled | E.Road | dusk, floodlights | ice channel, named curve signs, tunnels, timing boards |\n1080\t| **Glory Ice Palace** | Figure Skating | threequarter | spotlights | rink, kiss & cry, flowers, plush rain |\n1081\t| **Glory Curling Club** | Curling | topdown | warm indoor | sheet, houses, scoreboard, pennants |\n1082\t| **Glory Arena** | Ice Hockey | threequarter | dark arena + spots | rink, glass, center jumbotron cube, goal lights, organ loft |\n1083\t\n1084\tUse `node vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/tools/asset-find.mjs \"<thing>\"` for generic props (benches, fences, pines,\n1085\tsnow blocks, banners, lamps, flags: the `kenney-holiday`, `kenney-nature`, `ambientcg` sets have snow, pines, ice and\n1086\tfences); cut the few you use into a set of your own with `tools/asset-set.mjs` and inline it.\n1087\t\n1088\t### 7.3 Story structure (The Games)\n1089\t\n1090\t| When | Beat | Content |\n1091\t|---|---|---|\n1092\t| Start | **Opening ceremony** | §7.4 |\n1093\t| Day 1 (before) | Max's welcome | in the call room: \"Lane four? Cute. I'm in lane five. Lane five is where legends warm up.\" |\n1094\t| After Day 2 | **Mascot incident** | Yikesy \"test-jumps\" the ski jump: a 6 s cutscene (the Blob launched, spinning, lands in a snowbank head-first). Chip: \"The mascot has... the mascot has set a personal best!\" Vera: \"And a personal worst. Simultaneously.\" |\n1095\t| After Day 4 | Curling chat | Rocky: \"Back home we curl to settle arguments. Mostly about curling.\" |\n1096\t| After Day 6 | **HALFTIME REPORT** | medal table + banter; Yikesy appears, dripping (\"rescued from the pool filter\"); Max line depends on standings (§7.6) |\n1097\t| After Day 8 | Coco's moment | Coco (any result): \"Grandpa, that one was for you.\" Vera, quietly: \"...Give me a second, Chip.\" |\n1098\t| After Day 10 | Sled scandal | Vera: \"Turbonia's sled has a spoiler. And a cup holder.\" Max: \"It's called aerodynamic hospitality.\" |\n1099\t| Day 12 (before) | **THE FINAL** | both anthems tease; Max: \"Two nations. One puck. Zero chance. For you.\" |\n1100\t| After Day 12 | Sportsmanship | win: Max: \"...Good game. Next Games I'm bringing two helmets. One for my ego.\" · loss: Max: \"Good game. You were almost me.\" |\n1101\t| End | **Closing ceremony** | §7.4; ending by rank |\n1102\t| Dynamic | Rival reactions | after any event with you and Max both in the top 4: a line from the bank (beat him / he beat you) |\n1103\t| Dynamic | Records & yikes | a WR by you → Vera's sentimental line; 5+ yikes → Vera: \"Statistically, the most entertaining athlete in Games history.\" |\n1104\t\n1105\t### 7.4 Ceremony scripts\n1106\t\n1107\t**Opening ceremony** (Glory Stadium at night, ~60 s, hold ✕ 1 s to skip):\n1108\t1. Fireworks over the twin city (the ski jump floodlit beyond the stadium rim). PA (echo): \"Ladies and gentlemen...\n1109\t   welcome to the Games of Mount Glory and Sunny Bay!\"\n1110\t2. Chip: \"Good evening, everybody! For the first time in history, the Summer and Winter Games are happening at the\n1111\t   SAME TIME, in the SAME PLACE!\" Vera: \"Some called it impossible. Others called it a scheduling error. Tonight we\n1112\t   call it... OLYMPIYIKES!\"\n1113\t3. **Parade of nations** (rigs marching in tracksuits behind a flag bearer, crowd waving that nation's colors), one\n1114\t   line each: SUNVALE \"where the sun never sets and the sunscreen budget is classified.\" · FROSTMARK \"their flag bearer\n1115\t   is carrying the flag AND a small sauna.\" · TURBONIA \"led by defending champion Max Overdrive, who has asked us to\n1116\t   call him 'The Defending Champion', even while he sleeps.\" · BONBONIA \"their uniforms are, legally, dessert.\" ·\n1117\t   VOLCANICA \"please don't stand too close. They're very warm people.\" · WAVELIA \"they arrived by boat. They prefer\n1118\t   it.\" · MOUNTOPIA \"they train at altitude, with less oxygen and more yodeling.\" · NEON REPUBLIC \"their uniforms\n1119\t   come with a firmware update.\" The player's nation enters last: \"And finally... the nation everyone came to see!\"\n1120\t4. **The flame (playable):** \"The final torchbearer is... YOU!\" A flaming javelin throw at the cauldron: hold\n1121\t   `action`, release in the gold zone of a `TimingBar`. Perfect: \"Bullseye! The cauldron is LIT!\" (+0.25 hype into\n1122\t   Day 1). Miss: the javelin hits the scoreboard, the scoreboard catches fire, \"...and the scoreboard is now the\n1123\t   cauldron. Olympiyikes!\" (it still lights).\n1124\t5. Max, in the tunnel (portrait close-up): \"Nice throw. Enjoy it. It's the closest you'll get to gold.\" Vera: \"Let\n1125\t   the Games... begin!\" Grand fireworks finale.\n1126\t\n1127\t**Medal ceremony** (each event, ~12 s, ✕ skips after 2 s): podium blocks 2–1–3 in the venue; athletes walk up; medals\n1128\tappear on their chests (a sprite at the neck joint); three flags rise on poles (tweens); the winner's **procedural\n1129\tanthem** (§9.5) plays; camera flashes; confetti in the winner's colors; one commentary line.\n1130\t\n1131\t**Closing ceremony** (~70 s, skippable): the final medal table on the jumbotron; all athletes dance in the infield\n1132\t(`cheer`, `wave`, spins); the \"Yikes reel\" counter for each nation; a snow cannon misfires and **puts out the\n1133\tcauldron** (\"OLYMPIYIKES!\"), then all eight star athletes relight it together with their torches; the motto appears:\n1134\t**FASTER. HIGHER. YIKES.**; the ending text; then the credits (paged).\n1135\t\n1136\t**Endings by your nation's final rank:**\n1137\t- 1st: \"Your nation tops the medal table! Back home they're renaming a mountain after you. It's a small mountain.\n1138\t  It's a hill. But it's YOUR hill.\"\n1139\t- 2nd–3rd: \"A podium nation! Respect. Max sends a fruit basket. It's mostly lemons.\"\n1140\t- 4th–8th: \"The medals didn't come, but the highlights did. Your yikes reel has four million views. Next Games, champ.\"\n1141\t- Multi-human Games add the **party champion** podium (by party points) before the ending.\n1142\t\n1143\t### 7.5 Records (in-world World Records, seeded into `oly:records`)\n1144\t\n1145\t| Event | WR | Holder | Qualify E / N / H |\n1146\t|---|---|---|---|\n1147\t| 100m Dash | 9.48 s | Max Overdrive (TRB) | 12.30 / 11.40 / 10.60 |\n1148\t| Javelin | 101.20 m | Blaze Cinderhart (VOL) | 58 / 72 / 82 m |\n1149\t| 50m Freestyle | 19.62 s | Marina Splashworth (WAV) | 25.5 / 23.2 / 21.6 |\n1150\t| 10m Diving | 338.40 | Coco Bonbon (BON) | 150 / 195 / 240 |\n1151\t| Archery | 60 (6 X) | Pixel Vance (NEO) | 40 / 48 / 53 |\n1152\t| Weightlifting | 270 kg | Blaze Cinderhart (VOL) | 200 / 225 / 245 kg |\n1153\t| Ski Jump | 296.4 (hill record 148.0 m) | Ingrid Snowcastle (FRM) | 160 / 210 / 245 |\n1154\t| Downhill | 47.62 s | Rocky Summit (MTP) | 58.0 / 52.5 / 49.0 |\n1155\t| Bobsled | 40.11 s per run (80.40 total) | Max Overdrive (TRB) | 92.0 / 86.0 / 82.0 |\n1156\t| Figure Skating | 228.56 | Coco Bonbon (BON) | 120 / 150 / 180 |\n1157\t| Curling, Ice Hockey | match events: \"most points in a final\" records (curling 6, hockey 7) | Rocky Summit / Max Overdrive | — |\n1158\t\n1159\tThe top-5 table of each event starts with the WR holder plus four seeded CPU marks a little below it.\n1160\t\n1161\t### 7.6 Commentary banks (write ≥ 160 lines in total; samples below set the voice)\n1162\t\n1163\tStyle: earnest Olympic broadcast (statistics, sentiment, national pride, \"up close and personal\") colliding with\n1164\tarcade bombast. Chip exaggerates; Vera undercuts with memories and dry wit. Short lines (≤ 70 characters each half).\n1165\tLines refer to athletes by `{name}` (or \"they\"), never a gendered pronoun: any athlete or player can be in any line.\n1166\t\n1167\t**Generic keys:** `start, lead, close, photo, wr, gr, pb, yikes, falsestart, foul, turbo, win, lose, last, comeback,\n1168\trivalBeat, rivalWins, idle (filler), dnf`.\n1169\t- start: Chip \"And they're OFF!\" · Chip \"Here we go, folks, the moment of truth!\" · Vera \"Breathe. That's all I ever told myself. Breathe and go.\"\n1170\t- lead: Chip \"{name} takes the lead for {nation}!\" · Chip \"{name} hits the front and the crowd is ON ITS FEET!\"\n1171\t- close: Chip \"Too close to call!\" · Vera \"Somebody fetch a ruler. A very small ruler.\"\n1172\t- photo: Chip \"We go to the PHOTO!\" · Vera \"Grab some popcorn, Chip. Photos take a while.\"\n1173\t- wr: Chip \"A NEW WORLD RECORD! Somebody call the record books! Somebody call the record books' MOTHER!\" · Vera \"I held a world record once. For eleven minutes. Cherish this.\"\n1174\t- yikes: Chip \"OLYMPIYIKES! That's going on the highlight reel for a thousand years!\" · Vera \"They're okay. The snow will need counseling.\" · Chip \"OH NO. Oh no no no. Oh... yes, actually, that was amazing.\"\n1175\t- falsestart: Chip \"Too eager! The gun hadn't even THOUGHT about firing!\" · Vera \"Nerves. I once false-started a press conference.\"\n1176\t- foul: Chip \"Over the line! The judges say NO!\" · Vera \"Lines are there for a reason. Mostly to be stepped on.\"\n1177\t- turbo: Chip \"{name} is ON FIRE!\" · Chip \"LOOK at that! Is that legal? Vera, is that legal?\" Vera \"Entirely. I checked in 1988.\"\n1178\t- win: Chip \"GOLD for {nation}!\" · Vera \"Somewhere, a small town is throwing a very loud party.\"\n1179\t- rivalWins: Max \"Second place is just first loser. That's a quote. Mine.\" · Max \"Did you see me? Everybody saw me.\"\n1180\t- rivalBeat: Max \"That was a fluke. A very fast fluke.\" · Max \"I let you have that one. For morale. Yours.\" · Max \"I'm not crying. Turbonians don't cry. We vent.\"\n1181\t- halftime (lead): Max \"Halftime means nothing. I'm a second-half athlete.\" · (trail) Max \"Halfway home, and already bored of winning.\"\n1182\t\n1183\t**Per event (≥ 8 each), examples:**\n1184\t- Sprint: \"Ten seconds. A whole life of training for ten seconds.\" · \"That's not a start, that's a LAUNCH!\"\n1185\t- Javelin: \"That javelin is still climbing!\" · \"It's left the stadium! Someone check the parking lot!\"\n1186\t- Swim: \"Perfect turn! Like a dolphin with a mortgage to pay!\" · Vera \"I could never do flip turns. I did flip-flops.\"\n1187\t- Diving: \"A rip entry! You could hear a pin drop. You could NOT hear that diver!\" · \"SLAP! You could hear that one in the next time zone.\"\n1188\t- Archery: \"Dead center! The wind didn't stand a chance.\" · Vera \"I tried archery once. The target was very relieved.\"\n1189\t- Weights: \"Look at that bar BEND!\" · \"Three white lights! GOOD LIFT!\"\n1190\t- Ski jump: \"{name} is flying! Still flying? STILL FLYING!\" · Vera \"Gravity always wins. It just takes its time.\"\n1191\t- Downhill: \"One hundred and thirty kilometers an hour down a frozen cliff. On purpose.\" · \"Into the netting! The netting has done its job!\"\n1192\t- Bobsled: \"Through the Omega like it isn't even there!\" · \"They're upside down! Still fast, though!\"\n1193\t- Figure: \"A quad! A QUAD YIKES!\" · Vera \"Grandpa would be whistling now.\"\n1194\t- Curling: \"HURRY HARD! HURRY HARD!\" · \"Double takeout! The house has been CLEARED!\"\n1195\t- Hockey: \"{name} shoots... and SCORES!\" · \"Into the glass! The glass is fine. The glass is always fine.\"\n1196\t\n1197\t**PA lines:** \"In lane {lane}... representing {nation}... {name}!\" · \"Ladies and gentlemen, a new World Record!\" ·\n1198\t\"Please rise for the anthem of {nation}.\"\n1199\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b1b95e-beb5-4384-ba72-665ccf7128b3","uuid":"f4970927-a5da-4353-a837-fa6e389c8112","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:41:32.789Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-074118__x0e4b02/work/PLAN.md","content":"  (good ≈ 4.9 s) → **load:** press `action` between 40 and 50 m (the \"LOAD\" zone flashes): in the zone no loss; early\n  ×0.95 speed; missed by 50 m → automatic load with −1.5 m/s and a **YIKES** (the brakeman flails, one leg out) →\n  **drive:** `a = g·sin(slope) − drag·v² − μ·g − scrape`; lateral `x'' = force·curveAt(z)·v² − steer·steerForce −\n  damp·x'`; the **groove** (ideal x for this curve and speed) shows as a glowing band on a U-shaped cross-section gauge;\n  |x − groove| > .25 → skid (−2%/s, sparks); |x| > 1.55 → **FLIP** (yikes: the sled slides on its roof for 2 s in\n  slow-mo, then rights itself at −35% speed) → finish and braking zone.\n- **Format:** attempts × 2 runs, combined time. Track record **40.11 s per run (MAX OVERDRIVE, TRB)**. Qualify (2 runs)\n  92.0 / 86.0 / 82.0. Points `6.4·(120 − total)^1.4`.\n- **CPU:** simulated; push rate by skill; groove error by skill.\n- **Turbo:** JET SLED: speed ×1.15 and auto-groove for 3 s, a jet flame from the tail.\n- **Tunables:** pushGain, loadZone, drag, curveForce, steerForce, grooveTolerance, flipHeight.\n- **Yikes:** LATE LOAD, FLIP. **Laurel:** ICE DANCER (a run with no skid or wall contact).\n- **Targets:** perfect bot 39.8–40.6 s per run; skill .5 ≈ 42.5–44; not steering in Omega → flip.\n- **Multiplayer:** alternate runs with the best run as a ghost; **hub:** yes (1 run).\n\n### 6.10 FIGURE SKATING (free skate) — winter · Glory Ice Palace · rhythm\n\n- **View:** `'threequarter'`; a 60×30 m rink (ice texture with scratches and reflections), boards with sponsor-free\n  banners, spotlights (ambient .45 + moving spots), the kiss & cry booth (bench, flowers, a giant plush mascot) where\n  scores are read, stands. The skater follows a closed `E.Path` (a large loop with a figure-8 crossing) at a pace tied\n  to the music.\n- **Music/chart:** original **\"Waltz of the Yikes\"** in 3/4 at 138 bpm, ~64 s (§9.1), played through `E.Rhythm`\n  (`lanes: ['left', 'down', 'up', 'right', 'action']`, holds on `action` are jumps). Windows perfect 45 / great 90 /\n  good 135 ms (×1.4 with Timing assist). Chart parts: Intro 4 bars · Step Sequence A 8 · Jump Combo 1 4 (two holds) ·\n  Spiral & Spin 8 · **Coach's Corner** 8 (4 bars of calls `c` from the coach, then you answer: PaRappa-style) · Step\n  Sequence B 8 (denser) · Jump Combo 2 4 (the 4-beat **QUAD YIKES** hold) · Finale 4 + the final-pose note. About 140\n  notes. Easy uses every other non-hold note.\n- **Highway:** a horizontal highway along the bottom third (notes travel right → left to a target line), 5 lanes\n  labeled with glyph icons (← ↓ ↑ → and ✕/Space), big notes (10 px), judgement words over the skater.\n- **Moves:** each judged note triggers a move on the rig: ←/→ edge steps and leans; ↑ spiral (one leg high behind,\n  arms out); ↓ sit spin (`rig.spin` accelerating); a hold = jump: take-off on the hold's head, airborne rotations\n  (`rig.spin` 4 turns/s, arms crossed), landing on release (great/perfect → clean landing with the free leg back; a\n  miss → **FALL**: slide on the backside, get up, combo lost).\n- **Scoring:** TES = Σ note value × (1 / .8 / .5 / 0) scaled so a perfect program = 130; PCS = 5 components (skating\n  skills, transitions, performance, composition, interpretation) 0–10 each from accuracy, max combo, falls and finish\n  pose, ×2 → max 100; falls −1 each. WR **228.56 (COCO BONBON, BON)**. Qualify 120 / 150 / 180. Points\n  `min(1200, 5.3·total)`.\n- **CPU:** simulated accuracy ~ skill ± noise → TES/PCS; the top 2 rivals' scores revealed in the kiss & cry.\n- **Turbo:** STAR POWER: 4 s, every judgement one level better, rainbow trail and glitter; afterwards the crowd throws\n  plush mascots onto the ice.\n- **Tunables:** perfectMs, greatMs, goodMs, lifeDrain, tesScale, pcsWeight.\n- **Yikes:** FALL. **Laurel:** FULL COMBO (no misses).\n- **Targets:** autoplay (`rh.hit` on every note) = full combo, ≈ 225–230; idle → life fails → program ends early with\n  low score but still a result.\n- **Multiplayer:** alternate programs; **hub:** no.\n\n### 6.11 CURLING (gold medal match) — winter · Glory Curling Club · aim + weight + sweep (physics)\n\n- **View:** `'topdown'`; an arcade sheet (meters): hack y = 0, near hog line 6, far hog line 22, tee (house center) 27,\n  back line 28.8, width 4.75 (x ±2.375), house radius 1.83 with rings (blue/white/red), stones r = 0.30 (arcade-sized,\n  granite with handles in the two nations' colors). M = 12; camera zoom 1.2 during the delivery, follows the stone,\n  2.5 over the house; a house-cam inset (top-right) always shows the house. Warm club lights, a scoreboard with ends.\n- **Match:** you vs one CPU nation (Mountopia unless you are Mountopia; then the best other curler), 2 ends × 4 stones\n  per team, alternating; hammer to the team that did not score (end 1 by coin flip from `rng('curling:hammer')`).\n- **Delivery:** (1) **AIM**: stick ←/→ (or the pointer) moves the skip's broom target across the house; (2) **CURL**:\n  `mashL` in-turn, `mashR` out-turn (an arrow on the stone; the first ~30% of the predicted path shows as dots);\n  (3) **WEIGHT**: `action` starts the slide; a weight meter oscillates 0 → 1 → 0 at 1.1 Hz *(T)* with bands GUARD\n  .25–.45, DRAW .45–.65, TAKEOUT .65–1.0; `action` again releases at that weight (`v0 = 1.8 + 2.0·w` m/s); releasing at\n  w ≥ .98 = over-throw slip (yikes, still delivered); (4) **SWEEP**: mash while the stone travels: sweep =\n  rate/8 Hz (clamped) cuts friction `μ = .019·(1 − .35·sweep)` and curl ×(1 − .5·sweep).\n- **Physics:** `E.Physics` with gravity 0 for collisions (`world.circle(..., { bounce: .85, friction: .1, bullet: true })`);\n  each step the game applies the ice: deceleration `μ·g` along the velocity and curl `a = spin·κ/(v + .5)`\n  (κ .05 *(T)*) across it. Stones that touch the side boards or pass the back line are removed; a stone that stops\n  before the far hog line is removed. Collisions above 2 m/s make sparks and a CLACK.\n- **Scoring per end:** the team with the stone nearest the button scores 1 per stone nearer than the opponent's\n  nearest (stones touching the house only). Ties after 2 ends → an extra end.\n- **CPU:** for its throw it evaluates 9 aims × 6 weights × 2 spins = 108 candidates, **each simulated in a sandbox\n  physics world** (12 per frame, so no hitch), scores the outcome (own shot stone in the house +, opponent shot\n  stones −, guards protecting own stones +), picks the best, then adds execution noise (aim ±.15 m, weight ±.06,\n  × (1 − skill)) and sweeps by its own plan.\n- **Turbo:** HYPER SWEEP: 3 s of maximum sweep regardless of mashing, glowing brooms and ice sparkles.\n- **Medals:** winner gold, loser silver, bronze from a simulated match between the next two nations.\n- **Tunables:** mu, sweepCut, curlK, weightHz, v0Base, v0Range, cpuNoise.\n- **Yikes:** OVER-THROW SLIP; a stone you throw that knocks your own shot stone out → \"OWN GOAL!\". **Laurel:** DOUBLE\n  TAKEOUT (two opponent stones removed by one throw).\n- **Targets:** a draw-weight throw with no sweep stops in the house (±1.5 m of the button); takeout weight on a stone\n  removes it; a .9-skill CPU beats a .3-skill CPU in ≥ 80% of 30 seeded matches; no frame spends > 8 ms on CPU sims.\n- **Multiplayer:** versus (P1 and P2 skip opposing teams) or co-op (P1 throws, P2 sweeps); **hub:** no.\n\n### 6.12 ICE HOCKEY FINAL (2-on-2 + goalies) — winter · Glory Arena · team action\n\n- **Start from `kits/sports.js`** (its cage, ball-as-Body, passes led to the teammate, `E.arc` lobs, shot meter with\n  aftertouch curl, formation AI, `game.allowJoin({ max: 4 })`) and turn it into hockey: the pitch becomes a rink\n  (ice floor texture, red center line, blue lines, faceoff circles, creases), the boards get glass on top (`h` higher,\n  translucent top band), nets 3 tiles wide with posts; the ball becomes a **puck** (flat sprite, `bounce` 0 on the\n  ice, board restitution .65, low friction); players skate with momentum (accel 220 u/s², max 105 u/s, glide);\n  add an **automatic goalie** per side (a Body on an arc in its crease that moves toward the puck–goal line at a\n  skill-limited speed and saves on contact, sometimes freezing the puck for a faceoff). Arena: dark with spotlights,\n  a center-hung jumbotron, goal lights and horn, organ music.\n- **Match:** your nation vs the rival (Turbonia, or §5.6's rival if you are Turbonia), 2 periods × 90 s of running clock *(T)*, a resurfacing machine\n  crossing at intermission, sudden-death overtime 90 s, then a **shootout** (3 rounds then sudden death: a skater\n  starts at center with the puck, 6 s to shoot, vs the goalie).\n- **Controls:** skate (stick), `mashL` pass (to the teammate the stick points at, led), `action` hold = shot meter,\n  release = shoot (stick aims; push sideways just after = curl), `mashR` = **check** without the puck (a shoulder\n  lunge: a hit knocks the opponent down 1 s, the puck squirts loose; into the boards → the glass shakes, crowd \"OOOH\")\n  or switch to the teammate nearer the puck when far, `alt` = skate burst (stamina bar), `turbo` = **ON FIRE** (when\n  the hype is full, or automatically after 3 straight good plays: the puck burns, shots ×1.4 speed, goalies react 50%\n  slower, until a goal or 8 s). Mouse: left hold/release shoots toward the cursor, right passes toward it.\n- **Hype:** completed passes, hits, shots on goal, saves avoided.\n- **Medals:** winner gold, loser silver; bronze simulated.\n- **Tunables:** periodLength, skateAccel, skateMax, shotPower, puckFriction, goalieSpeed, checkPower.\n- **Yikes:** CHECKED INTO THE GLASS (when you get hit), OWN GOAL. **Laurel:** HAT TRICK (one skater scores 3).\n- **Targets:** bot vs bot (skill .9 vs .3) wins ≥ 80% of 30 seeded matches; goals happen (≥ 1 per period on average\n  at equal skill .7); a shot on an empty net scores; checks knock down.\n- **Multiplayer:** up to 4: 2v2 versus or co-op vs the CPU; **hub:** no.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Content\n\n**Originality rules:** fictional nations, athletes, venues and mascot; no Olympic rings or official emblems, no real\nanthems, fanfares or broadcast themes; in-game text says \"the Games\". The hub `source` meta may say \"The Olympic\nGames\" (it is descriptive).\n\n### 7.1 Nations and their star athletes (8 = 8 lanes)\n\n| Code | Nation | Colors (a / b / c) | Flag (drawn in code) | Athlete | Rig (`new E.Humanoid`) | Voice | Personality |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| SUN | SUNVALE | `#f2b632` gold / `#2f7fe0` sky / `#ffffff` | sky field, gold sun disc with 8 rays | **DASH GOLDBERRY** | heroic, hair short `#3a2414`, skin `#8d5a3b` | pitch 1.0, speed 1.1 | sunny optimist |\n| FRM | FROSTMARK | `#f4f8ff` snow / `#2fa8d8` glacier / `#1a3a6a` navy | white field, glacier snowflake, navy border | **INGRID SNOWCASTLE** | heroic, ponytail `#f3e6c0`, skin `#f2d4c4` | 1.3, 0.9 | deadpan |\n| TRB | TURBONIA | `#e23b2e` red / `#1e2026` carbon / `#ffd23a` yellow | diagonal red/carbon split, yellow lightning bolt | **MAX OVERDRIVE** (the rival) | heroic, spiky `#141414`, skin `#c88a5e`, red headband (`hat: band`) | 0.9, 1.25 | arrogant, loud |\n| BON | BONBONIA | `#ff7fb8` pink / `#6fe0c0` mint / `#ffffff` | vertical candy stripes, small heart | **COCO BONBON** | heroic, long `#ff9ad0`, skin `#f5c9a8`, `face: { eyes: 'big' }` | 1.45, 1.05 | theatrical |\n| VOL | VOLCANICA | `#ff6a1a` lava / `#3a2e2e` basalt / `#ffd0a0` ember | basalt field, orange volcano, yellow eruption dot | **BLAZE CINDERHART** | **bulky**, bald, skin `#6a4028` | 0.7, 0.85 | gentle giant |\n| WAV | WAVELIA | `#1fa8a0` teal / `#0e4a6a` deep / `#e8fbf7` foam | teal field, three white waves | **MARINA SPLASHWORTH** | heroic, short `#24160e`, skin `#5a3420` | 1.25, 0.95 | calm poet |\n| MTP | MOUNTOPIA | `#6a3fc8` purple / `#c8ccd8` silver / `#ffffff` | purple field, white peak, 3 silver stars | **ROCKY SUMMIT** | heroic, short `#8a5a2a`, skin `#e0b090`, beanie (`hat: cap`) | 0.95, 1.0 | folksy |\n| NEO | NEON REPUBLIC | `#e83ae0` magenta / `#14102a` night / `#3ae8f0` cyan | night field, cyan ring, magenta star | **PIXEL VANCE** | heroic, spiky `#3ae8f0`, skin `#f0c8a8` | 1.15, 1.2 | gamer slang |\n\nOutfits come from `O.makeRig(nation, sport)`: singlet + shorts (track, weights: belt), swim cap + goggles (pool),\nracing suit + helmet + goggles (downhill, bobsled, ski jump bib with number), sparkly costume (figure skating: the\nnation's colors + `trim` sequins), sweater (curling), padded jersey + helmet (hockey), team tracksuit (ceremonies).\nEvery rig size 1.25 (bulky Blaze 1.3), with the nation's 4–6 colors (never engine defaults).\n\n**CPU skill per event** (0–1; effective skill per §5.6):\n\n| | 100m | Jav | Swim | Dive | Arch | Wts | SkiJ | Down | Bob | Fig | Curl | Hock |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| SUN | .92 | .85 | .70 | .62 | .66 | .70 | .60 | .65 | .78 | .60 | .62 | .74 |\n| FRM | .70 | .74 | .66 | .68 | .80 | .66 | .94 | .92 | .74 | .76 | .80 | .78 |\n| TRB | .93 | .90 | .78 | .70 | .72 | .82 | .80 | .84 | .95 | .62 | .66 | .93 |\n| BON | .66 | .62 | .80 | .92 | .74 | .58 | .70 | .68 | .62 | .95 | .70 | .64 |\n| VOL | .72 | .88 | .62 | .55 | .64 | .95 | .62 | .70 | .86 | .52 | .82 | .88 |\n| WAV | .74 | .68 | .95 | .88 | .70 | .64 | .66 | .62 | .64 | .80 | .72 | .66 |\n| MTP | .68 | .72 | .64 | .60 | .86 | .74 | .82 | .88 | .80 | .66 | .93 | .80 |\n| NEO | .78 | .70 | .72 | .74 | .93 | .60 | .74 | .76 | .70 | .82 | .76 | .84 |\n\n**Teammates** (bobsled brakeman, hockey partner and goalie, curling team), generated rigs in team colors:\nSUN Sunny Ray, Bo Marigold, Lux Daybright · FRM Sven Driftholm, Liv Hailstrom, Nils Frostby · TRB Rev Throttleton,\nNitro Vex, Gigi Torque · BON Taffy Swirl, Praline Dupree, Nougat Fizz · VOL Ash Kindleton, Ember Stone, Obsidia Crag ·\nWAV Coral Finley, Tide Brennan, Kai Seaborne · MTP Edelweiss Vogt, Cliff Hangar, Scree Halvorsen · NEO Byte Ortega,\nGlitch Kowalski, Vector Nakamura.\n\n**\"Up Close & Personal\" bios** (one per day card, rotating; the player's own athlete gets one on Day 1):\n- **Dash Goldberry (SUN):** \"Dash grew up on a farm in rural Sunvale, chasing the family's prize ostrich to school\n  every morning. The ostrich never once let him win. Today, he runs for Daisy.\"\n- **Ingrid Snowcastle (FRM):** \"Ingrid's grandmother taught her to ski jump off the roof of the family sauna. The sauna\n  has since been rebuilt. Twice.\"\n- **Max Overdrive (TRB):** \"Defending champion in, quote, 'everything'. Max has never lost a race, a staring contest,\n  or an argument with a mirror. His hobbies include winning and describing winning.\"\n- **Coco Bonbon (BON):** \"Coco skates every program to the songs her grandfather whistled. She says she can still hear\n  him in the crowd. Usually slightly off-key.\"\n- **Blaze Cinderhart (VOL):** \"Every winter morning, Blaze lifts the family car out of a volcanic ash drift. The car is\n  fine. The car is extremely well-defined.\"\n- **Marina Splashworth (WAV):** \"Born on a houseboat, Marina didn't touch dry land until she was four. On land she still\n  walks like the deck is moving. In the water... poetry.\"\n- **Rocky Summit (MTP):** \"Rocky's village sits so high that the mail arrives by curling stone. He has been sweeping since\n  before he could walk. His first word was 'HARD!'\"\n- **Pixel Vance (NEO):** \"Pixel learned archery from an arcade cabinet and has never seen daylight without sunglasses.\n  Pixel's coach is a toaster named Gary. Gary believes in Pixel.\"\n\n### 7.2 Venues (levels)\n\n| Venue | Events / scenes | View | Light | Key art (all drawn in code; generic props from the engine library/asset store) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Glory Stadium** (Sunny Bay) | 100m, Javelin; opening & closing ceremonies; stadium podiums | brawler | day (events), night + fireworks (ceremonies) | red 8-lane track with lane numbers, infield grass with mown stripes, 3-tier stands + crowd, the cauldron tower, jumbotron, finish gantry & clock, flags of the 8 nations on the rim, the blimp, parking lot past the wall |\n| **Splash Palace** | 50m Free, Diving | brawler / side | indoor bright, caustics | pool, lane ropes, blocks, flags line, the dive tower, judges' table, windows onto the beach, jumbotron |\n| **Bullseye Lawn** | Archery | overlay + side inset | sunny, breezy | target faces, palms, the sea, wind flags, shade tent |\n| **Iron Hall** | Weightlifting | brawler | dark, two spotlights | platform, chalk bowl, referee lights, plate rack, dim crowd |\n| **Mount Glory Jumping Hill** | Ski Jump | side | night floodlights, light snow | tower, in-run, K/HS lines, distance boards, out-run crowd with cowbells and flags |\n| **The Yikes Face** | Downhill | E.Road | bright day, sun glare, light snow | piste, orange netting, pines, start hut, ice tunnel, jumps, finish arch, grandstand |\n| **Glory Ice Track** | Bobsled | E.Road | dusk, floodlights | ice channel, named curve signs, tunnels, timing boards |\n| **Glory Ice Palace** | Figure Skating | threequarter | spotlights | rink, kiss & cry, flowers, plush rain |\n| **Glory Curling Club** | Curling | topdown | warm indoor | sheet, houses, scoreboard, pennants |\n| **Glory Arena** | Ice Hockey | threequarter | dark arena + spots | rink, glass, center jumbotron cube, goal lights, organ loft |\n\nUse `node vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/tools/asset-find.mjs \"<thing>\"` for generic props (benches, fences, pines,\nsnow blocks, banners, lamps, flags: the `kenney-holiday`, `kenney-nature`, `ambientcg` sets have snow, pines, ice and\nfences); cut the few you use into a set of your own with `tools/asset-set.mjs` and inline it.\n\n### 7.3 Story structure (The Games)\n\n| When | Beat | Content |\n|---|---|---|\n| Start | **Opening ceremony** | §7.4 |\n| Day 1 (before) | Max's welcome | in the call room: \"Lane four? Cute. I'm in lane five. Lane five is where legends warm up.\" |\n| After Day 2 | **Mascot incident** | Yikesy \"test-jumps\" the ski jump: a 6 s cutscene (the Blob launched, spinning, lands in a snowbank head-first). Chip: \"The mascot has... the mascot has set a personal best!\" Vera: \"And a personal worst. Simultaneously.\" |\n| After Day 4 | Curling chat | Rocky: \"Back home we curl to settle arguments. Mostly about curling.\" |\n| After Day 6 | **HALFTIME REPORT** | medal table + banter; Yikesy appears, dripping (\"rescued from the pool filter\"); Max line depends on standings (§7.6) |\n| After Day 8 | Coco's moment | Coco (any result): \"Grandpa, that one was for you.\" Vera, quietly: \"...Give me a second, Chip.\" |\n| After Day 10 | Sled scandal | Vera: \"Turbonia's sled has a spoiler. And a cup holder.\" Max: \"It's called aerodynamic hospitality.\" |\n| Day 12 (before) | **THE FINAL** | both anthems tease; Max: \"Two nations. One puck. Zero chance. For you.\" |\n| After Day 12 | Sportsmanship | win: Max: \"...Good game. Next Games I'm bringing two helmets. One for my ego.\" · loss: Max: \"Good game. You were almost me.\" |\n| End | **Closing ceremony** | §7.4; ending by rank |\n| Dynamic | Rival reactions | after any event with you and Max both in the top 4: a line from the bank (beat him / he beat you) |\n| Dynamic | Records & yikes | a WR by you → Vera's sentimental line; 5+ yikes → Vera: \"Statistically, the most entertaining athlete in Games history.\" |\n\n### 7.4 Ceremony scripts\n\n**Opening ceremony** (Glory Stadium at night, ~60 s, hold ✕ 1 s to skip):\n1. Fireworks over the twin city (the ski jump floodlit beyond the stadium rim). PA (echo): \"Ladies and gentlemen...\n   welcome to the Games of Mount Glory and Sunny Bay!\"\n2. Chip: \"Good evening, everybody! For the first time in history, the Summer and Winter Games are happening at the\n   SAME TIME, in the SAME PLACE!\" Vera: \"Some called it impossible. Others called it a scheduling error. Tonight we\n   call it... OLYMPIYIKES!\"\n3. **Parade of nations** (rigs marching in tracksuits behind a flag bearer, crowd waving that nation's colors), one\n   line each: SUNVALE \"where the sun never sets and the sunscreen budget is classified.\" · FROSTMARK \"their flag bearer\n   is carrying the flag AND a small sauna.\" · TURBONIA \"led by defending champion Max Overdrive, who has asked us to\n   call him 'The Defending Champion', even while he sleeps.\" · BONBONIA \"their uniforms are, legally, dessert.\" ·\n   VOLCANICA \"please don't stand too close. They're very warm people.\" · WAVELIA \"they arrived by boat. They prefer\n   it.\" · MOUNTOPIA \"they train at altitude, with less oxygen and more yodeling.\" · NEON REPUBLIC \"their uniforms\n   come with a firmware update.\" The player's nation enters last: \"And finally... the nation everyone came to see!\"\n4. **The flame (playable):** \"The final torchbearer is... YOU!\" A flaming javelin throw at the cauldron: hold\n   `action`, release in the gold zone of a `TimingBar`. Perfect: \"Bullseye! The cauldron is LIT!\" (+0.25 hype into\n   Day 1). Miss: the javelin hits the scoreboard, the scoreboard catches fire, \"...and the scoreboard is now the\n   cauldron. Olympiyikes!\" (it still lights).\n5. Max, in the tunnel (portrait close-up): \"Nice throw. Enjoy it. It's the closest you'll get to gold.\" Vera: \"Let\n   the Games... begin!\" Grand fireworks finale.\n\n**Medal ceremony** (each event, ~12 s, ✕ skips after 2 s): podium blocks 2–1–3 in the venue; athletes walk up; medals\nappear on their chests (a sprite at the neck joint); three flags rise on poles (tweens); the winner's **procedural\nanthem** (§9.5) plays; camera flashes; confetti in the winner's colors; one commentary line.\n\n**Closing ceremony** (~70 s, skippable): the final medal table on the jumbotron; all athletes dance in the infield\n(`cheer`, `wave`, spins); the \"Yikes reel\" counter for each nation; a snow cannon misfires and **puts out the\ncauldron** (\"OLYMPIYIKES!\"), then all eight star athletes relight it together with their torches; the motto appears:\n**FASTER. HIGHER. YIKES.**; the ending text; then the credits (paged).\n\n**Endings by your nation's final rank:**\n- 1st: \"Your nation tops the medal table! Back home they're renaming a mountain after you. It's a small mountain.\n  It's a hill. But it's YOUR hill.\"\n- 2nd–3rd: \"A podium nation! Respect. Max sends a fruit basket. It's mostly lemons.\"\n- 4th–8th: \"The medals didn't come, but the highlights did. Your yikes reel has four million views. Next Games, champ.\"\n- Multi-human Games add the **party champion** podium (by party points) before the ending.\n\n### 7.5 Records (in-world World Records, seeded into `oly:records`)\n\n| Event | WR | Holder | Qualify E / N / H |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 100m Dash | 9.48 s | Max Overdrive (TRB) | 12.30 / 11.40 / 10.60 |\n| Javelin | 101.20 m | Blaze Cinderhart (VOL) | 58 / 72 / 82 m |\n| 50m Freestyle | 19.62 s | Marina Splashworth (WAV) | 25.5 / 23.2 / 21.6 |\n| 10m Diving | 338.40 | Coco Bonbon (BON) | 150 / 195 / 240 |\n| Archery | 60 (6 X) | Pixel Vance (NEO) | 40 / 48 / 53 |\n| Weightlifting | 270 kg | Blaze Cinderhart (VOL) | 200 / 225 / 245 kg |\n| Ski Jump | 296.4 (hill record 148.0 m) | Ingrid Snowcastle (FRM) | 160 / 210 / 245 |\n| Downhill | 47.62 s | Rocky Summit (MTP) | 58.0 / 52.5 / 49.0 |\n| Bobsled | 40.11 s per run (80.40 total) | Max Overdrive (TRB) | 92.0 / 86.0 / 82.0 |\n| Figure Skating | 228.56 | Coco Bonbon (BON) | 120 / 150 / 180 |\n| Curling, Ice Hockey | match events: \"most points in a final\" records (curling 6, hockey 7) | Rocky Summit / Max Overdrive | — |\n\nThe top-5 table of each event starts with the WR holder plus four seeded CPU marks a little below it.\n\n### 7.6 Commentary banks (write ≥ 160 lines in total; samples below set the voice)\n\nStyle: earnest Olympic broadcast (statistics, sentiment, national pride, \"up close and personal\") colliding with\narcade bombast. Chip exaggerates; Vera undercuts with memories and dry wit. Short lines (≤ 70 characters each half).\nLines refer to athletes by `{name}` (or \"they\"), never a gendered pronoun: any athlete or player can be in any line.\n\n**Generic keys:** `start, lead, close, photo, wr, gr, pb, yikes, falsestart, foul, turbo, win, lose, last, comeback,\nrivalBeat, rivalWins, idle (filler), dnf`.\n- start: Chip \"And they're OFF!\" · Chip \"Here we go, folks, the moment of truth!\" · Vera \"Breathe. That's all I ever told myself. Breathe and go.\"\n- lead: Chip \"{name} takes the lead for {nation}!\" · Chip \"{name} hits the front and the crowd is ON ITS FEET!\"\n- close: Chip \"Too close to call!\" · Vera \"Somebody fetch a ruler. A very small ruler.\"\n- photo: Chip \"We go to the PHOTO!\" · Vera \"Grab some popcorn, Chip. Photos take a while.\"\n- wr: Chip \"A NEW WORLD RECORD! Somebody call the record books! Somebody call the record books' MOTHER!\" · Vera \"I held a world record once. For eleven minutes. Cherish this.\"\n- yikes: Chip \"OLYMPIYIKES! That's going on the highlight reel for a thousand years!\" · Vera \"They're okay. The snow will need counseling.\" · Chip \"OH NO. Oh no no no. Oh... yes, actually, that was amazing.\"\n- falsestart: Chip \"Too eager! The gun hadn't even THOUGHT about firing!\" · Vera \"Nerves. I once false-started a press conference.\"\n- foul: Chip \"Over the line! The judges say NO!\" · Vera \"Lines are there for a reason. Mostly to be stepped on.\"\n- turbo: Chip \"{name} is ON FIRE!\" · Chip \"LOOK at that! Is that legal? Vera, is that legal?\" Vera \"Entirely. I checked in 1988.\"\n- win: Chip \"GOLD for {nation}!\" · Vera \"Somewhere, a small town is throwing a very loud party.\"\n- rivalWins: Max \"Second place is just first loser. That's a quote. Mine.\" · Max \"Did you see me? Everybody saw me.\"\n- rivalBeat: Max \"That was a fluke. A very fast fluke.\" · Max \"I let you have that one. For morale. Yours.\" · Max \"I'm not crying. Turbonians don't cry. We vent.\"\n- halftime (lead): Max \"Halftime means nothing. I'm a second-half athlete.\" · (trail) Max \"Halfway home, and already bored of winning.\"\n\n**Per event (≥ 8 each), examples:**\n- Sprint: \"Ten seconds. A whole life of training for ten seconds.\" · \"That's not a start, that's a LAUNCH!\"\n- Javelin: \"That javelin is still climbing!\" · \"It's left the stadium! Someone check the parking lot!\"\n- Swim: \"Perfect turn! Like a dolphin with a mortgage to pay!\" · Vera \"I could never do flip turns. I did flip-flops.\"\n- Diving: \"A rip entry! You could hear a pin drop. You could NOT hear that diver!\" · \"SLAP! You could hear that one in the next time zone.\"\n- Archery: \"Dead center! The wind didn't stand a chance.\" · Vera \"I tried archery once. The target was very relieved.\"\n- Weights: \"Look at that bar BEND!\" · \"Three white lights! GOOD LIFT!\"\n- Ski jump: \"{name} is flying! Still flying? STILL FLYING!\" · Vera \"Gravity always wins. It just takes its time.\"\n- Downhill: \"One hundred and thirty kilometers an hour down a frozen cliff. On purpose.\" · \"Into the netting! The netting has done its job!\"\n- Bobsled: \"Through the Omega like it isn't even there!\" · \"They're upside down! Still fast, though!\"\n- Figure: \"A quad! A QUAD YIKES!\" · Vera \"Grandpa would be whistling now.\"\n- Curling: \"HURRY HARD! HURRY HARD!\" · \"Double takeout! The house has been CLEARED!\"\n- Hockey: \"{name} shoots... and SCORES!\" · \"Into the glass! The glass is fine. The glass is always fine.\"\n\n**PA lines:** \"In lane {lane}... representing {nation}... {name}!\" · \"Ladies and gentlemen, a new World Record!\" ·\n\"Please rise for the anthem of {nation}.\"\n","numLines":300,"startLine":900,"totalLines":1723}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Likd9pdj3R4VWr4fEjciUo","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi4bqnByJyuLK5xV8yCS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RepwPhEUDP1CCtxow5ken2","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-074118__x0e4b02/work/PLAN.md","offset":1200,"limit":300},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10838,"cache_read_input_tokens":22643,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10838},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b1b95e-beb5-4384-ba72-665ccf7128b3","uuid":"ef72c77c-df23-40df-b873-13c178f98030","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:41:33.556Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi4bqVaHhUf9bqcq8gxF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01RepwPhEUDP1CCtxow5ken2":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-074118__x0e4b02/work/PLAN.md","offset":1200,"limit":300}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RepwPhEUDP1CCtxow5ken2","type":"tool_result","content":"1200\t### 7.7 Pictograms, emblem, flags\n1201\t\n1202\t- **12 pictograms** (16×16 `E.sprite` strings; white figure on a rounded tile, summer coral `#ff6b4a`, winter ice-blue\n1203\t  `#3fa8e8`; drawn ×2 or ×3 on cards): sprint (leaning runner), javelin (arm back, diagonal shaft), swim (head and\n1204\t  arm arc over waves), diving (inverted figure over a splash), archery (figure drawing a bow), weights (bar overhead),\n1205\t  ski jump (forward-leaning figure on long V skis), downhill (tucked skier, diagonal), bobsled (sled with two\n1206\t  helmets), figure (spinning figure, one leg out), curling (stone + broom), hockey (stick + puck + skater). Used on the\n1207\t  schedule, event cards, results, Single Event tiles, the HUD and the records tabs.\n1208\t- **Emblem \"the Yikes Flame\":** a flame split down the middle, orange (summer) and ice-blue (winter), inside a gold\n1209\t  laurel wreath. Title, ceremonies, hub card, favicon (an inline SVG data URI of the same shape).\n1210\t- **Flags:** `O.Art.flag(g, x, y, w, h, nation, wave)` draws each flag from its spec with a 2-step cloth wave and\n1211\t  shading (`E.tones`).\n1212\t\n1213\t### 7.8 Items, power-ups, opponents and hazards\n1214\t\n1215\t| Kind | Content |\n1216\t|---|---|\n1217\t| **Equipment (items)** | spikes and blocks, javelin, swim cap and goggles, bow and arrows, barbell and color-coded plates, jump skis, downhill skis and poles, the two-man sled, curling stones and brooms, hockey sticks, puck and nets, the torch. Drawn by `O.Gear` (§8.2) in the nation's colors |\n1218\t| **Golden gear (unlock)** | winning gold in an event turns that event's equipment golden for that nation in later plays (saved in the cabinet); shown in Records → Cabinet |\n1219\t| **Power-ups** | YIKES TURBO (one per event, §6: HYPER ARM, DOLPHIN MODE, SLOW-MO SUPREMACY, EAGLE EYE, IRON WILL, ROCKET SKIS, AVALANCHE, JET SLED, STAR POWER, HYPER SWEEP, ON FIRE and the sprint's TURBO); sympathy hype after a yikes; speed gates in the downhill |\n1220\t| **Collectibles** | medals (cabinet), 12 laurels, world records and top-5 places with initials |\n1221\t| **Opponents (\"enemies\")** | the 7 CPU nations' stars with per-event skills (§7.1); the rival Max Overdrive (+0.03, always shown live); CPU curling skips that plan shots by simulation; the Turbonia hockey team and the goalies |\n1222\t| **Hazards** | the starter's gun (false starts), the foul line, wind and gusts, the pool wall, the take-off table's edge, gravity under a loaded bar, orange netting, crests that launch you, the tunnel's ice, banked walls that flip a sled, the hog and back lines, the boards and the glass |\n1223\t\n1224\t---\n1225\t\n1226\t## 8. Art and animation\n1227\t\n1228\t### 8.1 Look (the engine's native style, pushed to its look target)\n1229\t\n1230\tFollow every step of API.md's \"Look target\": `res: 'ps1'` + `expand`, HD Humanoids at size 1.25 dressed in each\n1231\tnation's palette, a backdrop or painted horizon behind every view, textured floors (`floorTex` functions for track,\n1232\tgrass, pool water, ice with scratches, snow with sparkle), 3–8 props per screen (`r.prop`/`r.shape`: flags, banners,\n1233\tlamps, benches, pines, fences, barriers, cameras on tripods, medal tables), effects on every impact, `E.font.title`\n1234\tlogos, lights in every scene, faces in every dialog (portraits). The season split in palettes: summer warm (gold,\n1235\tcoral, sky), winter cool (ice blue, violet, white) with warm floodlights; UI panels navy `#0c1028` with gold `#f2b632`\n1236\ttrim. Screenshots should compare with the best PS1-era 2D, not NES.\n1237\t\n1238\t### 8.2 Pose layer (`O.Pose`, src/06-pose.js) and the engine's pose hook\n1239\t\n1240\t- The Humanoid already animates runs, jumps (`air`), crouch, kneel, cheer, wave, hips, down, die, rolls (`flip`),\n1241\t  climbs, landings (`rig.land`) and every move in `E.MOVES` (use `new E.Attack('throw')` for the javelin release,\n1242\t  `'bash'` for hockey checks, `'twohand'` for slapshots, `'cast'` for the torch raise). **Use these first.**\n1243\t- For what it lacks, `O.Pose.set(rig, name, params)` installs `rig.post = (rig, J) => ...` (engine change 5). A pose\n1244\t  edits joints in the rig's own frame `[forward, right, up]`: `J.hipC, hipL/R, kneeL/R, footL/R, shC, shL/R, elbowL/R,\n1245\t  handL/R, head`, using helpers `armTo(J, side, target, hint)` and `legTo(J, side, target, hint)` (two-bone IK with\n1246\t  `E.ik3` and the rig's limb lengths `rig.o.armUpper/armLower/legUpper/legLower`), `lean(J, fwd, side)`,\n1247\t  `look(J, dir)`. Poses blend in/out with a weight (ease .15 s). Whole-body rotations set `rig.bodyPitch`,\n1248\t  `rig.bodyRoll`, `rig.pivot`.\n1249\t- **Pose list** (each previewable in the Pose Lab, `#poselab`): `blocks` (sprint crouch, hands on the line), `set`\n1250\t  (hips up), `dip` (torso thrown forward), `javCarry` (right hand above the shoulder), `javWithdraw`, `swimCrawl(phase,\n1251\t  breath)` (prone via bodyPitch 90°, arms on circles around the shoulders, flutter kick, head turned on breaths),\n1252\t  `diveStart(u)`, `flipTurn(u)`, `armsUp` (diving stance), `tuck`, `pike`, `layout`, `entry` (hands joined over the\n1253\t  head), `bellyFlop`, `archerDraw(u)` (bow arm extended to the target, string hand to the jaw), `archerRelease`,\n1254\t  `liftSetup`, `liftClean(h)` (hands on the bar, bar height h), `liftRack`, `liftJerk(u)` (split stance, arms locked\n1255\t  overhead), `liftDrop(u)`, `skiTuck`, `skiFlight(α)` (V-style: straight body leaning over the skis, arms back),\n1256\t  `telemark`, `tumble(t)`, `bobPush`, `bobPilot`, `bobBrake`, `skateGlide`, `skateSpiral`, `sitSpin`, `skateJump`\n1257\t  (arms crossed), `skateLand`, `curlSlide` (deep lunge, hand on the stone), `sweep(phase)`, `skipPoint`,\n1258\t  `hockeyStride`, `stickHandle`, `goalieStance`, `kneeSlide` (goal celebration), `flagCarry`, `torchRaise`, `bowHead`\n1259\t  (receiving a medal), `medalBite`, `podiumWave`, `faceplant` (built-in `flip` roll + `down`).\n1260\t- **Gear** (`O.Gear`, drawn with `r.queue` at projected joint positions so it depth-sorts with the rig): javelin,\n1261\t  bow + string + arrow, barbell + plates (ellipses facing the camera) with bend, skis (two long quads from the feet\n1262\t  along the ski direction, V in flight), poles, helmets/goggles, swim cap/goggles, bobsled (boxes through the view,\n1263\t  like `kits/kart.js` `box()`), curling stone and broom, hockey stick (line from hands to a blade on the ice) and puck,\n1264\t  medals, flags on poles, torch (with `particles.fire` and a light).\n1265\t- **Rear view for E.Road events:** `new E.View('rear', 'Rear', 0, 18, 1.6, 1)`; a rig with `facing: Math.PI / 2` faces\n1266\t  into the screen. Draw it inside the road's overlay at the skier's screen point (`rig.draw(g, sx, sy, REAR)`); for\n1267\t  ghosts and other sleds at a distance, cache views per quantized scale (`E.View(..., scale)` at 12 steps) as\n1268\t  `m7.view(k)` does in the kart kit.\n1269\t- **Check every pose** with `tools/filmstrip.mjs <page>#poselab/<pose> --steps \"wait:300 rec:16:2\" --seed 1`: no\n1270\t  joints through the body, no snapping when blending, readable silhouettes at 1×.\n1271\t\n1272\t### 8.3 Effects\n1273\t\n1274\tFireworks (`particles.explosion(..., { debris: false })` + colored `glints`, launched with trails), confetti (`bits`\n1275\tin nation colors), splashes (blue/white `bit` particles sized by entry error; a rip makes only bubbles), snow spray\n1276\t(white dust on carves and crashes), sparks (sled scrapes, curling clacks, skate stops), chalk dust, camera flashes\n1277\t(white glints in the stands), turbo flames (`fire` + emissive glow), the gun's smoke puff, speed lines and sun\n1278\tglare overlays on the road events, the \"YIKES!\" stamp, the WR burst (rays + stars), the plush rain.\n1279\t\n1280\t### 8.4 Lighting per venue\n1281\t\n1282\t`game.lights.enabled = true` in every venue's enter: stadium day ambient .85 warm; stadium night .4 + stadium\n1283\tfloodlights + fireworks flashes; pool .8 cool + caustic glows; lawn .9; Iron Hall .35 + two warm spots; ski jump .35\n1284\t+ floodlights along the hill; ice palace .45 + moving colored spots; curling .6 warm; arena .4 + spots + goal light\n1285\tflash. E.Road scenes draw as overlays (unlit): bake the mood into their colors and add additive glow sprites.\n1286\t\n1287\t### 8.5 The mascot: YIKESY\n1288\t\n1289\tAn `E.Blob({ R: 9, ears: 'cat', feet: true, mouth: true, colors: { base: '#f8f8ff', dk: '#d8e2f0', lt: '#ffffff' } })`\n1290\t(a round snow-yeti) with a flame tuft on its head (fire particles + glow) and a half-orange/half-blue scarf drawn on\n1291\ttop. Appears on the title, in ceremonies, story beats, the attract mode, the curling scoreboard, as plush toys on the\n1292\tice, and in the Pose Lab. Voice: squeaky gibberish (pitch 1.9).\n1293\t\n1294\t---\n1295\t\n1296\t## 9. Audio (all in code)\n1297\t\n1298\t### 9.1 Music (engine songs `{ bpm, steps: 4, tracks }`, every one original)\n1299\t\n1300\t| Id | Where | Feel | BPM | Notes |\n1301\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1302\t| `title` | title, menus' first entry | heroic brass fanfare with a comic chromatic \"yikes\" slide, then triumph | 120 | motif below |\n1303\t| `menu` | main menu, setup screens | bright funk-pop loop | 112 | |\n1304\t| `parade` | opening ceremony | march, snare rolls | 116 | |\n1305\t| `sprint` | 100m | chiptune drum & bass | 172 | `hype` drum layer |\n1306\t| `javelin` | javelin | funky groove | 104 | |\n1307\t| `swim` | 50m free | bubbly arpeggios | 128 | |\n1308\t| `diving` | diving | sparse, timpani, suspense | 90 | |\n1309\t| `archery` | archery | tense minimal + heartbeat kick | 80 | heartbeat speeds with `hr` |\n1310\t| `iron` | weightlifting | heavy rock riff (saw bass) | 96 | |\n1311\t| `alpine` | ski jump | floodlit alpine pulse, bells | 124 | |\n1312\t| `yikesface` | downhill | driving rock | 150 | |\n1313\t| `icesurf` | bobsled | surf rock | 160 | |\n1314\t| `waltz` | figure skating | \"Waltz of the Yikes\", 3/4 (bars of 12 steps) | 138 | the rhythm chart's song |\n1315\t| `lounge` | curling | lounge jazz (swing feel) | 92 | |\n1316\t| `organ` | hockey | stadium organ + chant | 132 | goal horn sting |\n1317\t| `table` | results, medal table | proud, warm | 100 | |\n1318\t| `closing` | closing ceremony, credits | emotional anthem turning into a party | 96 → 128 | |\n1319\t| stings | WR, YIKES (descending trombone \"wah-wah-wah-waaah\"), laurel, qualify fail, games over, victory, goal horn | | | `audio.sting` |\n1320\t\n1321\tEvery event song names a `hype` track (`on: false`) faded in during turbo. Title motif (lead, one token a 16th, bars\n1322\tof 16): `G4 - - - C5 - - - E5 - - - G5 - - - | C6 - - - - - - - B5 - A5 - G5 - - - | A5 - - - F5 - - - D5 - - - G5 - - - |\n1323\tE5 - - - D#5 - - - D5 - - - C#5 - - - | C5 - - - . . G4 - C5 - E5 - G5 - - - | C6 - - - - - - - - - - - . . . .`\n1324\tover a bass `C3 C3 G2 G2 | A2 A2 E2 E2 | F2 F2 G2 G2 | C3 B2 Bb2 A2 | F2 G2 C3 - | C3 - - -` (quarters) and drums\n1325\t`k . . . s . . . k . k . s . . .` with a snare roll into the last bar. Keep the \"rise, comic slide, recover\" shape:\n1326\tit is the game's sonic logo.\n1327\t\n1328\t### 9.2 Sound effects (`audio.define`, layered voices; names → recipe)\n1329\t\n1330\t`gun` (noise burst 1800→200 Hz .12 s + sine 90→40 .3 s), `beep` (sine 880 .15), `step` (engine preset, pitched by\n1331\tspeed), `whoosh`, `thunk` (javelin into turf: noise lowpass + sine 140→60), `boing` (triangle 300→600→300 with vib),\n1332\t`twang` (pulse 220→180 with fast vibrato), `thwack` (noise 3000→800 .05 + sine 180), `clank` (square 800 + noise,\n1333\tmetallic `arp`), `slam` (bar drop: boom preset + rattle), `splash` (noise 2000→300 .5, size by vol), `slap` (belly\n1334\tflop: noise 4000→900 .08 + boom), `bubbles` (sine blips 600–1200), `swish` (ski carve: noise highpass 2–4 kHz),\n1335\t`crunch` (snow), `rumble` (sled: low noise loop by speed), `scrape` (noise 3–6 kHz + square 70), `clack` (stone:\n1336\tnoise 1500 .04 + square 400), `brush` (sweep: noise bursts), `puck` (click 2000 .03), `check` (boom + noise),\n1337\t`glass` (noise 5 kHz + triangle 1200 shimmer), `horn` (saw 220 + 277 + 330 1.2 s), `buzzer` (square 180 .8 s),\n1338\t`whistle` (from the sports kit), `cowbell` (square 560 + 840 decay), `camera` (click + highpass noise), `firework`\n1339\t(explode + crackle bits), `medal` (chime triangle C6–E6–G6), `cough` (noise formant), `alarm` (car alarm: square\n1340\t880↔660), `pop` (blimp: noise 3000→100), `yikes` sting. All go through the engine's sfx bus (volume settings apply).\n1341\t\n1342\t### 9.3 Voices: `O.Voice.speak(text, voice)` (Animalese/Simlish gibberish)\n1343\t\n1344\t- Split the line into syllables (`/[^aeiouy\\s]*[aeiouy]+[^aeiouy\\s]*|[.,!?]/gi`). For each syllable: vowel → formants\n1345\t  (a 730/1090, e 530/1840, i 270/2290, o 570/840, u 300/870, y 300/2000 Hz) scaled by the voice's `formant` (female\n1346\t  1.15, child/mascot 1.5); pitch `f0 = voice.base · 2^((hashOffset + contour)/12)` with `hashOffset` −3…+3 semitones\n1347\t  from a hash of the syllable (deterministic: never `Math.random`), contour rising on a question's last syllable,\n1348\t  falling on a period, +4 semitones and faster on \"!\". Duration `(.075 + .012·len) / voice.speed`, gap .02 s, pauses\n1349\t  .12 (comma) / .22 (period).\n1350\t- Source: an `OscillatorNode` (sawtooth for Chip, triangle for Vera, square for the PA, a narrow pulse built with `createPeriodicWave` for Max) with a little\n1351\t  vibrato and a −1 semitone fall at the end; consonant onsets add a 12 ms highpassed noise tick; two parallel band-pass\n1352\t  filters at F1 (Q 6) and F2 (Q 9); envelope 5 ms attack, 25 ms release; into the voice bus (engine change 6). The PA\n1353\t  adds a `DelayNode` echo (.18 s, feedback .3).\n1354\t- Returns the line's duration (subtitle timing, portrait mouth). Headless or before the first input: returns the\n1355\t  duration and makes no sound.\n1356\t- Voices: Chip (base 140 Hz, speed 1.15), Vera (210, .95), PA (120, .8, echo), Max (150, 1.25), each athlete per §7.1\n1357\t  (base 130 Hz × pitch), Yikesy (420, 1.4), crowd chant (6 detuned voices on \"O-LY-YI-KES!\").\n1358\t\n1359\t### 9.4 Crowd\n1360\t\n1361\t`O.CrowdAudio`: a looping noise source → band-pass (900 Hz, Q .7) → gain = `crowd volume × (.15 + .6·level)`, plus a\n1362\tlow murmur layer; events: cheer swell (level → 1, filter up), gasp (fast filter fall), \"OOOH\" (a cluster of 6 voices on\n1363\t\"oooh\"), applause (deterministic clap bursts), the chant, cowbells (winter outdoor), organ stabs (arena). Starts at the\n1364\tfirst user input (browsers' rule), ducks under the pause menu.\n1365\t\n1366\t### 9.5 Anthems\n1367\t\n1368\t`O.Anthem.song(nation)`: deterministic from the nation's seed: a major key (C, D, Eb, F, G or Bb), 8 bars of 4/4 at\n1369\t84–96 bpm, rhythm cells drawn from a small set (half + 2 quarters, dotted quarter + eighth + half, 4 quarters), melody\n1370\ton chord tones on strong beats over I–IV–V–I–vi–IV–V–I, brass lead (saw), harmony (square, quiet), bass (triangle),\n1371\ttimpani (low sine `k`) on downbeats and a snare roll into bar 8. ≈ 20 s, played once at the medal ceremony (and a\n1372\t4-bar excerpt for \"THE FINAL\" tease). Two nations never share a melody (test).\n1373\t\n1374\t### 9.6 Mix\n1375\t\n1376\tDefaults: master .7 (engine), music .5, effects 1, voices .8, crowd .7. While a commentary line plays, music ducks\n1377\t×0.7. Pause ducks everything (engine). Sound on/off and every volume live in the engine's Settings → Sound.\n1378\t\n1379\t---\n1380\t\n1381\t## 10. Modes and flow\n1382\t\n1383\t### 10.1 The Games (the campaign)\n1384\t\n1385\t```\n1386\tmenu → gamesSetup → nations (join + pick) → opening\n1387\t  → for day 1..12: [beat before?] → dayCard → eventCard → ev:<id> → results → [initials]\n1388\t        → (failed qualifying? → torch → retry the event | 0 torches → gamesOver → continue? retry : title)\n1389\t        → podium → medals → [beat after?] → autosave\n1390\t  → closing → ending (+ party podium if several humans) → credits → title\n1391\t```\n1392\t- **Setup:** Length (Full 12 days / Quick 4 with its playlist), Difficulty, Qualifying (On by default for 1 player,\n1393\t  Off for several).\n1394\t- **Nations:** every human picks a different nation; CPU nations take the rest (8 total always compete).\n1395\t- **Day card + event card** always shown; the event card waits until every human pressed `confirm` (\"READY\" in their\n1396\t  color) or P1 presses Start.\n1397\t- **Autosave** after each day's medal table (`oly:games`); CONTINUE GAMES resumes at the next day card. Quitting to\n1398\t  the title (the engine asks first) keeps the autosave. Finishing the Games deletes it and fills the cabinet.\n1399\t- **Quick Games:** playlists *Track & Pool* (100m, Javelin, 50m Free, Diving), *Snow & Ice* (Ski Jump, Downhill,\n1400\t  Bobsled, Curling), *Greatest Hits* (100m, Ski Jump, Diving, Ice Hockey), *Random 4* (2 summer + 2 winter from a\n1401\t  stream). A short flame-lighting opening (no parade), rival reactions only, party podium at the end.\n1402\t\n1403\t### 10.2 Single Event\n1404\t\n1405\tsingle (event grid) → nations (join + pick) → eventCard (with **Practice** on △: no CPUs, unlimited attempts, no\n1406\trecords) → ev → results → [initials] → short podium → a menu: **Retry · Change event · Main menu**.\n1407\t\n1408\t### 10.3 Records, How to Play, Settings, About\n1409\t\n1410\t- **Records:** one tab per event (top-5 table with initials, nation flag, date-free), **Laurels** (12 tiles with hints),\n1411\t  **Cabinet** (nation × event best medal icons). ←/→ or L1/R1 switch tabs.\n1412\t- **How to Play:** *Basics* (4 pages: mash, timing, hype & turbo, yikes) then the 12 event cards.\n1413\t- **Settings:** `game.menu('settings')` (engine HTML, scaled), with the Game group of §2.5.\n1414\t- **About & Credits** (paged, 10-foot): (1) **Source Information** (every field TASK.md lists), (2) **Testing\n1415\t  Feedback**, (3) **Engine Feedback**, (4) **Prompt Feedback** (the answers to TASK.md's questions, the same text as\n1416\t  the chat reply and `exit-interview.json`), (5) **Credits** (planned and built by which models, engine and version,\n1417\t  AI Hub client version, the engine changes of §4.6, asset sets used with their CC0 sources), (6) **Controls** (the\n1418\t  action map with glyphs for the current device).\n1419\t\n1420\t---\n1421\t\n1422\t## 11. Attract mode\n1423\t\n1424\t- **Trigger:** 10 s without input on the title or any main-menu screen (title, menu, single, records, howto, about,\n1425\t  gamesSetup, nations before anyone joined). \"Input\" = any key, mouse button, wheel, mouse movement > 4 px, gamepad\n1426\t  button or stick past the dead zone, touch. Tracked per step in the scene wrapper (`E.HOOKS.input` catches presses\n1427\t  while menus are open). The idle clock does not run while an engine HTML screen (settings, controls) is open\n1428\t  (`game.shell && game.shell.screen`).\n1429\t- **Playlist** (a director scene; every segment loads the real event scene with `meet.mode = 'attract'`):\n1430\t  `LOGO (4 s) → EVENT → RECORDS TABLE (6 s) → EVENT → MEDAL TABLE (6 s) → EVENT → LAUREL / TIP CARD (5 s) → EVENT → loop`,\n1431\t  events rotating through all 12 across loops: sprint, skijump, diving, downhill, curling, figure, hockey, javelin,\n1432\t  swim, archery, weights, bobsled. Each event has `attract.setup(ctx)` that starts at its showcase moment: the sprint\n1433\t  from SET, the ski jump from the gate with rocket skis, the YIKES quintuple dive, the downhill from the Yikes Face\n1434\t  jump, a curling end set up for a double takeout, figure skating from Jump Combo 2, 25 s of 2-on-2 hockey ending in an\n1435\t  ON FIRE goal, the out-of-the-stadium javelin, a perfect flip turn, a Robin Hood arrow, the YIKES BAR lift, the\n1436\t  Labyrinth on the bobsled. Segment length = `attract.seconds` (15–25 s).\n1437\t- **Cheating is allowed:** every athlete is a bot; the featured one uses `cheat: 'perfect'` (frame-perfect inputs,\n1438\t  infinite hype). Each loop also shows one scripted wipeout by a non-featured athlete, so the demo shows what can go\n1439\t  wrong.\n1440\t- **Overlay:** \"DEMO\" badge, the small logo, \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\" with the glyph of the last device (touch-only: the\n1441\t  \"Controller or keyboard required\" line instead), commentary subtitles on.\n1442\t- **Exit:** any input → title (the input is consumed so it doesn't also press anything there). Attract never writes\n1443\t  records, laurels, saves or ghosts.\n1444\t\n1445\t---\n1446\t\n1447\t## 12. Multiplayer\n1448\t\n1449\t### 12.1 Local (the game on its own)\n1450\t\n1451\t- Players join on the Nations screen (and in Single Event) with `game.allowJoin({ max: 4, onJoin })`: Start/✕ on a\n1452\t  free gamepad, or **2** on the keyboard (the halves split); ○/Esc leaves before the event starts\n1453\t  (`game.removePlayer`). Each player's color is `E.PLAYER_COLORS[i]` and tag P1–P4.\n1454\t- Formats: races put humans in middle lanes, simultaneously (one shared camera framing the humans); attempts/programs\n1455\t  take turns with a **turn card** (\"P2 — YOUR TURN\") and the previous player's attempt as a ghost; matches offer\n1456\t  **Versus** (P1 vs P2, or 2v2 in hockey) or **Co-op** (humans on one team; curling co-op = one throws, one sweeps).\n1457\t- Every prompt, pause (\"P2 PAUSED\") and Controls page is per player (engine).\n1458\t\n1459\t### 12.2 AI Hub sessions: \"Hub Heats\" in **ghost** mode\n1460\t\n1461\tWhy ghost: every copy runs its own seeded heat of the same three events at the same moments on the hub's clock, and\n1462\tshows the other players as ghosts in neighbouring lanes, so it plays like a real head-to-head final with no\n1463\thost-authoritative sync.\n1464\t\n1465\t- **Tags** (§4.9): `hub:session 1`, `hub:session-players 1-4`, `hub:session-mode ghost`, `hub:session-minutes 4`,\n1466\t  goal and how-to. The client `vendor/hub/session.js` is pasted unmodified as the first script in `<head>`.\n1467\t- **Detect:** `AIHub.active` (true from the first line). Then the game **never shows the title, attract or menus**.\n1468\t  A boot step awaits `AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`; if it resolves `null`, boot the\n1469\t  normal game.\n1470\t- **The deal:** three events from `AIHub.rng('deal')`, one per group: A {sprint, swim}, B {javelin, archery, weights,\n1471\t  diving, skijump}, C {downhill, bobsled}; order A, B, C. Nations by seat from `AIHub.rng('nations')` (a permutation);\n1472\t  names and colors come from `info.players` (seat colors `#e8443a #3b82f6 #22c55e #f5b700`) and are drawn with the\n1473\t  pixel font, never inserted as HTML. No CPU athletes in hub heats; a translucent \"WR pace\" marker gives a target.\n1474\t- **Our own card** (`card: true`, scene `hubCard`): the venue of event 1 as backdrop, the three dealt events with\n1475\t  pictograms, the players lined up in seat colors with a READY tick each (from `card` events), \"Most points over three\n1476\t  events wins\", this player's controls (keyboard and controller columns with glyph icons), the countdown from\n1477\t  `card.left`. **Enter/✕/tap on READY → `AIHub.answer('ready')`; △ (button 3), the T key or a tap on MORE TIME →\n1478\t  `AIHub.answer('more')`** (again takes it back). No menus, settings or choices on the card. **No `Math.random`\n1479\t  consumers on the card:** with engine change 2 the rigs and particles no longer call `Math.random`, so the card may\n1480\t  animate them; any randomness of the card's own comes from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n1481\t- **Ready:** call `AIHub.ready()` once, as soon as boot has built the first venue, with no key press.\n1482\t- **Start:** on `start`, show a big 3-2-1 synced to `AIHub.time()` (negative during the countdown); play begins at\n1483\t  `AIHub.time() >= 0`.\n1484\t- **Slots on the hub clock:** event *i* runs in a fixed slot (`hub.seconds` per event: sprint 35, swim 45, javelin 45,\n1485\t  archery 50, weights 50, diving 45, skijump 40, downhill 70, bobsled 60). Each slot: 5 s \"GET READY\" (the event card\n1486\t  as an overlay + countdown), the heat (hub variant: attempts as in §6), then a 4 s results splash; finishing early\n1487\t  means watching the ghosts until the slot ends; reaching the slot's end unfinished finalizes the attempt (DNF scores 0\n1488\t  for that event). Everyone moves to the next event together. If the tab was hidden past a slot, finalize it and\n1489\t  jump to the current slot.\n1490\t- **Ghost traffic:** ~10 messages/s, unreliable: `{ t: 'g', e: eventId, i: slot, a: attempt, s: [x, y, z, facing,\n1491\t  poseCode, extra] }` (≈ 60–90 bytes); reliable on each attempt and event result: `{ t: 'r', e, i, perf, pts, total }`.\n1492\t  Ghosts render as translucent athletes tinted in their seat color with their hub name: other lanes in races (lanes\n1493\t  assigned by seat around yours), alongside jumpers/divers/javelins (offset slightly in depth), colored hit marks on\n1494\t  the archery target, extra platforms for weights, road \"cars\" in downhill/bobsled. Ghosts never affect your world.\n1495\t  `leave` removes that ghost.\n1496\t- **Scoring:** points per event (§6 formulas); `AIHub.progress({ score: total, label: '100m · 9.87 s · 1,032 pts' })`\n1497\t  whenever points change and about once a second; after the third event: **`AIHub.result({ score: total, stats:\n1498\t  { '100m': '9.87 s', ... }, awards: [{ title: 'WORLD RECORD', detail: '100m · 9.41 s' }] })` exactly once**.\n1499\t- **`time-up`:** if no result was sent, send `AIHub.result({ score: total })` at once and freeze input (\"TIME!\")."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b1b95e-beb5-4384-ba72-665ccf7128b3","uuid":"270f0a1f-e9fa-48d7-a06d-be77da6247f9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:41:33.576Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-074118__x0e4b02/work/PLAN.md","content":"### 7.7 Pictograms, emblem, flags\n\n- **12 pictograms** (16×16 `E.sprite` strings; white figure on a rounded tile, summer coral `#ff6b4a`, winter ice-blue\n  `#3fa8e8`; drawn ×2 or ×3 on cards): sprint (leaning runner), javelin (arm back, diagonal shaft), swim (head and\n  arm arc over waves), diving (inverted figure over a splash), archery (figure drawing a bow), weights (bar overhead),\n  ski jump (forward-leaning figure on long V skis), downhill (tucked skier, diagonal), bobsled (sled with two\n  helmets), figure (spinning figure, one leg out), curling (stone + broom), hockey (stick + puck + skater). Used on the\n  schedule, event cards, results, Single Event tiles, the HUD and the records tabs.\n- **Emblem \"the Yikes Flame\":** a flame split down the middle, orange (summer) and ice-blue (winter), inside a gold\n  laurel wreath. Title, ceremonies, hub card, favicon (an inline SVG data URI of the same shape).\n- **Flags:** `O.Art.flag(g, x, y, w, h, nation, wave)` draws each flag from its spec with a 2-step cloth wave and\n  shading (`E.tones`).\n\n### 7.8 Items, power-ups, opponents and hazards\n\n| Kind | Content |\n|---|---|\n| **Equipment (items)** | spikes and blocks, javelin, swim cap and goggles, bow and arrows, barbell and color-coded plates, jump skis, downhill skis and poles, the two-man sled, curling stones and brooms, hockey sticks, puck and nets, the torch. Drawn by `O.Gear` (§8.2) in the nation's colors |\n| **Golden gear (unlock)** | winning gold in an event turns that event's equipment golden for that nation in later plays (saved in the cabinet); shown in Records → Cabinet |\n| **Power-ups** | YIKES TURBO (one per event, §6: HYPER ARM, DOLPHIN MODE, SLOW-MO SUPREMACY, EAGLE EYE, IRON WILL, ROCKET SKIS, AVALANCHE, JET SLED, STAR POWER, HYPER SWEEP, ON FIRE and the sprint's TURBO); sympathy hype after a yikes; speed gates in the downhill |\n| **Collectibles** | medals (cabinet), 12 laurels, world records and top-5 places with initials |\n| **Opponents (\"enemies\")** | the 7 CPU nations' stars with per-event skills (§7.1); the rival Max Overdrive (+0.03, always shown live); CPU curling skips that plan shots by simulation; the Turbonia hockey team and the goalies |\n| **Hazards** | the starter's gun (false starts), the foul line, wind and gusts, the pool wall, the take-off table's edge, gravity under a loaded bar, orange netting, crests that launch you, the tunnel's ice, banked walls that flip a sled, the hog and back lines, the boards and the glass |\n\n---\n\n## 8. Art and animation\n\n### 8.1 Look (the engine's native style, pushed to its look target)\n\nFollow every step of API.md's \"Look target\": `res: 'ps1'` + `expand`, HD Humanoids at size 1.25 dressed in each\nnation's palette, a backdrop or painted horizon behind every view, textured floors (`floorTex` functions for track,\ngrass, pool water, ice with scratches, snow with sparkle), 3–8 props per screen (`r.prop`/`r.shape`: flags, banners,\nlamps, benches, pines, fences, barriers, cameras on tripods, medal tables), effects on every impact, `E.font.title`\nlogos, lights in every scene, faces in every dialog (portraits). The season split in palettes: summer warm (gold,\ncoral, sky), winter cool (ice blue, violet, white) with warm floodlights; UI panels navy `#0c1028` with gold `#f2b632`\ntrim. Screenshots should compare with the best PS1-era 2D, not NES.\n\n### 8.2 Pose layer (`O.Pose`, src/06-pose.js) and the engine's pose hook\n\n- The Humanoid already animates runs, jumps (`air`), crouch, kneel, cheer, wave, hips, down, die, rolls (`flip`),\n  climbs, landings (`rig.land`) and every move in `E.MOVES` (use `new E.Attack('throw')` for the javelin release,\n  `'bash'` for hockey checks, `'twohand'` for slapshots, `'cast'` for the torch raise). **Use these first.**\n- For what it lacks, `O.Pose.set(rig, name, params)` installs `rig.post = (rig, J) => ...` (engine change 5). A pose\n  edits joints in the rig's own frame `[forward, right, up]`: `J.hipC, hipL/R, kneeL/R, footL/R, shC, shL/R, elbowL/R,\n  handL/R, head`, using helpers `armTo(J, side, target, hint)` and `legTo(J, side, target, hint)` (two-bone IK with\n  `E.ik3` and the rig's limb lengths `rig.o.armUpper/armLower/legUpper/legLower`), `lean(J, fwd, side)`,\n  `look(J, dir)`. Poses blend in/out with a weight (ease .15 s). Whole-body rotations set `rig.bodyPitch`,\n  `rig.bodyRoll`, `rig.pivot`.\n- **Pose list** (each previewable in the Pose Lab, `#poselab`): `blocks` (sprint crouch, hands on the line), `set`\n  (hips up), `dip` (torso thrown forward), `javCarry` (right hand above the shoulder), `javWithdraw`, `swimCrawl(phase,\n  breath)` (prone via bodyPitch 90°, arms on circles around the shoulders, flutter kick, head turned on breaths),\n  `diveStart(u)`, `flipTurn(u)`, `armsUp` (diving stance), `tuck`, `pike`, `layout`, `entry` (hands joined over the\n  head), `bellyFlop`, `archerDraw(u)` (bow arm extended to the target, string hand to the jaw), `archerRelease`,\n  `liftSetup`, `liftClean(h)` (hands on the bar, bar height h), `liftRack`, `liftJerk(u)` (split stance, arms locked\n  overhead), `liftDrop(u)`, `skiTuck`, `skiFlight(α)` (V-style: straight body leaning over the skis, arms back),\n  `telemark`, `tumble(t)`, `bobPush`, `bobPilot`, `bobBrake`, `skateGlide`, `skateSpiral`, `sitSpin`, `skateJump`\n  (arms crossed), `skateLand`, `curlSlide` (deep lunge, hand on the stone), `sweep(phase)`, `skipPoint`,\n  `hockeyStride`, `stickHandle`, `goalieStance`, `kneeSlide` (goal celebration), `flagCarry`, `torchRaise`, `bowHead`\n  (receiving a medal), `medalBite`, `podiumWave`, `faceplant` (built-in `flip` roll + `down`).\n- **Gear** (`O.Gear`, drawn with `r.queue` at projected joint positions so it depth-sorts with the rig): javelin,\n  bow + string + arrow, barbell + plates (ellipses facing the camera) with bend, skis (two long quads from the feet\n  along the ski direction, V in flight), poles, helmets/goggles, swim cap/goggles, bobsled (boxes through the view,\n  like `kits/kart.js` `box()`), curling stone and broom, hockey stick (line from hands to a blade on the ice) and puck,\n  medals, flags on poles, torch (with `particles.fire` and a light).\n- **Rear view for E.Road events:** `new E.View('rear', 'Rear', 0, 18, 1.6, 1)`; a rig with `facing: Math.PI / 2` faces\n  into the screen. Draw it inside the road's overlay at the skier's screen point (`rig.draw(g, sx, sy, REAR)`); for\n  ghosts and other sleds at a distance, cache views per quantized scale (`E.View(..., scale)` at 12 steps) as\n  `m7.view(k)` does in the kart kit.\n- **Check every pose** with `tools/filmstrip.mjs <page>#poselab/<pose> --steps \"wait:300 rec:16:2\" --seed 1`: no\n  joints through the body, no snapping when blending, readable silhouettes at 1×.\n\n### 8.3 Effects\n\nFireworks (`particles.explosion(..., { debris: false })` + colored `glints`, launched with trails), confetti (`bits`\nin nation colors), splashes (blue/white `bit` particles sized by entry error; a rip makes only bubbles), snow spray\n(white dust on carves and crashes), sparks (sled scrapes, curling clacks, skate stops), chalk dust, camera flashes\n(white glints in the stands), turbo flames (`fire` + emissive glow), the gun's smoke puff, speed lines and sun\nglare overlays on the road events, the \"YIKES!\" stamp, the WR burst (rays + stars), the plush rain.\n\n### 8.4 Lighting per venue\n\n`game.lights.enabled = true` in every venue's enter: stadium day ambient .85 warm; stadium night .4 + stadium\nfloodlights + fireworks flashes; pool .8 cool + caustic glows; lawn .9; Iron Hall .35 + two warm spots; ski jump .35\n+ floodlights along the hill; ice palace .45 + moving colored spots; curling .6 warm; arena .4 + spots + goal light\nflash. E.Road scenes draw as overlays (unlit): bake the mood into their colors and add additive glow sprites.\n\n### 8.5 The mascot: YIKESY\n\nAn `E.Blob({ R: 9, ears: 'cat', feet: true, mouth: true, colors: { base: '#f8f8ff', dk: '#d8e2f0', lt: '#ffffff' } })`\n(a round snow-yeti) with a flame tuft on its head (fire particles + glow) and a half-orange/half-blue scarf drawn on\ntop. Appears on the title, in ceremonies, story beats, the attract mode, the curling scoreboard, as plush toys on the\nice, and in the Pose Lab. Voice: squeaky gibberish (pitch 1.9).\n\n---\n\n## 9. Audio (all in code)\n\n### 9.1 Music (engine songs `{ bpm, steps: 4, tracks }`, every one original)\n\n| Id | Where | Feel | BPM | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `title` | title, menus' first entry | heroic brass fanfare with a comic chromatic \"yikes\" slide, then triumph | 120 | motif below |\n| `menu` | main menu, setup screens | bright funk-pop loop | 112 | |\n| `parade` | opening ceremony | march, snare rolls | 116 | |\n| `sprint` | 100m | chiptune drum & bass | 172 | `hype` drum layer |\n| `javelin` | javelin | funky groove | 104 | |\n| `swim` | 50m free | bubbly arpeggios | 128 | |\n| `diving` | diving | sparse, timpani, suspense | 90 | |\n| `archery` | archery | tense minimal + heartbeat kick | 80 | heartbeat speeds with `hr` |\n| `iron` | weightlifting | heavy rock riff (saw bass) | 96 | |\n| `alpine` | ski jump | floodlit alpine pulse, bells | 124 | |\n| `yikesface` | downhill | driving rock | 150 | |\n| `icesurf` | bobsled | surf rock | 160 | |\n| `waltz` | figure skating | \"Waltz of the Yikes\", 3/4 (bars of 12 steps) | 138 | the rhythm chart's song |\n| `lounge` | curling | lounge jazz (swing feel) | 92 | |\n| `organ` | hockey | stadium organ + chant | 132 | goal horn sting |\n| `table` | results, medal table | proud, warm | 100 | |\n| `closing` | closing ceremony, credits | emotional anthem turning into a party | 96 → 128 | |\n| stings | WR, YIKES (descending trombone \"wah-wah-wah-waaah\"), laurel, qualify fail, games over, victory, goal horn | | | `audio.sting` |\n\nEvery event song names a `hype` track (`on: false`) faded in during turbo. Title motif (lead, one token a 16th, bars\nof 16): `G4 - - - C5 - - - E5 - - - G5 - - - | C6 - - - - - - - B5 - A5 - G5 - - - | A5 - - - F5 - - - D5 - - - G5 - - - |\nE5 - - - D#5 - - - D5 - - - C#5 - - - | C5 - - - . . G4 - C5 - E5 - G5 - - - | C6 - - - - - - - - - - - . . . .`\nover a bass `C3 C3 G2 G2 | A2 A2 E2 E2 | F2 F2 G2 G2 | C3 B2 Bb2 A2 | F2 G2 C3 - | C3 - - -` (quarters) and drums\n`k . . . s . . . k . k . s . . .` with a snare roll into the last bar. Keep the \"rise, comic slide, recover\" shape:\nit is the game's sonic logo.\n\n### 9.2 Sound effects (`audio.define`, layered voices; names → recipe)\n\n`gun` (noise burst 1800→200 Hz .12 s + sine 90→40 .3 s), `beep` (sine 880 .15), `step` (engine preset, pitched by\nspeed), `whoosh`, `thunk` (javelin into turf: noise lowpass + sine 140→60), `boing` (triangle 300→600→300 with vib),\n`twang` (pulse 220→180 with fast vibrato), `thwack` (noise 3000→800 .05 + sine 180), `clank` (square 800 + noise,\nmetallic `arp`), `slam` (bar drop: boom preset + rattle), `splash` (noise 2000→300 .5, size by vol), `slap` (belly\nflop: noise 4000→900 .08 + boom), `bubbles` (sine blips 600–1200), `swish` (ski carve: noise highpass 2–4 kHz),\n`crunch` (snow), `rumble` (sled: low noise loop by speed), `scrape` (noise 3–6 kHz + square 70), `clack` (stone:\nnoise 1500 .04 + square 400), `brush` (sweep: noise bursts), `puck` (click 2000 .03), `check` (boom + noise),\n`glass` (noise 5 kHz + triangle 1200 shimmer), `horn` (saw 220 + 277 + 330 1.2 s), `buzzer` (square 180 .8 s),\n`whistle` (from the sports kit), `cowbell` (square 560 + 840 decay), `camera` (click + highpass noise), `firework`\n(explode + crackle bits), `medal` (chime triangle C6–E6–G6), `cough` (noise formant), `alarm` (car alarm: square\n880↔660), `pop` (blimp: noise 3000→100), `yikes` sting. All go through the engine's sfx bus (volume settings apply).\n\n### 9.3 Voices: `O.Voice.speak(text, voice)` (Animalese/Simlish gibberish)\n\n- Split the line into syllables (`/[^aeiouy\\s]*[aeiouy]+[^aeiouy\\s]*|[.,!?]/gi`). For each syllable: vowel → formants\n  (a 730/1090, e 530/1840, i 270/2290, o 570/840, u 300/870, y 300/2000 Hz) scaled by the voice's `formant` (female\n  1.15, child/mascot 1.5); pitch `f0 = voice.base · 2^((hashOffset + contour)/12)` with `hashOffset` −3…+3 semitones\n  from a hash of the syllable (deterministic: never `Math.random`), contour rising on a question's last syllable,\n  falling on a period, +4 semitones and faster on \"!\". Duration `(.075 + .012·len) / voice.speed`, gap .02 s, pauses\n  .12 (comma) / .22 (period).\n- Source: an `OscillatorNode` (sawtooth for Chip, triangle for Vera, square for the PA, a narrow pulse built with `createPeriodicWave` for Max) with a little\n  vibrato and a −1 semitone fall at the end; consonant onsets add a 12 ms highpassed noise tick; two parallel band-pass\n  filters at F1 (Q 6) and F2 (Q 9); envelope 5 ms attack, 25 ms release; into the voice bus (engine change 6). The PA\n  adds a `DelayNode` echo (.18 s, feedback .3).\n- Returns the line's duration (subtitle timing, portrait mouth). Headless or before the first input: returns the\n  duration and makes no sound.\n- Voices: Chip (base 140 Hz, speed 1.15), Vera (210, .95), PA (120, .8, echo), Max (150, 1.25), each athlete per §7.1\n  (base 130 Hz × pitch), Yikesy (420, 1.4), crowd chant (6 detuned voices on \"O-LY-YI-KES!\").\n\n### 9.4 Crowd\n\n`O.CrowdAudio`: a looping noise source → band-pass (900 Hz, Q .7) → gain = `crowd volume × (.15 + .6·level)`, plus a\nlow murmur layer; events: cheer swell (level → 1, filter up), gasp (fast filter fall), \"OOOH\" (a cluster of 6 voices on\n\"oooh\"), applause (deterministic clap bursts), the chant, cowbells (winter outdoor), organ stabs (arena). Starts at the\nfirst user input (browsers' rule), ducks under the pause menu.\n\n### 9.5 Anthems\n\n`O.Anthem.song(nation)`: deterministic from the nation's seed: a major key (C, D, Eb, F, G or Bb), 8 bars of 4/4 at\n84–96 bpm, rhythm cells drawn from a small set (half + 2 quarters, dotted quarter + eighth + half, 4 quarters), melody\non chord tones on strong beats over I–IV–V–I–vi–IV–V–I, brass lead (saw), harmony (square, quiet), bass (triangle),\ntimpani (low sine `k`) on downbeats and a snare roll into bar 8. ≈ 20 s, played once at the medal ceremony (and a\n4-bar excerpt for \"THE FINAL\" tease). Two nations never share a melody (test).\n\n### 9.6 Mix\n\nDefaults: master .7 (engine), music .5, effects 1, voices .8, crowd .7. While a commentary line plays, music ducks\n×0.7. Pause ducks everything (engine). Sound on/off and every volume live in the engine's Settings → Sound.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Modes and flow\n\n### 10.1 The Games (the campaign)\n\n```\nmenu → gamesSetup → nations (join + pick) → opening\n  → for day 1..12: [beat before?] → dayCard → eventCard → ev:<id> → results → [initials]\n        → (failed qualifying? → torch → retry the event | 0 torches → gamesOver → continue? retry : title)\n        → podium → medals → [beat after?] → autosave\n  → closing → ending (+ party podium if several humans) → credits → title\n```\n- **Setup:** Length (Full 12 days / Quick 4 with its playlist), Difficulty, Qualifying (On by default for 1 player,\n  Off for several).\n- **Nations:** every human picks a different nation; CPU nations take the rest (8 total always compete).\n- **Day card + event card** always shown; the event card waits until every human pressed `confirm` (\"READY\" in their\n  color) or P1 presses Start.\n- **Autosave** after each day's medal table (`oly:games`); CONTINUE GAMES resumes at the next day card. Quitting to\n  the title (the engine asks first) keeps the autosave. Finishing the Games deletes it and fills the cabinet.\n- **Quick Games:** playlists *Track & Pool* (100m, Javelin, 50m Free, Diving), *Snow & Ice* (Ski Jump, Downhill,\n  Bobsled, Curling), *Greatest Hits* (100m, Ski Jump, Diving, Ice Hockey), *Random 4* (2 summer + 2 winter from a\n  stream). A short flame-lighting opening (no parade), rival reactions only, party podium at the end.\n\n### 10.2 Single Event\n\nsingle (event grid) → nations (join + pick) → eventCard (with **Practice** on △: no CPUs, unlimited attempts, no\nrecords) → ev → results → [initials] → short podium → a menu: **Retry · Change event · Main menu**.\n\n### 10.3 Records, How to Play, Settings, About\n\n- **Records:** one tab per event (top-5 table with initials, nation flag, date-free), **Laurels** (12 tiles with hints),\n  **Cabinet** (nation × event best medal icons). ←/→ or L1/R1 switch tabs.\n- **How to Play:** *Basics* (4 pages: mash, timing, hype & turbo, yikes) then the 12 event cards.\n- **Settings:** `game.menu('settings')` (engine HTML, scaled), with the Game group of §2.5.\n- **About & Credits** (paged, 10-foot): (1) **Source Information** (every field TASK.md lists), (2) **Testing\n  Feedback**, (3) **Engine Feedback**, (4) **Prompt Feedback** (the answers to TASK.md's questions, the same text as\n  the chat reply and `exit-interview.json`), (5) **Credits** (planned and built by which models, engine and version,\n  AI Hub client version, the engine changes of §4.6, asset sets used with their CC0 sources), (6) **Controls** (the\n  action map with glyphs for the current device).\n\n---\n\n## 11. Attract mode\n\n- **Trigger:** 10 s without input on the title or any main-menu screen (title, menu, single, records, howto, about,\n  gamesSetup, nations before anyone joined). \"Input\" = any key, mouse button, wheel, mouse movement > 4 px, gamepad\n  button or stick past the dead zone, touch. Tracked per step in the scene wrapper (`E.HOOKS.input` catches presses\n  while menus are open). The idle clock does not run while an engine HTML screen (settings, controls) is open\n  (`game.shell && game.shell.screen`).\n- **Playlist** (a director scene; every segment loads the real event scene with `meet.mode = 'attract'`):\n  `LOGO (4 s) → EVENT → RECORDS TABLE (6 s) → EVENT → MEDAL TABLE (6 s) → EVENT → LAUREL / TIP CARD (5 s) → EVENT → loop`,\n  events rotating through all 12 across loops: sprint, skijump, diving, downhill, curling, figure, hockey, javelin,\n  swim, archery, weights, bobsled. Each event has `attract.setup(ctx)` that starts at its showcase moment: the sprint\n  from SET, the ski jump from the gate with rocket skis, the YIKES quintuple dive, the downhill from the Yikes Face\n  jump, a curling end set up for a double takeout, figure skating from Jump Combo 2, 25 s of 2-on-2 hockey ending in an\n  ON FIRE goal, the out-of-the-stadium javelin, a perfect flip turn, a Robin Hood arrow, the YIKES BAR lift, the\n  Labyrinth on the bobsled. Segment length = `attract.seconds` (15–25 s).\n- **Cheating is allowed:** every athlete is a bot; the featured one uses `cheat: 'perfect'` (frame-perfect inputs,\n  infinite hype). Each loop also shows one scripted wipeout by a non-featured athlete, so the demo shows what can go\n  wrong.\n- **Overlay:** \"DEMO\" badge, the small logo, \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\" with the glyph of the last device (touch-only: the\n  \"Controller or keyboard required\" line instead), commentary subtitles on.\n- **Exit:** any input → title (the input is consumed so it doesn't also press anything there). Attract never writes\n  records, laurels, saves or ghosts.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Multiplayer\n\n### 12.1 Local (the game on its own)\n\n- Players join on the Nations screen (and in Single Event) with `game.allowJoin({ max: 4, onJoin })`: Start/✕ on a\n  free gamepad, or **2** on the keyboard (the halves split); ○/Esc leaves before the event starts\n  (`game.removePlayer`). Each player's color is `E.PLAYER_COLORS[i]` and tag P1–P4.\n- Formats: races put humans in middle lanes, simultaneously (one shared camera framing the humans); attempts/programs\n  take turns with a **turn card** (\"P2 — YOUR TURN\") and the previous player's attempt as a ghost; matches offer\n  **Versus** (P1 vs P2, or 2v2 in hockey) or **Co-op** (humans on one team; curling co-op = one throws, one sweeps).\n- Every prompt, pause (\"P2 PAUSED\") and Controls page is per player (engine).\n\n### 12.2 AI Hub sessions: \"Hub Heats\" in **ghost** mode\n\nWhy ghost: every copy runs its own seeded heat of the same three events at the same moments on the hub's clock, and\nshows the other players as ghosts in neighbouring lanes, so it plays like a real head-to-head final with no\nhost-authoritative sync.\n\n- **Tags** (§4.9): `hub:session 1`, `hub:session-players 1-4`, `hub:session-mode ghost`, `hub:session-minutes 4`,\n  goal and how-to. The client `vendor/hub/session.js` is pasted unmodified as the first script in `<head>`.\n- **Detect:** `AIHub.active` (true from the first line). Then the game **never shows the title, attract or menus**.\n  A boot step awaits `AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`; if it resolves `null`, boot the\n  normal game.\n- **The deal:** three events from `AIHub.rng('deal')`, one per group: A {sprint, swim}, B {javelin, archery, weights,\n  diving, skijump}, C {downhill, bobsled}; order A, B, C. Nations by seat from `AIHub.rng('nations')` (a permutation);\n  names and colors come from `info.players` (seat colors `#e8443a #3b82f6 #22c55e #f5b700`) and are drawn with the\n  pixel font, never inserted as HTML. No CPU athletes in hub heats; a translucent \"WR pace\" marker gives a target.\n- **Our own card** (`card: true`, scene `hubCard`): the venue of event 1 as backdrop, the three dealt events with\n  pictograms, the players lined up in seat colors with a READY tick each (from `card` events), \"Most points over three\n  events wins\", this player's controls (keyboard and controller columns with glyph icons), the countdown from\n  `card.left`. **Enter/✕/tap on READY → `AIHub.answer('ready')`; △ (button 3), the T key or a tap on MORE TIME →\n  `AIHub.answer('more')`** (again takes it back). No menus, settings or choices on the card. **No `Math.random`\n  consumers on the card:** with engine change 2 the rigs and particles no longer call `Math.random`, so the card may\n  animate them; any randomness of the card's own comes from `AIHub.rng('card')`.\n- **Ready:** call `AIHub.ready()` once, as soon as boot has built the first venue, with no key press.\n- **Start:** on `start`, show a big 3-2-1 synced to `AIHub.time()` (negative during the countdown); play begins at\n  `AIHub.time() >= 0`.\n- **Slots on the hub clock:** event *i* runs in a fixed slot (`hub.seconds` per event: sprint 35, swim 45, javelin 45,\n  archery 50, weights 50, diving 45, skijump 40, downhill 70, bobsled 60). Each slot: 5 s \"GET READY\" (the event card\n  as an overlay + countdown), the heat (hub variant: attempts as in §6), then a 4 s results splash; finishing early\n  means watching the ghosts until the slot ends; reaching the slot's end unfinished finalizes the attempt (DNF scores 0\n  for that event). Everyone moves to the next event together. If the tab was hidden past a slot, finalize it and\n  jump to the current slot.\n- **Ghost traffic:** ~10 messages/s, unreliable: `{ t: 'g', e: eventId, i: slot, a: attempt, s: [x, y, z, facing,\n  poseCode, extra] }` (≈ 60–90 bytes); reliable on each attempt and event result: `{ t: 'r', e, i, perf, pts, total }`.\n  Ghosts render as translucent athletes tinted in their seat color with their hub name: other lanes in races (lanes\n  assigned by seat around yours), alongside jumpers/divers/javelins (offset slightly in depth), colored hit marks on\n  the archery target, extra platforms for weights, road \"cars\" in downhill/bobsled. Ghosts never affect your world.\n  `leave` removes that ghost.\n- **Scoring:** points per event (§6 formulas); `AIHub.progress({ score: total, label: '100m · 9.87 s · 1,032 pts' })`\n  whenever points change and about once a second; after the third event: **`AIHub.result({ score: total, stats:\n  { '100m': '9.87 s', ... }, awards: [{ title: 'WORLD RECORD', detail: '100m · 9.41 s' }] })` exactly once**.\n- **`time-up`:** if no result was sent, send `AIHub.result({ score: total })` at once and freeze input (\"TIME!\").","numLines":300,"startLine":1200,"totalLines":1723}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RepwPhEUDP1CCtxow5ken2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi4bqnByJyuLK5xV8yCS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EuwB9cc1AhrkppQMH8yHtd","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-074118__x0e4b02/work/PLAN.md","offset":1500,"limit":225},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10838,"cache_read_input_tokens":22643,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10838},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b1b95e-beb5-4384-ba72-665ccf7128b3","uuid":"7616d369-0db0-45fc-b56a-97e42658bf59","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:41:34.387Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi4bqVaHhUf9bqcq8gxF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01EuwB9cc1AhrkppQMH8yHtd":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-074118__x0e4b02/work/PLAN.md","offset":1500,"limit":225}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EuwB9cc1AhrkppQMH8yHtd","type":"tool_result","content":"1500\t- **`end`:** stop taking input (all players' `input.clear()` and a flag the scene wrapper checks), `audio.music(null)`,\n1501\t  silence voices/crowd, show \"ROUND OVER\" over the venue; send nothing afterwards.\n1502\t- **Rules:** no network but the hub, no `alert/confirm/prompt`, no new windows, no navigation; the pause menu has no\n1503\t  Quit, Restart or Dev mode (§4.4); Options is ignored while Create (pad button 8) is held (§2.1); storage is the\n1504\t  client's empty one (nothing to do); fullscreen requests go through the client automatically.\n1505\t\n1506\t---\n1507\t\n1508\t## 13. Dev mode (pause menu → \"Dev mode\"; the ` key also opens it; absent in hub sessions)\n1509\t\n1510\t- **Opening** closes the engine's pause menu (`game.resume()`) and sets `game.timeScale = 0` (the scene keeps updating with dt 0, so the\n1511\t  scene wrapper can run the panel); closing restores the previous time scale. **LIVE** (a toggle on the panel) lets\n1512\t  the game run at the dev speed while the panel stays open; then the panel suppresses the game's actions each step\n1513\t  (`input.suppress`), so only bots and the autopilot play.\n1514\t- **Panel:** pixel art, right 45% of the screen, 10-foot sized, tabs **TUNE · GLOBAL · CHEATS · JUMP · VIEW · DATA**\n1515\t  (L1/R1, Q/E or click). ↑/↓ choose a row, ←/→ change it (held: accelerates after .5 s), Shift/R2 = fine steps, ✕\n1516\t  activates the row (toggles and buttons; on a slider it resets that slider), △ resets the whole tab to defaults,\n1517\t  ○/Esc closes. Mouse: hover focuses, drag a slider, wheel nudges.\n1518\t- **TUNE:** the current event's tunables (≥ 6, listed in §6) as live sliders with their default marked; changed\n1519\t  values in gold with a count; **RESET TO DEFAULTS**; **COPY JSON** (clipboard + console) of changed values;\n1520\t  **KEEP AFTER RELOAD** (stores `oly:tune`, off by default).\n1521\t- **GLOBAL:** the global tunables (§5.13), same controls and reset.\n1522\t- **CHEATS:** Autopilot P1 (the AutoPlayer), Perfect P1, God mode (no wipeouts, fouls, DQs for humans), Infinite hype,\n1523\t  WIN NOW (gold), LOSE NOW (8th), DNF NOW, SKIP TO PHASE (each event lists its phases: e.g. ski jump: gate / take-off /\n1524\t  flight / landing; downhill: section 1–8; hockey: period 2 / overtime / shootout), NEXT ATTEMPT, UNLOCK ALL LAURELS,\n1525\t  TORCHES +3, GIVE MEDAL (gold/silver/bronze to your nation).\n1526\t- **JUMP:** any event (Single Event, P1 SUN vs CPU), any Games day (earlier days simulated), opening ceremony, closing\n1527\t  ceremony + ending (choose rank), podium and medal table with sample data, any story beat, attract, Pose Lab, the hub\n1528\t  card with a local stub hub and three fake ghosts (to see ghost rendering offline).\n1529\t- **VIEW:** rig skeletons (`rig.debug`), physics bodies (`world.draw`), radii/hitboxes, input display (each player's\n1530\t  `input.history` as glyph icons), FPS (the engine setting), state JSON (`game.debug.snapshot()`, paged), time scale\n1531\t  0.1×–4× and a FRAME STEP button (each ✕ on it advances one fixed step while frozen), free camera (`cam.free`) and zoom, HUD on/off,\n1532\t  lights on/off, photo mode (all UI hidden).\n1533\t- **DATA:** meet seed (view/set), reset records, reset laurels, clear the Games save, clear ghosts, sound test (any song,\n1534\t  sting, sfx, voice line), commentary test (cue any key).\n1535\t- `O.Dev.set(group, key, v)`, `O.Dev.cheat(name)`, `O.Dev.jump(target)` are the same actions for tests.\n1536\t\n1537\t---\n1538\t\n1539\t## 14. Build order and milestones\n1540\t\n1541\tBuild the spine and one complete event first, de-risk the hard techniques with spikes, then fill in events by reuse.\n1542\tEach milestone ends with `node tests/run.mjs` green and a short screenshot review.\n1543\t\n1544\t| M | Scope | Exit criteria |\n1545\t|---|---|---|\n1546\t| **M0 Setup** | §0.1 fetch; folder; `index.html`; `tests/run.mjs` + harness; `tools/bundle.mjs`; engine changes 1–4 | headless boot to a blank `title`; bundle opens via `tools/check.mjs` with no errors; tests print one line |\n1547\t| **M1 Spine** | 00–12 core files: game object, `OLY_KEYS`, pilots, `Mash` and timing widgets, `O.Prompt`, 10-foot widgets, tuning registry, streams, nations + rig factory (basic outfits), scene wrapper, `O.flow` (title → menu → single → event card → event → results → back), EventKit with formats, results/records/points, hype/turbo, yikes, comms (text first), crowd (visual), store | the 100m sim runs headless with 8 bots, deterministic twice, results and records correct; menus navigable by keys, pad codes and mouse in tests; prompts resolve to icons for every device |\n1548\t| **M2 Reference event + presentation** | 100m complete (stadium art, crowd, jumbotron, lights, music, sfx, `O.Voice`, crowd audio, commentary with portraits, HUD with glyphs, photo finish, false starts, faceplant, turbo, laurel); podium + anthem generator; medal table; dev panel v1 (TUNE/GLOBAL/CHEATS/JUMP); attract v1 (title → sprint demo → records → loop); touch-only notice; 10-foot CSS for the engine's HTML screens | all 100m targets (§6.1) pass; screenshots of title, stadium, HUD, podium, dev panel at 1920×1080 read well |\n1549\t| **M3 Risk spikes** (before more events; independent of M2) | (a) Pose layer + engine change 5: swim crawl, tuck/pike rotation, V-flight, telemark, jerk in the Pose Lab + filmstrips; (b) rear-view skier and gates on `E.Road`; (c) hub: a minimal ghost round with the sprint in the real harness via Playwright; (d) bundle from `file://` at full size; (e) curling ice model calibration (draw/takeout distances); (f) `E.Rhythm` 5-lane chart with the waltz + skater path | each spike has a passing test or an approved filmstrip; findings folded into §6 numbers |\n1550\t| **M4 Summer events** | Javelin (reuses the stadium), 50m Free, Diving, Archery, Weightlifting | each meets the event Definition of Done (below) |\n1551\t| **M5 Winter events** | Ski Jump, Downhill, Bobsled (reuses Downhill), Figure Skating, Curling, Ice Hockey (from the sports kit) | each meets the event Definition of Done |\n1552\t| **M6 The Games** | setup, nations + join, opening ceremony, day cards, all story beats, qualifying/torches/continue, halftime report, closing ceremony, endings, credits, autosave/continue, Quick Games, party points; local multiplayer in every format | the scripted playthrough (§16.3) passes for 1 player and for 2 players |\n1553\t| **M7 Front end** | attract (full playlist), Records/Laurels/Cabinet, How to Play, all Game settings, About & Credits pages | attract test passes; every menu screen reachable by keys, pad and mouse in tests |\n1554\t| **M8 AI Hub** | §12.2 complete: tags, card, deal, slots, ghosts for the 9 hub events, progress/result/time-up/end/leave, Create+Options | headless hub-stub suite passes; real harness: 2 players auto, 4 players with latency/jitter/loss, host-leave → `__hubCheck.pass === true` |\n1555\t| **M9 Balance and polish** | bot statistics per event and difficulty, commentary density, audio mix, visual passes per venue, crowd, effects | every event's targets (§6) hold; screenshot review of all venues; no runtime warnings in `check.mjs` |\n1556\t| **M10 Ship** | final bundle, full test run, final screenshots, About & Credits filled with real Source Information and feedback, `exit-interview.json` (valid JSON, every field), the chat reply | §17 checklist all ticked |\n1557\t\n1558\t**Event Definition of Done:** playable start to finish by keyboard, pad (and mouse where §2.2 says), and by bots;\n1559\tCPU rivals; HUD with glyph prompts and the event card; ≥ 6 tunables; turbo; every listed yikes; laurel; ≥ 8\n1560\tcommentary lines; its music and sfx; records, qualifying and points; multiplayer as specified; hub variant where\n1561\tlisted; attract segment; headless tests (determinism, bot completes, skill monotonic, every mechanic check of §6);\n1562\ta screenshot reviewed.\n1563\t\n1564\t---\n1565\t\n1566\t## 15. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1567\t\n1568\t| Risk | Impact | Mitigation | Early signal |\n1569\t|---|---|---|---|\n1570\t| Scope: 12 events + ceremonies + hub | an unfinished game | one event contract and widgets; reference event first; reuse kits (sports → hockey, road → downhill + bobsled, rhythm → figure, physics/pinball → curling); events written in order of reuse; nothing beyond this plan | milestone burn-down; DoD per event |\n1571\t| Custom athlete animation looks broken | cheap look, unreadable actions | built-in rig vocabulary first; `O.Pose` + Pose Lab + filmstrips in M3; equipment carries readability (a javelin, a barbell, skis say what the pose is) | M3 filmstrips |\n1572\t| Rigs from behind on `E.Road` | downhill/bobsled unconvincing | M3 spike with a custom rear `E.View`; fallback: skier and sled drawn as code-drawn sprites with 8 lean frames | spike screenshot |\n1573\t| Hub protocol failures | the game is kept out of sessions | M3 spike against the real harness; follow §12.2 literally; test every scenario | harness pass |\n1574\t| Cosmetic `Math.random` use (rigs, particles) | hub card rule broken; flaky tests | engine change 2; gameplay only via `O.rng` streams; proofs run twice | determinism tests; `Math.random` call-count check on the card |\n1575\t| Input conflicts (J/K/Space/○ in menus vs play) | skipped screens, accidental cancels | custom preset without J/K in confirm/cancel; lockouts; `consumeAll` on enter; hold-to-skip cinematics | input tests |\n1576\t| Missing ✕○□△ in the pixel font | `?` in prompts | `O.Prompt` icons + font glyphs (engine change 3) | prompt test for every action × device × glyph style |\n1577\t| Engine HTML menus too small on a TV | 10-foot failure | CSS override; 1920×1080 screenshot | screenshot |\n1578\t| Unbalanced events | boring or unfair | points tables; bot calibration tests per skill; dev sliders; difficulty presets | bot statistics test |\n1579\t| Slow headless tests | tests skipped | sims are draw-free; `--quick`; the full playthrough uses perfect bots | test time printed |\n1580\t| Bundle breakage (`</script>`, order, size) | a broken deliverable | bundler escapes; a bundle test in Chromium from `file://` | bundle test |\n1581\t| Voices grating | players mute everything | cooldowns, priorities, voices volume, subtitles-only | a listening pass with the dev sound test |\n1582\t| Touch-only misdetection on touch laptops | locked-out players | coarse && no fine pointer && no key/pad seen; any key or pad unlocks | touch emulation test |\n1583\t| Curling CPU cost (108 sims) | hitches | 12 candidates per frame, early exits | per-frame timing test |\n1584\t\n1585\t---\n1586\t\n1587\t## 16. Testing\n1588\t\n1589\t### 16.1 The one command\n1590\t\n1591\t`node tests/run.mjs` (from the dev folder) runs every suite: headless Node suites first, then the browser suites\n1592\t(Playwright). It prints **only failures** (suite, check, a one-line detail) and then **one line**:\n1593\t`olympiyikes: 512 checks, 0 failed (headless 41 s, browser 63 s)`; exit code 1 on any failure. `--quick` runs only the\n1594\theadless suites; `--only <suite>` runs one. Rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers. The browser suites\n1595\tload Playwright from the handoff's install (`createRequire(<dev>/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/package.json)('playwright')`),\n1596\tso there is one `npm install` for everything.\n1597\t\n1598\t### 16.2 The harness (`tests/harness.mjs`)\n1599\t\n1600\tAs the handoff's `game/test.mjs` and `kits/test.mjs`: a `vm` context with stand-ins (`window`, `addEventListener`,\n1601\t`location`, `matchMedia`, `navigator`, a fake clipboard), the engine, then the `src` files in `index.html` order;\n1602\toptionally a **fake `AIHub`** (connect resolves an info object; `time()` driven by the test; `send/progress/result`\n1603\trecorded; `emit(event)` to deliver `card/start/message/leave/time-up/end`). Helpers: `tap(action, player)`,\n1604\t`hold(action, on, player)`, `advance(s)`, `until(cond, maxS)`, `snap()` (= `game.debug.snapshot()`), `jump(target)`.\n1605\t**`game.debug.snapshot()`** returns `{ scene, mode, day, event, phase, attempt, round, athletes: [{ id, nation,\n1606\thuman, x, v, hype, perf, notes }], results, medals, torches, hub: { slot, total, sent }, dev: { open, changed },\n1607\terrors: game.errors.length }`.\n1608\t\n1609\t### 16.3 Suites and what they check\n1610\t\n1611\t- **core:** boot reaches `title`; every scene registered; `OLY_KEYS` has no J/K in confirm/cancel; the glyph\n1612\t  default is PlayStation and the setting switches to Xbox; `O.Prompt` resolves an icon for every action × device\n1613\t  (keyboard, mouse, gamepad) × family (playstation, xbox) with no `?`; points formulas are monotonic; WR/top-5 table\n1614\t  insertion and initials flow; tuning registry reset restores defaults; streams are deterministic per label; engine\n1615\t  changes present (`E.HOOKS`, `rig.post`, font glyphs, voice bus).\n1616\t- **events (×12):** for each event, in a sandbox with fixed seeds: (1) a full heat/attempt set with bots completes,\n1617\t  results valid, **the same hash twice** (determinism); (2) skill monotonic (skill .9 beats .3 in ≥ 90% of 40 seeds,\n1618\t  ≥ 80% for matches over 30); (3) the perfect bot hits the event's target band (§6); (4) every listed mechanic check\n1619\t  (false start, dip, foul, flat landing, belly-flop start, gasp, bonk, rip vs belly flop, Robin Hood, drop, fell off\n1620\t  the table, telemark vs crash, netting crash, gate penalty, load timing, flip, full combo, fall, curl direction sign,\n1621\t  takeout removes a stone, hog-line removal, goal, check knockdown, shootout); (5) every yikes kind reachable;\n1622\t  (6) the laurel test fires for a crafted performance; (7) a human pilot fed by scripted `input.tap/hold` (not the\n1623\t  bot) completes the event (the human path works); (8) idle human: the event still ends with a valid result.\n1624\t- **flow / playthrough:** the **scripted playthrough of the whole game**: title → menu → THE GAMES (Full, Normal,\n1625\t  Qualifying On) → nation SUN → opening (the torch throw played) → 12 days, P1 driven by the AutoPlayer at skill .95\n1626\t  through the real input path (cards confirmed, results continued, initials entered, ceremonies watched to their end,\n1627\t  not skipped, on days 1 and 12) → closing → credits → title. Asserts: 12 results, 12 golds/12 silvers/12 bronzes\n1628\t  awarded in the medal table, autosave written each day and cleared at the end, no errors. A second run with a\n1629\t  .2-skill autopilot exercises torches, GAMES OVER and CONTINUE. A third: Quick Games with 2 humans (both\n1630\t  autopiloted), party points, versus hockey. A fourth: CONTINUE GAMES resumes at the right day after a reload of\n1631\t  the store.\n1632\t- **attract:** title idle 9.9 s → still title; 10.1 s → `attract`; runs 3 full loops (all 12 events seen, records/\n1633\t  medal cards seen) with no errors and no store writes; one tap → title.\n1634\t- **dev:** open from the pause item; time frozen; a TUNE slider change (sprint `vMax` ×1.5) makes the next bot heat\n1635\t  ≥ 25% faster; RESET TO DEFAULTS restores the default and the timing; each cheat does what it says; each JUMP target\n1636\t  reaches its scene; the panel suppresses game actions in LIVE mode; absent in hub mode.\n1637\t- **local multiplayer:** 4 players via `game.addPlayer` (pads 1–3); 100m with 4 humans holding their own inputs → 4\n1638\t  lanes move independently; javelin turns rotate P1→P2→P3→P4 with turn cards; hockey 2v2 each human controls its own\n1639\t  skater; keyboard halves map our actions.\n1640\t- **hub (headless, fake AIHub):** tags present in `index.html`; with `active` true the title never appears; `connect`\n1641\t  called with `{ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true }`; `ready()` once without input; Enter on the card →\n1642\t  `answer('ready')`; △ → `answer('more')`; no `Math.random` calls while the card runs; the deal is the same for two\n1643\t  contexts with the same seed; play starts at `time() >= 0`; slots advance on the hub clock; `send` rate ≤ 20/s and\n1644\t  payloads ≤ 16 KB; progress sent; `result` exactly once; `time-up` before the end → result at once; `end` stops input\n1645\t  and music; `leave` removes the ghost; pause menu has no Quit/Restart/Dev.\n1646\t- **browser (Playwright, against the bundled HTML):** (1) **bundle**: the root HTML exists with the TASK.md name; its\n1647\t  first `<script>` after `<meta charset>` is byte-identical to `vendor/hub/session.js`; all hub tags present; opens\n1648\t  from `file://` with no console errors; title visible within 10 s; `#ev/sprint` deep link plays (via\n1649\t  `tools/check.mjs`-style probing of `__oly`); (2) **touch-only**: a mobile context with touch and coarse pointer\n1650\t  shows the notice and the SETTINGS button opens settings; after 10 s the attract runs; a keypress restores the\n1651\t  title; (3) **hub harness**: copy the bundle, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` into `<dev>/.hubtest/`, start\n1652\t  `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` there (parse the port; confirm `game=` page's title is \"Olympiyikes!\"),\n1653\t  run `harness.html?game=<bundle>&players=2&auto=1`, then `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, then\n1654\t  `&scenario=host-leave` (and `&players=1&auto=1`); each must end with `document.body.dataset.complete === \"true\"` and\n1655\t  `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`; kill the server by its PID.\n1656\t\n1657\t### 16.4 Screenshots (only what scripts can't judge)\n1658\t\n1659\tUse `vendor/.../tools/check.mjs <bundle>#<deep link>` and `tools/filmstrip.mjs` (via `tools/shots.mjs`), at 1920×1080\n1660\tand 1280×720: title, main menu, nations, opening ceremony (parade + flame), each of the 12 venues in play with its\n1661\tHUD, a results screen, the podium, the medal table, the dev panel, the touch-only notice, the hub card, the engine's\n1662\tpause and settings screens (10-foot CSS), and filmstrips of every pose in the Pose Lab plus the javelin throw, a\n1663\tdive, a ski-jump flight and landing, a skating jump, a curling slide and a hockey check. Act on `check.mjs` look notes.\n1664\t\n1665\t### 16.5 Rules\n1666\t\n1667\tTests never depend on wall-clock time (only `game.advance`), never on `Math.random` (streams with fixed seeds), and\n1668\tprint nothing on success. Keep the headless suites under ~2 minutes (perfect bots, short segments) so they get run.\n1669\t\n1670\t---\n1671\t\n1672\t## 17. Done checklist (TASK.md → where in this plan → how it's verified)\n1673\t\n1674\t| TASK.md requirement | Plan | Verified by |\n1675\t|---|---|---|\n1676\t| Genre and perspective chosen to fit the source | §1.3 | review |\n1677\t| Title: playful riff, 50 brainstormed, picked by a real RNG | top of this file | done at planning |\n1678\t| Single HTML named per the pattern, in the root; dev files in the subfolder | §0, §4.2, §4.9 | bundle test |\n1679\t| Built on the my-3d2dge handoff; engine changes allowed and listed | §4.1, §4.6 | core test; About |\n1680\t| Engine-native art + new source-specific assets | §7.2, §7.7, §8 | screenshots |\n1681\t| Engine-native animation + new animations | §8.2 | Pose Lab filmstrips |\n1682\t| All music, sfx and voices in code; gibberish voices | §9 | core/audio checks; listening |\n1683\t| Online via AI Hub, and multiplayer on its own | §12 | hub suites; local multiplayer suite |\n1684\t| Working environment, ports, processes, file:// first | §0 | practice |\n1685\t| Headless tests behind one command printing failures + a count; scripted playthrough of the whole game | §16 | `node tests/run.mjs` |\n1686\t| Original game capturing the source's world, characters, themes, tone | §1, §7 | review |\n1687\t| Feature-complete vertical slice showing every mechanic | §6 (12 events, every mechanic family), §10 | playthrough suite |\n1688\t| Dev mode from the pause menu; live sliders with reset to defaults | §13 | dev suite |\n1689\t| Attract mode after 10 s idle on title/menus; any input exits; may cheat | §11 | attract suite |\n1690\t| Narrative tone like the source (broadcast + ceremony + human interest) | §7.3–§7.6 | review |\n1691\t| 10-foot, controller-first; native keyboard/mouse; prompts follow the last input; PlayStation glyphs default, Xbox option; no dense web screens | §2, §3 | core prompt tests; screenshots |\n1692\t| Touch-only: \"Controller or keyboard required\" + settings button; attract runs | §3.3 | touch-only browser test |\n1693\t| No TODOs, placeholders, stubs | §0 | grep for TODO/FIXME/placeholder in `src` (a core check) |\n1694\t| Source Information, Testing/Engine/Prompt Feedback in the chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen | §10.3, Appendix A | review |\n1695\t| `exit-interview.json` beside the HTML, valid JSON, every field filled | Appendix A | a bundle-suite check parses it |\n1696\t\n1697\t---\n1698\t\n1699\t## Appendix A: About & Credits, the chat reply and `exit-interview.json`\n1700\t\n1701\tThe builders fill these at the end from their own run (write \"unknown\" for anything they can't confirm). Known at\n1702\tplanning time:\n1703\t\n1704\t- **Date:** 2026-11-03 17:48:37 (TASK.md's value) · **Source:** the complete Summer and Winter Olympic Games\n1705\t  (over-the-top arcade style) · **Plan:** `PLAN.md`\n1706\t- **Genre and Perspective:** arcade multi-event sports; 2.5D side lanes, side view, pseudo-3D behind-the-athlete,\n1707\t  three-quarter and top-down per event (§1.3)\n1708\t- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff (full engine with the road, rhythm, physics, arcade and songs modules), modified\n1709\t  (§4.6); AI Hub session client 1.4.0; Node + Playwright 1.63.0 for tests; single self-contained HTML\n1710\t- **Art Direction:** the engine's native PS1-era pixel art with HD Humanoid rigs; new flags, pictograms, venues,\n1711\t  equipment, mascot · **Animation:** the engine's procedural Humanoid rigs + the `O.Pose` layer and `E.MOVES`\n1712\t- **Audio:** the engine's chip synth: original songs, procedural anthems, synthesized sfx and crowd, gibberish voices\n1713\t- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode (\"Hub Heats\"); local 1–4 players\n1714\t- **Testing / Research / Environment / Model / Usage:** from the build run (TASK.md's wording for Environment)\n1715\t- **AI Hub catalogue block (suggested):** name `Olympiyikes!`, tagline `Faster. Higher. Yikes.`, description\n1716\t  \"Twelve over-the-top Summer and Winter events in one wild fortnight: sprint, swim, fly off a ski jump, sweep stones\n1717\t  and win the hockey final for your nation, alone or with up to four players.\", type `Game`, genre `Sports`, source\n1718\t  `The Olympic Games`, series `` (empty), players `1–4`, controls `Stick/WASD move · □○ or J K mash · ✕/Space act ·\n1719\t  △/Shift turbo · R2/L hold`, tags `[\"2d\", \"arcade\", \"pixel art\", \"comedy\", \"versus\", \"retro\"]`.\n1720\t- The Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback answers (TASK.md's questions, in order) go on About pages 2–4, in the chat\n1721\t  reply and in `exit-interview.json` with identical text. Check the JSON parses (`node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`).\n1722\t\n1723\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b1b95e-beb5-4384-ba72-665ccf7128b3","uuid":"bdf5f51b-6f43-4efc-8d3a-bcc964853b13","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:41:34.410Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-074118__x0e4b02/work/PLAN.md","content":"- **`end`:** stop taking input (all players' `input.clear()` and a flag the scene wrapper checks), `audio.music(null)`,\n  silence voices/crowd, show \"ROUND OVER\" over the venue; send nothing afterwards.\n- **Rules:** no network but the hub, no `alert/confirm/prompt`, no new windows, no navigation; the pause menu has no\n  Quit, Restart or Dev mode (§4.4); Options is ignored while Create (pad button 8) is held (§2.1); storage is the\n  client's empty one (nothing to do); fullscreen requests go through the client automatically.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Dev mode (pause menu → \"Dev mode\"; the ` key also opens it; absent in hub sessions)\n\n- **Opening** closes the engine's pause menu (`game.resume()`) and sets `game.timeScale = 0` (the scene keeps updating with dt 0, so the\n  scene wrapper can run the panel); closing restores the previous time scale. **LIVE** (a toggle on the panel) lets\n  the game run at the dev speed while the panel stays open; then the panel suppresses the game's actions each step\n  (`input.suppress`), so only bots and the autopilot play.\n- **Panel:** pixel art, right 45% of the screen, 10-foot sized, tabs **TUNE · GLOBAL · CHEATS · JUMP · VIEW · DATA**\n  (L1/R1, Q/E or click). ↑/↓ choose a row, ←/→ change it (held: accelerates after .5 s), Shift/R2 = fine steps, ✕\n  activates the row (toggles and buttons; on a slider it resets that slider), △ resets the whole tab to defaults,\n  ○/Esc closes. Mouse: hover focuses, drag a slider, wheel nudges.\n- **TUNE:** the current event's tunables (≥ 6, listed in §6) as live sliders with their default marked; changed\n  values in gold with a count; **RESET TO DEFAULTS**; **COPY JSON** (clipboard + console) of changed values;\n  **KEEP AFTER RELOAD** (stores `oly:tune`, off by default).\n- **GLOBAL:** the global tunables (§5.13), same controls and reset.\n- **CHEATS:** Autopilot P1 (the AutoPlayer), Perfect P1, God mode (no wipeouts, fouls, DQs for humans), Infinite hype,\n  WIN NOW (gold), LOSE NOW (8th), DNF NOW, SKIP TO PHASE (each event lists its phases: e.g. ski jump: gate / take-off /\n  flight / landing; downhill: section 1–8; hockey: period 2 / overtime / shootout), NEXT ATTEMPT, UNLOCK ALL LAURELS,\n  TORCHES +3, GIVE MEDAL (gold/silver/bronze to your nation).\n- **JUMP:** any event (Single Event, P1 SUN vs CPU), any Games day (earlier days simulated), opening ceremony, closing\n  ceremony + ending (choose rank), podium and medal table with sample data, any story beat, attract, Pose Lab, the hub\n  card with a local stub hub and three fake ghosts (to see ghost rendering offline).\n- **VIEW:** rig skeletons (`rig.debug`), physics bodies (`world.draw`), radii/hitboxes, input display (each player's\n  `input.history` as glyph icons), FPS (the engine setting), state JSON (`game.debug.snapshot()`, paged), time scale\n  0.1×–4× and a FRAME STEP button (each ✕ on it advances one fixed step while frozen), free camera (`cam.free`) and zoom, HUD on/off,\n  lights on/off, photo mode (all UI hidden).\n- **DATA:** meet seed (view/set), reset records, reset laurels, clear the Games save, clear ghosts, sound test (any song,\n  sting, sfx, voice line), commentary test (cue any key).\n- `O.Dev.set(group, key, v)`, `O.Dev.cheat(name)`, `O.Dev.jump(target)` are the same actions for tests.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Build order and milestones\n\nBuild the spine and one complete event first, de-risk the hard techniques with spikes, then fill in events by reuse.\nEach milestone ends with `node tests/run.mjs` green and a short screenshot review.\n\n| M | Scope | Exit criteria |\n|---|---|---|\n| **M0 Setup** | §0.1 fetch; folder; `index.html`; `tests/run.mjs` + harness; `tools/bundle.mjs`; engine changes 1–4 | headless boot to a blank `title`; bundle opens via `tools/check.mjs` with no errors; tests print one line |\n| **M1 Spine** | 00–12 core files: game object, `OLY_KEYS`, pilots, `Mash` and timing widgets, `O.Prompt`, 10-foot widgets, tuning registry, streams, nations + rig factory (basic outfits), scene wrapper, `O.flow` (title → menu → single → event card → event → results → back), EventKit with formats, results/records/points, hype/turbo, yikes, comms (text first), crowd (visual), store | the 100m sim runs headless with 8 bots, deterministic twice, results and records correct; menus navigable by keys, pad codes and mouse in tests; prompts resolve to icons for every device |\n| **M2 Reference event + presentation** | 100m complete (stadium art, crowd, jumbotron, lights, music, sfx, `O.Voice`, crowd audio, commentary with portraits, HUD with glyphs, photo finish, false starts, faceplant, turbo, laurel); podium + anthem generator; medal table; dev panel v1 (TUNE/GLOBAL/CHEATS/JUMP); attract v1 (title → sprint demo → records → loop); touch-only notice; 10-foot CSS for the engine's HTML screens | all 100m targets (§6.1) pass; screenshots of title, stadium, HUD, podium, dev panel at 1920×1080 read well |\n| **M3 Risk spikes** (before more events; independent of M2) | (a) Pose layer + engine change 5: swim crawl, tuck/pike rotation, V-flight, telemark, jerk in the Pose Lab + filmstrips; (b) rear-view skier and gates on `E.Road`; (c) hub: a minimal ghost round with the sprint in the real harness via Playwright; (d) bundle from `file://` at full size; (e) curling ice model calibration (draw/takeout distances); (f) `E.Rhythm` 5-lane chart with the waltz + skater path | each spike has a passing test or an approved filmstrip; findings folded into §6 numbers |\n| **M4 Summer events** | Javelin (reuses the stadium), 50m Free, Diving, Archery, Weightlifting | each meets the event Definition of Done (below) |\n| **M5 Winter events** | Ski Jump, Downhill, Bobsled (reuses Downhill), Figure Skating, Curling, Ice Hockey (from the sports kit) | each meets the event Definition of Done |\n| **M6 The Games** | setup, nations + join, opening ceremony, day cards, all story beats, qualifying/torches/continue, halftime report, closing ceremony, endings, credits, autosave/continue, Quick Games, party points; local multiplayer in every format | the scripted playthrough (§16.3) passes for 1 player and for 2 players |\n| **M7 Front end** | attract (full playlist), Records/Laurels/Cabinet, How to Play, all Game settings, About & Credits pages | attract test passes; every menu screen reachable by keys, pad and mouse in tests |\n| **M8 AI Hub** | §12.2 complete: tags, card, deal, slots, ghosts for the 9 hub events, progress/result/time-up/end/leave, Create+Options | headless hub-stub suite passes; real harness: 2 players auto, 4 players with latency/jitter/loss, host-leave → `__hubCheck.pass === true` |\n| **M9 Balance and polish** | bot statistics per event and difficulty, commentary density, audio mix, visual passes per venue, crowd, effects | every event's targets (§6) hold; screenshot review of all venues; no runtime warnings in `check.mjs` |\n| **M10 Ship** | final bundle, full test run, final screenshots, About & Credits filled with real Source Information and feedback, `exit-interview.json` (valid JSON, every field), the chat reply | §17 checklist all ticked |\n\n**Event Definition of Done:** playable start to finish by keyboard, pad (and mouse where §2.2 says), and by bots;\nCPU rivals; HUD with glyph prompts and the event card; ≥ 6 tunables; turbo; every listed yikes; laurel; ≥ 8\ncommentary lines; its music and sfx; records, qualifying and points; multiplayer as specified; hub variant where\nlisted; attract segment; headless tests (determinism, bot completes, skill monotonic, every mechanic check of §6);\na screenshot reviewed.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Risks and how to de-risk them\n\n| Risk | Impact | Mitigation | Early signal |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Scope: 12 events + ceremonies + hub | an unfinished game | one event contract and widgets; reference event first; reuse kits (sports → hockey, road → downhill + bobsled, rhythm → figure, physics/pinball → curling); events written in order of reuse; nothing beyond this plan | milestone burn-down; DoD per event |\n| Custom athlete animation looks broken | cheap look, unreadable actions | built-in rig vocabulary first; `O.Pose` + Pose Lab + filmstrips in M3; equipment carries readability (a javelin, a barbell, skis say what the pose is) | M3 filmstrips |\n| Rigs from behind on `E.Road` | downhill/bobsled unconvincing | M3 spike with a custom rear `E.View`; fallback: skier and sled drawn as code-drawn sprites with 8 lean frames | spike screenshot |\n| Hub protocol failures | the game is kept out of sessions | M3 spike against the real harness; follow §12.2 literally; test every scenario | harness pass |\n| Cosmetic `Math.random` use (rigs, particles) | hub card rule broken; flaky tests | engine change 2; gameplay only via `O.rng` streams; proofs run twice | determinism tests; `Math.random` call-count check on the card |\n| Input conflicts (J/K/Space/○ in menus vs play) | skipped screens, accidental cancels | custom preset without J/K in confirm/cancel; lockouts; `consumeAll` on enter; hold-to-skip cinematics | input tests |\n| Missing ✕○□△ in the pixel font | `?` in prompts | `O.Prompt` icons + font glyphs (engine change 3) | prompt test for every action × device × glyph style |\n| Engine HTML menus too small on a TV | 10-foot failure | CSS override; 1920×1080 screenshot | screenshot |\n| Unbalanced events | boring or unfair | points tables; bot calibration tests per skill; dev sliders; difficulty presets | bot statistics test |\n| Slow headless tests | tests skipped | sims are draw-free; `--quick`; the full playthrough uses perfect bots | test time printed |\n| Bundle breakage (`</script>`, order, size) | a broken deliverable | bundler escapes; a bundle test in Chromium from `file://` | bundle test |\n| Voices grating | players mute everything | cooldowns, priorities, voices volume, subtitles-only | a listening pass with the dev sound test |\n| Touch-only misdetection on touch laptops | locked-out players | coarse && no fine pointer && no key/pad seen; any key or pad unlocks | touch emulation test |\n| Curling CPU cost (108 sims) | hitches | 12 candidates per frame, early exits | per-frame timing test |\n\n---\n\n## 16. Testing\n\n### 16.1 The one command\n\n`node tests/run.mjs` (from the dev folder) runs every suite: headless Node suites first, then the browser suites\n(Playwright). It prints **only failures** (suite, check, a one-line detail) and then **one line**:\n`olympiyikes: 512 checks, 0 failed (headless 41 s, browser 63 s)`; exit code 1 on any failure. `--quick` runs only the\nheadless suites; `--only <suite>` runs one. Rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers. The browser suites\nload Playwright from the handoff's install (`createRequire(<dev>/vendor/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/package.json)('playwright')`),\nso there is one `npm install` for everything.\n\n### 16.2 The harness (`tests/harness.mjs`)\n\nAs the handoff's `game/test.mjs` and `kits/test.mjs`: a `vm` context with stand-ins (`window`, `addEventListener`,\n`location`, `matchMedia`, `navigator`, a fake clipboard), the engine, then the `src` files in `index.html` order;\noptionally a **fake `AIHub`** (connect resolves an info object; `time()` driven by the test; `send/progress/result`\nrecorded; `emit(event)` to deliver `card/start/message/leave/time-up/end`). Helpers: `tap(action, player)`,\n`hold(action, on, player)`, `advance(s)`, `until(cond, maxS)`, `snap()` (= `game.debug.snapshot()`), `jump(target)`.\n**`game.debug.snapshot()`** returns `{ scene, mode, day, event, phase, attempt, round, athletes: [{ id, nation,\nhuman, x, v, hype, perf, notes }], results, medals, torches, hub: { slot, total, sent }, dev: { open, changed },\nerrors: game.errors.length }`.\n\n### 16.3 Suites and what they check\n\n- **core:** boot reaches `title`; every scene registered; `OLY_KEYS` has no J/K in confirm/cancel; the glyph\n  default is PlayStation and the setting switches to Xbox; `O.Prompt` resolves an icon for every action × device\n  (keyboard, mouse, gamepad) × family (playstation, xbox) with no `?`; points formulas are monotonic; WR/top-5 table\n  insertion and initials flow; tuning registry reset restores defaults; streams are deterministic per label; engine\n  changes present (`E.HOOKS`, `rig.post`, font glyphs, voice bus).\n- **events (×12):** for each event, in a sandbox with fixed seeds: (1) a full heat/attempt set with bots completes,\n  results valid, **the same hash twice** (determinism); (2) skill monotonic (skill .9 beats .3 in ≥ 90% of 40 seeds,\n  ≥ 80% for matches over 30); (3) the perfect bot hits the event's target band (§6); (4) every listed mechanic check\n  (false start, dip, foul, flat landing, belly-flop start, gasp, bonk, rip vs belly flop, Robin Hood, drop, fell off\n  the table, telemark vs crash, netting crash, gate penalty, load timing, flip, full combo, fall, curl direction sign,\n  takeout removes a stone, hog-line removal, goal, check knockdown, shootout); (5) every yikes kind reachable;\n  (6) the laurel test fires for a crafted performance; (7) a human pilot fed by scripted `input.tap/hold` (not the\n  bot) completes the event (the human path works); (8) idle human: the event still ends with a valid result.\n- **flow / playthrough:** the **scripted playthrough of the whole game**: title → menu → THE GAMES (Full, Normal,\n  Qualifying On) → nation SUN → opening (the torch throw played) → 12 days, P1 driven by the AutoPlayer at skill .95\n  through the real input path (cards confirmed, results continued, initials entered, ceremonies watched to their end,\n  not skipped, on days 1 and 12) → closing → credits → title. Asserts: 12 results, 12 golds/12 silvers/12 bronzes\n  awarded in the medal table, autosave written each day and cleared at the end, no errors. A second run with a\n  .2-skill autopilot exercises torches, GAMES OVER and CONTINUE. A third: Quick Games with 2 humans (both\n  autopiloted), party points, versus hockey. A fourth: CONTINUE GAMES resumes at the right day after a reload of\n  the store.\n- **attract:** title idle 9.9 s → still title; 10.1 s → `attract`; runs 3 full loops (all 12 events seen, records/\n  medal cards seen) with no errors and no store writes; one tap → title.\n- **dev:** open from the pause item; time frozen; a TUNE slider change (sprint `vMax` ×1.5) makes the next bot heat\n  ≥ 25% faster; RESET TO DEFAULTS restores the default and the timing; each cheat does what it says; each JUMP target\n  reaches its scene; the panel suppresses game actions in LIVE mode; absent in hub mode.\n- **local multiplayer:** 4 players via `game.addPlayer` (pads 1–3); 100m with 4 humans holding their own inputs → 4\n  lanes move independently; javelin turns rotate P1→P2→P3→P4 with turn cards; hockey 2v2 each human controls its own\n  skater; keyboard halves map our actions.\n- **hub (headless, fake AIHub):** tags present in `index.html`; with `active` true the title never appears; `connect`\n  called with `{ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4], card: true }`; `ready()` once without input; Enter on the card →\n  `answer('ready')`; △ → `answer('more')`; no `Math.random` calls while the card runs; the deal is the same for two\n  contexts with the same seed; play starts at `time() >= 0`; slots advance on the hub clock; `send` rate ≤ 20/s and\n  payloads ≤ 16 KB; progress sent; `result` exactly once; `time-up` before the end → result at once; `end` stops input\n  and music; `leave` removes the ghost; pause menu has no Quit/Restart/Dev.\n- **browser (Playwright, against the bundled HTML):** (1) **bundle**: the root HTML exists with the TASK.md name; its\n  first `<script>` after `<meta charset>` is byte-identical to `vendor/hub/session.js`; all hub tags present; opens\n  from `file://` with no console errors; title visible within 10 s; `#ev/sprint` deep link plays (via\n  `tools/check.mjs`-style probing of `__oly`); (2) **touch-only**: a mobile context with touch and coarse pointer\n  shows the notice and the SETTINGS button opens settings; after 10 s the attract runs; a keypress restores the\n  title; (3) **hub harness**: copy the bundle, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` into `<dev>/.hubtest/`, start\n  `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` there (parse the port; confirm `game=` page's title is \"Olympiyikes!\"),\n  run `harness.html?game=<bundle>&players=2&auto=1`, then `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, then\n  `&scenario=host-leave` (and `&players=1&auto=1`); each must end with `document.body.dataset.complete === \"true\"` and\n  `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`; kill the server by its PID.\n\n### 16.4 Screenshots (only what scripts can't judge)\n\nUse `vendor/.../tools/check.mjs <bundle>#<deep link>` and `tools/filmstrip.mjs` (via `tools/shots.mjs`), at 1920×1080\nand 1280×720: title, main menu, nations, opening ceremony (parade + flame), each of the 12 venues in play with its\nHUD, a results screen, the podium, the medal table, the dev panel, the touch-only notice, the hub card, the engine's\npause and settings screens (10-foot CSS), and filmstrips of every pose in the Pose Lab plus the javelin throw, a\ndive, a ski-jump flight and landing, a skating jump, a curling slide and a hockey check. Act on `check.mjs` look notes.\n\n### 16.5 Rules\n\nTests never depend on wall-clock time (only `game.advance`), never on `Math.random` (streams with fixed seeds), and\nprint nothing on success. Keep the headless suites under ~2 minutes (perfect bots, short segments) so they get run.\n\n---\n\n## 17. Done checklist (TASK.md → where in this plan → how it's verified)\n\n| TASK.md requirement | Plan | Verified by |\n|---|---|---|\n| Genre and perspective chosen to fit the source | §1.3 | review |\n| Title: playful riff, 50 brainstormed, picked by a real RNG | top of this file | done at planning |\n| Single HTML named per the pattern, in the root; dev files in the subfolder | §0, §4.2, §4.9 | bundle test |\n| Built on the my-3d2dge handoff; engine changes allowed and listed | §4.1, §4.6 | core test; About |\n| Engine-native art + new source-specific assets | §7.2, §7.7, §8 | screenshots |\n| Engine-native animation + new animations | §8.2 | Pose Lab filmstrips |\n| All music, sfx and voices in code; gibberish voices | §9 | core/audio checks; listening |\n| Online via AI Hub, and multiplayer on its own | §12 | hub suites; local multiplayer suite |\n| Working environment, ports, processes, file:// first | §0 | practice |\n| Headless tests behind one command printing failures + a count; scripted playthrough of the whole game | §16 | `node tests/run.mjs` |\n| Original game capturing the source's world, characters, themes, tone | §1, §7 | review |\n| Feature-complete vertical slice showing every mechanic | §6 (12 events, every mechanic family), §10 | playthrough suite |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu; live sliders with reset to defaults | §13 | dev suite |\n| Attract mode after 10 s idle on title/menus; any input exits; may cheat | §11 | attract suite |\n| Narrative tone like the source (broadcast + ceremony + human interest) | §7.3–§7.6 | review |\n| 10-foot, controller-first; native keyboard/mouse; prompts follow the last input; PlayStation glyphs default, Xbox option; no dense web screens | §2, §3 | core prompt tests; screenshots |\n| Touch-only: \"Controller or keyboard required\" + settings button; attract runs | §3.3 | touch-only browser test |\n| No TODOs, placeholders, stubs | §0 | grep for TODO/FIXME/placeholder in `src` (a core check) |\n| Source Information, Testing/Engine/Prompt Feedback in the chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen | §10.3, Appendix A | review |\n| `exit-interview.json` beside the HTML, valid JSON, every field filled | Appendix A | a bundle-suite check parses it |\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A: About & Credits, the chat reply and `exit-interview.json`\n\nThe builders fill these at the end from their own run (write \"unknown\" for anything they can't confirm). Known at\nplanning time:\n\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 17:48:37 (TASK.md's value) · **Source:** the complete Summer and Winter Olympic Games\n  (over-the-top arcade style) · **Plan:** `PLAN.md`\n- **Genre and Perspective:** arcade multi-event sports; 2.5D side lanes, side view, pseudo-3D behind-the-athlete,\n  three-quarter and top-down per event (§1.3)\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff (full engine with the road, rhythm, physics, arcade and songs modules), modified\n  (§4.6); AI Hub session client 1.4.0; Node + Playwright 1.63.0 for tests; single self-contained HTML\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native PS1-era pixel art with HD Humanoid rigs; new flags, pictograms, venues,\n  equipment, mascot · **Animation:** the engine's procedural Humanoid rigs + the `O.Pose` layer and `E.MOVES`\n- **Audio:** the engine's chip synth: original songs, procedural anthems, synthesized sfx and crowd, gibberish voices\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode (\"Hub Heats\"); local 1–4 players\n- **Testing / Research / Environment / Model / Usage:** from the build run (TASK.md's wording for Environment)\n- **AI Hub catalogue block (suggested):** name `Olympiyikes!`, tagline `Faster. Higher. Yikes.`, description\n  \"Twelve over-the-top Summer and Winter events in one wild fortnight: sprint, swim, fly off a ski jump, sweep stones\n  and win the hockey final for your nation, alone or with up to four players.\", type `Game`, genre `Sports`, source\n  `The Olympic Games`, series `` (empty), players `1–4`, controls `Stick/WASD move · □○ or J K mash · ✕/Space act ·\n  △/Shift turbo · R2/L hold`, tags `[\"2d\", \"arcade\", \"pixel art\", \"comedy\", \"versus\", \"retro\"]`.\n- The Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback answers (TASK.md's questions, in order) go on About pages 2–4, in the chat\n  reply and in `exit-interview.json` with identical text. Check the JSON parses (`node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`).\n\n","numLines":224,"startLine":1500,"totalLines":1723}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EuwB9cc1AhrkppQMH8yHtd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
