{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HdvTGVNkVRC6FiqVP5DZ22","type":"tool_result","content":"/*!\nmy-3D2dge module ROAD v0.85.2: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nOutRun's, Pole Position's, Hang-On's and Road Rash's view: the road a run of short segments, each a band of grass, rumble\nand road drawn smaller with its distance, bending and rising, and what stands beside it scaled the same way.\n- const road = new E.Road({ segment: 200 (a segment's length, world units), width: 2000 (half the road), lanes: 3,\n  rumble: 3 (segments a stripe), draw: 240 (segments ahead), fov: 100, height: 1000 (the camera over the road), colors:\n  { road: [a, b], grass: [a, b], rumble: [a, b], lane, wall: [a, b], roof, portal }, fog: { color, density: 5 } | null, sky:\n  a Backdrop (full engine) | '#color' }).\n- Build it: road.add(n, { curve: -6..6 (+ bends right), hill: units up (- down) over the n segments, tunnel: true,\n  colors }) (curves eased in and out); road.place(z, offset, what, scale): scenery at distance z, offset across (-1\n  and 1: the road's edges; beyond: roadside); what: an E.sprite or E.anim (scale: world units a pixel, 8) or {\n  draw(g, sx, sy, scale), w: its width in units }. road.length: the lap (it loops).\n- Each frame: road.draw(r, { z (the camera's distance along), x (across, in half roads), h (its height over the road),\n  turn (the sky's offset: add curve * speed each step), cars: [{ z, x, w, draw(g, sx, sy, scale) }] }) as an overlay\n  over the frame (in a split screen, in r.viewport). A hill's crest hides what lies past it. The player's car, drawn\n  at the screen's bottom, is road.ahead(h) past z.\n- For the game: road.curveAt(z) (how hard it bends there: the push outward), road.yAt(z) (its height), road.hits(z, x,\n  w) (the scenery a body w half roads wide touches there), road.project(z, x, y) -> [sx, sy, scale] for the camera\n  last drawn (scale * a width in units = pixels).\n\n```js road\nconst E = My3D2dge, road = new E.Road({ segment: 200 });\nroad.add(50); road.add(60, { curve: 4, hill: 1200 }); road.add(40, { curve: -3, hill: -1200 }); road.place(3000, -1.4, { w: 300, draw() {} });\nif (road.length !== 150 * 200 || road.curveAt(80 * 200) <= 0 || !(road.yAt(110 * 200) > 0) || road.hits(3000, -1.3, .1).length !== 1) throw new Error('a road');\n```\nRules: z grows ahead and wraps at road.length; x is in half roads (0 the middle line); build the road before the first\ndraw; cars and scenery are drawn far to near after the road under them.\n*/\n(function (E) {\n'use strict';\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module ROAD: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * ROAD  the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, scenery, tunnels\n * ========================================================================== */\nconst { clamp } = E, easeIn = (a, b, u) => a + (b - a) * u * u, easeInOut = (a, b, u) => a + (b - a) * (-Math.cos(u * Math.PI) / 2 + .5);\nconst COLORS = { road: ['#6a6a6a', '#646464'], grass: ['#10aa10', '#009a00'], rumble: ['#e8e8e8', '#c01818'], lane: '#d8d8d8', wall: ['#5a4a3a', '#4a3a2a'], roof: '#2a2420', portal: '#6a5a48' };\nclass Road {\n  /** new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above) */\n  constructor(o = {}) {\n    /** o: its options (colors over the defaults) */\n    this.o = Object.assign({ segment: 200, width: 2000, lanes: 3, rumble: 3, draw: 240, fov: 100, height: 1000, fog: { color: '#a0c0e0', density: 5 }, sky: '#6aa8e8' }, o);\n    this.o.colors = Object.assign({}, COLORS, o.colors);\n    /** segs: its segments ({ i, z, y0, y1, curve, tunnel, colors, things }); length: the lap in world units; depth: the\n     *  camera's depth (1 / tan(fov / 2): a unit that far away fills half the screen's width) */\n    this.segs = []; this.length = 0; this.depth = 1 / Math.tan(this.o.fov / 2 * Math.PI / 180);\n    this._cam = null; this._out = null;\n  }\n  /** n segments more, bending (curve) and climbing (hill: units up, - down), eased in and out; o.tunnel, o.colors */\n  add(n, o = {}) {\n    const y0 = this.segs.length ? this.segs[this.segs.length - 1].y1 : 0, curve = o.curve || 0, hill = o.hill || 0, e = Math.max(1, Math.min(n / 3, 25)), L = this.o.segment;\n    for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) {\n      const c = k < e ? easeIn(0, curve, k / e) : k > n - e ? easeInOut(curve, 0, (k - (n - e)) / e) : curve, i = this.segs.length;\n      this.segs.push({ i, z: i * L, y0: easeInOut(y0, y0 + hill, k / n), y1: easeInOut(y0, y0 + hill, (k + 1) / n), curve: c, tunnel: !!o.tunnel, colors: o.colors || null, things: [] });\n    }\n    this.length = this.segs.length * this.o.segment; return this;\n  }","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b1b95e-beb5-4384-ba72-665ccf7128b3","uuid":"328621a7-6c8d-432c-97ee-e3fd6680fb51","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:43:12.466Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/*!\nmy-3D2dge module ROAD v0.85.2: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nOutRun's, Pole Position's, Hang-On's and Road Rash's view: the road a run of short segments, each a band of grass, rumble\nand road drawn smaller with its distance, bending and rising, and what stands beside it scaled the same way.\n- const road = new E.Road({ segment: 200 (a segment's length, world units), width: 2000 (half the road), lanes: 3,\n  rumble: 3 (segments a stripe), draw: 240 (segments ahead), fov: 100, height: 1000 (the camera over the road), colors:\n  { road: [a, b], grass: [a, b], rumble: [a, b], lane, wall: [a, b], roof, portal }, fog: { color, density: 5 } | null, sky:\n  a Backdrop (full engine) | '#color' }).\n- Build it: road.add(n, { curve: -6..6 (+ bends right), hill: units up (- down) over the n segments, tunnel: true,\n  colors }) (curves eased in and out); road.place(z, offset, what, scale): scenery at distance z, offset across (-1\n  and 1: the road's edges; beyond: roadside); what: an E.sprite or E.anim (scale: world units a pixel, 8) or {\n  draw(g, sx, sy, scale), w: its width in units }. road.length: the lap (it loops).\n- Each frame: road.draw(r, { z (the camera's distance along), x (across, in half roads), h (its height over the road),\n  turn (the sky's offset: add curve * speed each step), cars: [{ z, x, w, draw(g, sx, sy, scale) }] }) as an overlay\n  over the frame (in a split screen, in r.viewport). A hill's crest hides what lies past it. The player's car, drawn\n  at the screen's bottom, is road.ahead(h) past z.\n- For the game: road.curveAt(z) (how hard it bends there: the push outward), road.yAt(z) (its height), road.hits(z, x,\n  w) (the scenery a body w half roads wide touches there), road.project(z, x, y) -> [sx, sy, scale] for the camera\n  last drawn (scale * a width in units = pixels).\n\n```js road\nconst E = My3D2dge, road = new E.Road({ segment: 200 });\nroad.add(50); road.add(60, { curve: 4, hill: 1200 }); road.add(40, { curve: -3, hill: -1200 }); road.place(3000, -1.4, { w: 300, draw() {} });\nif (road.length !== 150 * 200 || road.curveAt(80 * 200) <= 0 || !(road.yAt(110 * 200) > 0) || road.hits(3000, -1.3, .1).length !== 1) throw new Error('a road');\n```\nRules: z grows ahead and wraps at road.length; x is in half roads (0 the middle line); build the road before the first\ndraw; cars and scenery are drawn far to near after the road under them.\n*/\n(function (E) {\n'use strict';\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module ROAD: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * ROAD  the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, scenery, tunnels\n * ========================================================================== */\nconst { clamp } = E, easeIn = (a, b, u) => a + (b - a) * u * u, easeInOut = (a, b, u) => a + (b - a) * (-Math.cos(u * Math.PI) / 2 + .5);\nconst COLORS = { road: ['#6a6a6a', '#646464'], grass: ['#10aa10', '#009a00'], rumble: ['#e8e8e8', '#c01818'], lane: '#d8d8d8', wall: ['#5a4a3a', '#4a3a2a'], roof: '#2a2420', portal: '#6a5a48' };\nclass Road {\n  /** new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above) */\n  constructor(o = {}) {\n    /** o: its options (colors over the defaults) */\n    this.o = Object.assign({ segment: 200, width: 2000, lanes: 3, rumble: 3, draw: 240, fov: 100, height: 1000, fog: { color: '#a0c0e0', density: 5 }, sky: '#6aa8e8' }, o);\n    this.o.colors = Object.assign({}, COLORS, o.colors);\n    /** segs: its segments ({ i, z, y0, y1, curve, tunnel, colors, things }); length: the lap in world units; depth: the\n     *  camera's depth (1 / tan(fov / 2): a unit that far away fills half the screen's width) */\n    this.segs = []; this.length = 0; this.depth = 1 / Math.tan(this.o.fov / 2 * Math.PI / 180);\n    this._cam = null; this._out = null;\n  }\n  /** n segments more, bending (curve) and climbing (hill: units up, - down), eased in and out; o.tunnel, o.colors */\n  add(n, o = {}) {\n    const y0 = this.segs.length ? this.segs[this.segs.length - 1].y1 : 0, curve = o.curve || 0, hill = o.hill || 0, e = Math.max(1, Math.min(n / 3, 25)), L = this.o.segment;\n    for (let k = 0; k < n; k++) {\n      const c = k < e ? easeIn(0, curve, k / e) : k > n - e ? easeInOut(curve, 0, (k - (n - e)) / e) : curve, i = this.segs.length;\n      this.segs.push({ i, z: i * L, y0: easeInOut(y0, y0 + hill, k / n), y1: easeInOut(y0, y0 + hill, (k + 1) / n), curve: c, tunnel: !!o.tunnel, colors: o.colors || null, things: [] });\n    }\n    this.length = this.segs.length * this.o.segment; return this;\n  }","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HdvTGVNkVRC6FiqVP5DZ22","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi4ja5rYfZScaEd9k9CV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0183xjME6M77edRjysga6n3S","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 1,75p modules/rhythm.js | cut -c1-500; echo ----; sed -n 1,60p modules/arcade.js | cut -c1-400","description":"Read rhythm and arcade module headers"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3433,"cache_read_input_tokens":195058,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3433},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b1b95e-beb5-4384-ba72-665ccf7128b3","uuid":"ad46d70c-2955-4cdd-a4d7-45159d83e750","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:43:16.598Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi4jZqU3fyxsETcJ2kUn","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0183xjME6M77edRjysga6n3S":{"command":"sed -n 1,75p modules/rhythm.js | cut -c1-500; echo ----; sed -n 1,60p modules/arcade.js | cut -c1-400","description":"Read rhythm and arcade module headers"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0183xjME6M77edRjysga6n3S","type":"tool_result","content":"/*!\nmy-3D2dge module RHYTHM v0.85.2: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine only. Needs: no other module.\n\nPaRappa's, Beatmania's, Dance Dance Revolution's and Space Channel 5's play: notes on a song's steps, hit in time.\n- const rh = new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes: ['left', 'down', 'up', 'right'] (the actions, one a lane),\n  windows: { perfect: 40, great: 80, good: 120 } (ms either side), life: .5, lead: 1.6 (seconds of notes shown\n  ahead), voice: { wave: 'square', vol: .2, dur: .09 } (the call notes' sound), on: { judge(j, note), fail(rh),\n  done(rh) } }).\n- chart: a string a lane, a character a step of the song: 'x' a note, 'h' a held note's head and '=' while it is\n  held, 'c' a call (PaRappa's teacher: it sounds and shows, the player answers after), '.' none; '|' and spaces are\n  ignored. Or { parts: { A: [lanes], B: [lanes] }, order: 'A A B A' } (the parts one after another), or { track: 1,\n  lanes: 4 } (that track's notes, a lane by pitch, a note held three steps or more a hold).\n- rh.start() plays the song from its start, synced (it pauses with the game); rh.update() each step after the input:\n  a lane's press is judged by its distance in ms from its nearest note's time on the music clock (game.audio.pos:\n  game time, never the sound's own), a hold let go before its end drops, a note past the good window is missed, a\n  call sounds on its step (game.audio.sfx(voice, { step })).\n- rh.hit(lane), rh.release(lane): play a lane without its action (a bot, a lane of your own on a touch screen).\n- State: score, combo, maxCombo, counts { perfect, great, good, miss }, life (0..1, at 0 failed), accuracy (0..1),\n  grade ('S' 'A' 'B' 'C' 'D'), done, failed, last ({ j, lane, ms, t }: the last judgment, for its flash), notes\n  (each { lane, step, end, call, j, ms }), total (the notes to play).\n- rh.ahead() -> the notes to show: [{ note, dt (seconds to its time, < 0 past it), dtEnd }]; rh.draw(r, { x, y (the\n  target line's middle), dir: 'down' | 'up' | 'left' | 'right' (the way notes travel), len: 150 (pixels for lead\n  seconds), gap: 24 (between lanes), size: 8, colors, arrows: false (four lanes' notes as arrows: left, down, up,\n  right), call: false (draw the call notes instead) }) draws a highway on the overlay: the lanes, their targets, notes\n  and holds, each lane's flash.\n\n```js rhythm\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true }); game.start({ update() {}, draw() {} });\nconst song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, loop: false, len: 32, tracks: [{ wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h .' }] };\nconst rh = new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart: ['x...x...', '..x.....', '......h===', '.'] });\nrh.start(); const hits = [[0, 0], [2, 1], [4, 0], [6, 2]];\nfor (let i = 0; i < 400 && !rh.done; i++) {\n  game.advance(1 / 120); const s = game.audio.pos.step;\n  for (const h of hits) if (!h.done && s >= h[0]) { rh.hit(h[1]); h.done = true; }\n  if (s >= 9) rh.release(2); rh.update();\n}\nif (rh.counts.perfect !== 4 || rh.combo !== 4 || rh.grade !== 'S') throw new Error(JSON.stringify(rh.counts));\n```\nRules: judge on the music clock (rh does), never on the sound's; give the player the audio offset (Settings, Sound:\nits calibration) and keep the windows generous on a phone; draw notes from rh.ahead() each frame.\n*/\n(function (E) {\n'use strict';\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module RHYTHM: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (the full engine) first');\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * RHYTHM  charts (lane strings, parts or a track's notes), judgments in ms of the music clock, combos, life, grades,\n * holds, calls (call and response), a note highway in any direction\n * ========================================================================== */\nconst SCORE = { perfect: 300, great: 200, good: 100 }, LIFE = { perfect: .03, great: .02, good: .005, miss: -.1 }, CALL = ['C5', 'E5', 'G5', 'C6', 'E6', 'G6'];\nconst clean = s => String(s).replace(/[|\\s]/g, '');\n// a part's lane strings laid at a step: notes { lane, step, end, call }\nfunction lanesOf(lanes, at, out) {\n  lanes.forEach((s, lane) => {\n    const c = clean(s);\n    for (let i = 0; i < c.length; i++) {\n      const ch = c[i];\n      if (ch === 'x' || ch === 'c') out.push({ lane, step: at + i, end: at + i, call: ch === 'c' });\n      else if (ch === 'h') { let j = i; while (c[j + 1] === '=') j++; out.push({ lane, step: at + i, end: at + j, call: false }); i = j; }\n    }\n  });\n  return out;\n}\n// a chart's notes: lane strings, parts in an order, or a track's notes (a lane by pitch)\nfunction notesOf(chart, song) {\n  if (Array.isArray(chart)) return lanesOf(chart, 0, []);\n  if (chart && chart.parts) {\n    const out = []; let at = 0;\n    for (const k of String(chart.order).trim().split(/\\s+/)) { const p = chart.parts[k]; if (!p) throw new Error('rhythm: the chart\\'s order names a part \"' + k + '\" it does not have'); lanesOf(p, at, out); at += Math.max(...p.map(s => clean(s).length)); }\n    return out;\n  }\n  if (chart && chart.track !== undefined) {\n    const tr = song.tracks[chart.track], toks = String(tr.notes).replace(/\\|/g, ' ').trim().split(/\\s+/), n = chart.lanes || 4, out = [];\n----\n/*!\nmy-3D2dge module ARCADE v0.85.2: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nWhat every coin-op had around its game: for arcade games, shooters, puzzles, pinball and brawlers.\n- const cab = new E.Arcade(game, { id: 'maze', lives: 3, extra: [10000] (or every: 20000), credits: null (free play;\n  a number: coins a game, cab.coin() adds one), hud: true }); cab.start(players, { demo }) begins a game (one or two\n  taking turns; false without the credits); cab.p is the player up ({ n, score, lives, save }), cab.players all.\n- cab.add(points, at): the score (at: a world point { x, y, z }: the points float up there), an extra life at each\n  threshold. cab.die() takes a life: 'again', 'next' (the other player's turn: \"PLAYER 2, READY!\"; keep each one's\n  stage in p.save) or 'over'; then cab.continue(10, done) counts down (done(true): lives back, the score kept).\n- Tables, saved per game and mode: cab.table(mode) (the top ten { name, score }), cab.qualifies(score, mode),\n  cab.enter(score, mode, done): initials on a letter wheel (up and down turn it, left and right move, confirm takes a\n  letter; taps on its arrows and OK do each); cab.entry is it while open. cab.drawTable(r, mode, y, title).\n- cab.card('STAGE 2', 2) shows a card (cab.carding while one is up), cab.say('READY!') a word under it.\n- The attract mode, on the title: cab.attract(dt) -> 'title', then 'demo' once o.idle seconds (20) pass without input\n  (play the game's own bot, start(1, { demo: true }): DEMO shows, no table), 'scores' for o.scores seconds (6) once\n  cab.endDemo() is called or o.demo seconds (30) pass, then 'title'; any input goes back to 'title'.\n- cab.update(dt) every step (cards, the entry, the continue); cab.draw(r, [x, y, w, h]) after your drawing: the HUD\n  (in the playfield's box: the screen when none), cards, DEMO, the continue and the entry.\n\n```js arcade\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true }), cab = new E.Arcade(game, { id: 'doc', lives: 2, extra: [500] });\ncab.start(1); cab.add(300); cab.add(300);\nif (cab.p.score !== 600 || cab.p.lives !== 3) throw new Error('extra life');\nif (cab.die() !== 'again' || cab.die() !== 'again' || cab.die() !== 'over') throw new Error('lives');\ncab.start(2); if (cab.die() !== 'next' || cab.p.n !== 2) throw new Error('turns');\n```\nRules: tables live in E.store ('arcade:' + id + ':' + mode; kept for the visit where storage is blocked); a demo is the game's own bot (or a recorded input log)\nplaying the real rules; the entry and the continue read the game's keys, so hold play while either is open.\n*/\n(function (E) {\n'use strict';\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module ARCADE: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * ARCADE  scores, tables, initials, lives, credits, turns, cards and the attract mode\n * ========================================================================== */\nconst LETTERS = 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789.-! ', COLS = ['#ff4a4a', '#ffffff', '#ffe070'];\nconst clicked = I => I.clicked ? I.clicked() : null;   // (a tap: the full engine's; the agent edition has none)\nconst KEPT = {};   // the tables this visit, beside E.store (they still show where storage is blocked)\nclass Arcade {\n  /** new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points),\n   *  credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds),\n   *  hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] }) */\n  constructor(game, o = {}) {\n    /** game: the game it serves; id: the game's name (its tables'); o: the options */\n    this.game = game; this.id = o.id || 'game'; this.o = Object.assign({ lives: 3, extra: [], credits: null, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6, hud: true, colors: COLS }, o);\n    /** players: [{ n, score, lives, save (the game's own: a stage kept while the other plays), next (the score of the\n     *  next extra life) }]; p: the player up; credits: coins in (null: free play); entry: the initials being entered\n     *  ({ score, mode, name, i }), or null */\n    this.players = []; this.p = null; this.credits = this.o.credits === null ? null : 0; this.entry = null;\n    /** mode: 'title' | 'play' | 'over'; demo: a demo is playing (no table); phase: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' |\n     *  'scores' */\n    this.mode = 'title'; this.demo = false; this.phase = 'title';\n    /** hi: the high score shown; wheel: where the letter wheel was last drawn (taps answer to it): { x, y, cw, up, down,\n     *  ok } in screen pixels: three columns cw wide from x, the up and down bands [y0, y1], the OK button [x, y, w, h] */\n    this._cards = []; this._idle = 0; this._t = 0; this._cont = null; this.wheel = null; this.hi = 0;\n  }","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b1b95e-beb5-4384-ba72-665ccf7128b3","uuid":"3947ac22-66c5-47ca-8122-dc87420822a6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:43:16.623Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/*!\nmy-3D2dge module RHYTHM v0.85.2: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine only. Needs: no other module.\n\nPaRappa's, Beatmania's, Dance Dance Revolution's and Space Channel 5's play: notes on a song's steps, hit in time.\n- const rh = new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes: ['left', 'down', 'up', 'right'] (the actions, one a lane),\n  windows: { perfect: 40, great: 80, good: 120 } (ms either side), life: .5, lead: 1.6 (seconds of notes shown\n  ahead), voice: { wave: 'square', vol: .2, dur: .09 } (the call notes' sound), on: { judge(j, note), fail(rh),\n  done(rh) } }).\n- chart: a string a lane, a character a step of the song: 'x' a note, 'h' a held note's head and '=' while it is\n  held, 'c' a call (PaRappa's teacher: it sounds and shows, the player answers after), '.' none; '|' and spaces are\n  ignored. Or { parts: { A: [lanes], B: [lanes] }, order: 'A A B A' } (the parts one after another), or { track: 1,\n  lanes: 4 } (that track's notes, a lane by pitch, a note held three steps or more a hold).\n- rh.start() plays the song from its start, synced (it pauses with the game); rh.update() each step after the input:\n  a lane's press is judged by its distance in ms from its nearest note's time on the music clock (game.audio.pos:\n  game time, never the sound's own), a hold let go before its end drops, a note past the good window is missed, a\n  call sounds on its step (game.audio.sfx(voice, { step })).\n- rh.hit(lane), rh.release(lane): play a lane without its action (a bot, a lane of your own on a touch screen).\n- State: score, combo, maxCombo, counts { perfect, great, good, miss }, life (0..1, at 0 failed), accuracy (0..1),\n  grade ('S' 'A' 'B' 'C' 'D'), done, failed, last ({ j, lane, ms, t }: the last judgment, for its flash), notes\n  (each { lane, step, end, call, j, ms }), total (the notes to play).\n- rh.ahead() -> the notes to show: [{ note, dt (seconds to its time, < 0 past it), dtEnd }]; rh.draw(r, { x, y (the\n  target line's middle), dir: 'down' | 'up' | 'left' | 'right' (the way notes travel), len: 150 (pixels for lead\n  seconds), gap: 24 (between lanes), size: 8, colors, arrows: false (four lanes' notes as arrows: left, down, up,\n  right), call: false (draw the call notes instead) }) draws a highway on the overlay: the lanes, their targets, notes\n  and holds, each lane's flash.\n\n```js rhythm\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true }); game.start({ update() {}, draw() {} });\nconst song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, loop: false, len: 32, tracks: [{ wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h .' }] };\nconst rh = new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart: ['x...x...', '..x.....', '......h===', '.'] });\nrh.start(); const hits = [[0, 0], [2, 1], [4, 0], [6, 2]];\nfor (let i = 0; i < 400 && !rh.done; i++) {\n  game.advance(1 / 120); const s = game.audio.pos.step;\n  for (const h of hits) if (!h.done && s >= h[0]) { rh.hit(h[1]); h.done = true; }\n  if (s >= 9) rh.release(2); rh.update();\n}\nif (rh.counts.perfect !== 4 || rh.combo !== 4 || rh.grade !== 'S') throw new Error(JSON.stringify(rh.counts));\n```\nRules: judge on the music clock (rh does), never on the sound's; give the player the audio offset (Settings, Sound:\nits calibration) and keep the windows generous on a phone; draw notes from rh.ahead() each frame.\n*/\n(function (E) {\n'use strict';\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module RHYTHM: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (the full engine) first');\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * RHYTHM  charts (lane strings, parts or a track's notes), judgments in ms of the music clock, combos, life, grades,\n * holds, calls (call and response), a note highway in any direction\n * ========================================================================== */\nconst SCORE = { perfect: 300, great: 200, good: 100 }, LIFE = { perfect: .03, great: .02, good: .005, miss: -.1 }, CALL = ['C5', 'E5', 'G5', 'C6', 'E6', 'G6'];\nconst clean = s => String(s).replace(/[|\\s]/g, '');\n// a part's lane strings laid at a step: notes { lane, step, end, call }\nfunction lanesOf(lanes, at, out) {\n  lanes.forEach((s, lane) => {\n    const c = clean(s);\n    for (let i = 0; i < c.length; i++) {\n      const ch = c[i];\n      if (ch === 'x' || ch === 'c') out.push({ lane, step: at + i, end: at + i, call: ch === 'c' });\n      else if (ch === 'h') { let j = i; while (c[j + 1] === '=') j++; out.push({ lane, step: at + i, end: at + j, call: false }); i = j; }\n    }\n  });\n  return out;\n}\n// a chart's notes: lane strings, parts in an order, or a track's notes (a lane by pitch)\nfunction notesOf(chart, song) {\n  if (Array.isArray(chart)) return lanesOf(chart, 0, []);\n  if (chart && chart.parts) {\n    const out = []; let at = 0;\n    for (const k of String(chart.order).trim().split(/\\s+/)) { const p = chart.parts[k]; if (!p) throw new Error('rhythm: the chart\\'s order names a part \"' + k + '\" it does not have'); lanesOf(p, at, out); at += Math.max(...p.map(s => clean(s).length)); }\n    return out;\n  }\n  if (chart && chart.track !== undefined) {\n    const tr = song.tracks[chart.track], toks = String(tr.notes).replace(/\\|/g, ' ').trim().split(/\\s+/), n = chart.lanes || 4, out = [];\n----\n/*!\nmy-3D2dge module ARCADE v0.85.2: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nWhat every coin-op had around its game: for arcade games, shooters, puzzles, pinball and brawlers.\n- const cab = new E.Arcade(game, { id: 'maze', lives: 3, extra: [10000] (or every: 20000), credits: null (free play;\n  a number: coins a game, cab.coin() adds one), hud: true }); cab.start(players, { demo }) begins a game (one or two\n  taking turns; false without the credits); cab.p is the player up ({ n, score, lives, save }), cab.players all.\n- cab.add(points, at): the score (at: a world point { x, y, z }: the points float up there), an extra life at each\n  threshold. cab.die() takes a life: 'again', 'next' (the other player's turn: \"PLAYER 2, READY!\"; keep each one's\n  stage in p.save) or 'over'; then cab.continue(10, done) counts down (done(true): lives back, the score kept).\n- Tables, saved per game and mode: cab.table(mode) (the top ten { name, score }), cab.qualifies(score, mode),\n  cab.enter(score, mode, done): initials on a letter wheel (up and down turn it, left and right move, confirm takes a\n  letter; taps on its arrows and OK do each); cab.entry is it while open. cab.drawTable(r, mode, y, title).\n- cab.card('STAGE 2', 2) shows a card (cab.carding while one is up), cab.say('READY!') a word under it.\n- The attract mode, on the title: cab.attract(dt) -> 'title', then 'demo' once o.idle seconds (20) pass without input\n  (play the game's own bot, start(1, { demo: true }): DEMO shows, no table), 'scores' for o.scores seconds (6) once\n  cab.endDemo() is called or o.demo seconds (30) pass, then 'title'; any input goes back to 'title'.\n- cab.update(dt) every step (cards, the entry, the continue); cab.draw(r, [x, y, w, h]) after your drawing: the HUD\n  (in the playfield's box: the screen when none), cards, DEMO, the continue and the entry.\n\n```js arcade\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true }), cab = new E.Arcade(game, { id: 'doc', lives: 2, extra: [500] });\ncab.start(1); cab.add(300); cab.add(300);\nif (cab.p.score !== 600 || cab.p.lives !== 3) throw new Error('extra life');\nif (cab.die() !== 'again' || cab.die() !== 'again' || cab.die() !== 'over') throw new Error('lives');\ncab.start(2); if (cab.die() !== 'next' || cab.p.n !== 2) throw new Error('turns');\n```\nRules: tables live in E.store ('arcade:' + id + ':' + mode; kept for the visit where storage is blocked); a demo is the game's own bot (or a recorded input log)\nplaying the real rules; the entry and the continue read the game's keys, so hold play while either is open.\n*/\n(function (E) {\n'use strict';\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module ARCADE: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * ARCADE  scores, tables, initials, lives, credits, turns, cards and the attract mode\n * ========================================================================== */\nconst LETTERS = 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789.-! ', COLS = ['#ff4a4a', '#ffffff', '#ffe070'];\nconst clicked = I => I.clicked ? I.clicked() : null;   // (a tap: the full engine's; the agent edition has none)\nconst KEPT = {};   // the tables this visit, beside E.store (they still show where storage is blocked)\nclass Arcade {\n  /** new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points),\n   *  credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds),\n   *  hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] }) */\n  constructor(game, o = {}) {\n    /** game: the game it serves; id: the game's name (its tables'); o: the options */\n    this.game = game; this.id = o.id || 'game'; this.o = Object.assign({ lives: 3, extra: [], credits: null, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6, hud: true, colors: COLS }, o);\n    /** players: [{ n, score, lives, save (the game's own: a stage kept while the other plays), next (the score of the\n     *  next extra life) }]; p: the player up; credits: coins in (null: free play); entry: the initials being entered\n     *  ({ score, mode, name, i }), or null */\n    this.players = []; this.p = null; this.credits = this.o.credits === null ? null : 0; this.entry = null;\n    /** mode: 'title' | 'play' | 'over'; demo: a demo is playing (no table); phase: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' |\n     *  'scores' */\n    this.mode = 'title'; this.demo = false; this.phase = 'title';\n    /** hi: the high score shown; wheel: where the letter wheel was last drawn (taps answer to it): { x, y, cw, up, down,\n     *  ok } in screen pixels: three columns cw wide from x, the up and down bands [y0, y1], the OK button [x, y, w, h] */\n    this._cards = []; this._idle = 0; this._t = 0; this._cont = null; this.wheel = null; this.hi = 0;\n  }","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0183xjME6M77edRjysga6n3S","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
