{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiCjeJnbVBTziAnrtuap","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019vqh5Fs8x2zRp6aEM5QqGA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -i \"s/E.rng(O.hash('stub:' + l))/E.rng(O.hash('offline:' + l))/\" src/44-hub.js && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('about.json'); j = json.loads(p.read_text())\nj['testingFeedback'] = [\n  \"About 30 game issues across the session (not counting mistakes in the tests themselves). Roughly a third were balance misses found by the bot statistics (each event's perfect bot and skill .9 / .5 / .3 bots measured against target bands: the sprint, javelin, ski jump, downhill, bobsled, curling and hockey all needed retuning, and the YIKES armstand dive was impossible to complete). The rest were bugs: a figure-skating crash (assigning to the rhythm module's read-only total), swimmers who could pass through the wall because the BONK never triggered, an idle javelin thrower and an idle curler that stalled forever, the autopilot dropping every held jump, the attract mode missing a press during a scene fade, the ` key opening and closing the dev panel in one step, no hub traffic or progress during the first five seconds (the AI Hub harness failed), deep links calling a function before it was defined, negative hash indexes giving undefined colours, overlapping HUD and menu text, and a too-small pause menu on a TV.\",\n  \"Six would have been game breaking: the figure-skating crash, the swim wall pass-through, the two idle stalls (a round that never ends), the AI Hub harness failure (the hub would keep the game out of sessions) and the autopilot hold bug (it hid that the scripted playthrough could not finish figure skating).\",\n  \"The scripted playthrough of the whole Games through the real input path (taps on every screen, the autopilot in every event, ceremonies, story beats, autosaves and credits), with the second run that fails on purpose to reach the torches, GAMES OVER and CONTINUE; and, for balance, the per-event bot statistics by skill.\",\n  \"The determinism check (the same seed twice gives the same results): it never failed, because all gameplay randomness went through labelled streams from the start.\"\n]\nj['sourceInformation']['usage'] = \"unknown cost and token count (no usage figures are visible to the model); session time about 2 hours (07:41 to about 09:45)\"\np.write_text(json.dumps(j, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + '\\n')\nprint('ok')\nEOF\nnode tools/bundle.mjs && python3 -c \"import json;d=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'));print(len(d['testingFeedback']),len(d['engineFeedback']),len(d['promptFeedback']), all(isinstance(v,str) and v for v in d['sourceInformation'].values()))\"","description":"Fill testing feedback, rebuild bundle and exit interview"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2386,"cache_read_input_tokens":878811,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2386},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e8b1b95e-beb5-4384-ba72-665ccf7128b3","uuid":"92e4d7a2-6f88-49c9-8488-aaaa1caf58da","timestamp":"2026-11-04T16:28:20.919Z","request_id":"req_011CgiCjdrW8sVGYHeGBKUbr","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019vqh5Fs8x2zRp6aEM5QqGA":{"command":"sed -i \"s/E.rng(O.hash('stub:' + l))/E.rng(O.hash('offline:' + l))/\" src/44-hub.js && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('about.json'); j = json.loads(p.read_text())\nj['testingFeedback'] = [\n  \"About 30 game issues across the session (not counting mistakes in the tests themselves). Roughly a third were balance misses found by the bot statistics (each event's perfect bot and skill .